1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,270
Gosh, I'm tired.

2
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:14,890
(Jin Ho looks through his notebook
in the morning.)

3
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:17,620
I had a lot on my mind.

4
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,760
Up until that point,
I had taken a step back.

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,260
I focused on assisting my team
while Xitsuh and Seong Beom took charge.

6
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:24,400
That was the position I had played.

7
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,500
But Xitsuh got eliminated.

8
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:30,370
Letting Seong Beom lead the team alone
might be too much for him.

9
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,640
I decided to play alongside Seong Beom...

10
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:36,440
and contribute more to lead the team.

11
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,340
I don't know.

12
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:40,910
- I'm sure it'll require us to team up.
- Right.

13
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:44,420
- There are 10 of us yet.
- Yes, there are 10 of us.

14
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,650
Excluding Beom, Seung Yong, and Ji Hoo,

15
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:50,120
there are seven of us.

16
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:53,290
Depending on whose side Sung Joo joins,
it will be either 6 to 4 or 7 to 3.

17
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,460
He'll probably team up with them.

18
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,030
So it might be 6 to 4.

19
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:58,800
For our alliance to make sense...

20
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,900
and to lead our alliance,

21
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,970
we need people.

22
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,010
We're playing individually now.

23
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:10,110
If we get a game
where teaming up makes sense,

24
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:11,440
I will...

25
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,350
try my best not to repeat...

26
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:15,880
yesterday's tragic outcome.

27
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:19,880
I want to be a reliable shield
for my teammates.

28
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:21,550
Gosh, it will be...

29
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,890
too much for me
if I end up going to the Deathmatch.

30
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,230
Let's get a clean win.

31
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:29,190
Winning the Money Challenge
looks like our best option.

32
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:32,360
You're right. Let's win, plain and simple.

33
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:37,300
I'm getting used to Bloody Game X.

34
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:39,370
When I heard the rules
in the beginning of the shoot,

35
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:42,940
I used to think, "Gosh, what kind of game
are we supposed to play?"

36
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,940
It looked like I wasn't quite fitting in.

37
00:01:45,210 --> 00:01:48,310
Now, it's different.
We get the rules from the screen.

38
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:50,380
I'm starting to see
how I'm supposed to play the games now.

39
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,880
What should we do
for the anti-jinx ritual this morning?

40
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,120
It's a thing we do every morning.

41
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,090
"All right,
I'll probably be going home today."

42
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:58,160
Then I do something.

43
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:00,530
Yesterday, I wrote down my phone number
and gave it to him.

44
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:02,630
- I see.
- With this ritual, we keep surviving.

45
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:05,100
When I told him, "We had a good run,"
we survived again.

46
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,700
When I said, "Call me when you get out,"
we survived once again.

47
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,770
So I must do something again.

48
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,370
I already packed my suitcase.

49
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:14,040
But Tae Gyun hadn't packed at all.

50
00:02:14,110 --> 00:02:16,140
I guess preparing for departure
prevents us from going home.

51
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,340
There must be energy working against it.

52
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:19,810
I should pack my suitcase too
on my way down.

53
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:22,080
I should close it up neatly too.

54
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,690
- You're already back.
- Yes.

55
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:28,690
I just ate.

56
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,820
I've been thinking in the shower.

57
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:34,190
I want to go home,

58
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,130
but it'd be a pity to go home
after I made it this far.

59
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:39,800
- I agree.
- I do want to go home,

60
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:41,900
but I'd hate to see Seung Yong advance.

61
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:42,970
Exactly.

62
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,070
I want to go home,
but I'd hate to lose to Seung Yong.

63
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,370
Part of me also thought it wasn't fair...

64
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:51,610
how Xitsuh got eliminated so early
in the competition.

65
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:54,150
As his former teammate,

66
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:57,750
I felt it wasn't fair
that I couldn't protect him in any way.

67
00:02:58,450 --> 00:03:00,290
Please gather in the main hall.

68
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:03,020
Good morning.

69
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,130
- Morning.
- Good morning.

70
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:16,800
You're wearing a short-sleeve shirt,
not a tank top.

71
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,000
- I'm wearing my regular clothes.
- Hey.

72
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,040
He should've gone to the outdoor
survival grounds in that outfit.

73
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:24,910
- Me too. Thank you.
- Well, we haven't...

74
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,050
- Did you get some sleep?
- Pardon?

75
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,680
Did you get some sleep after betraying us?

76
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:34,350
I drank so much.

77
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,090
He betrayed you?

78
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:38,890
No. I moved to a bigger room.
Back to Team P2's room.

79
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,390
It must be nice
having the room all to yourself.

80
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:41,890
- It's nice.
- Right.

81
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,230
What am I still doing here?

82
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,740
I've been placing last since Day One.

83
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,240
I got eliminated once.
I was sent to the basement.

84
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,340
- My gosh.
- Exactly.

85
00:03:57,340 --> 00:04:00,610
Every time I wake up and come down
to play, I keep finding you sitting here.

86
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:03,580
Right. I just sit here. That's all.

87
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:06,950
This guy doesn't seem to go away
how hard we try to get rid of him.

88
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,720
Somehow, I'm still here.

89
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,630
I guess I have a lot of good luck
this year.

90
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:17,000
I kicked him out,
but he found his way back.

91
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,460
- He keeps coming back.
- Right.

92
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,630
I can't even count
how many times you came back.

93
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:21,700
Exactly.

94
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,440
Before explaining the rules,

95
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:29,270
the winning benefits
of the Money Challenge will be announced.

96
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:33,110
The winner will receive 20,000 dollars...

97
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,610
and two elimination immunity passes.

98
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:39,780
One of the elimination immunity passes
can be transferred to another player.

99
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,860
Today's Deathmatch
will require three players.

100
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,590
The bottom two players will be up...

101
00:04:49,730 --> 00:04:51,360
for elimination by default.

102
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:53,670
The two bottom players will single out...

103
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:56,870
a player each,

104
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,740
and a vote will be held
for the chosen players.

105
00:04:58,740 --> 00:04:59,900
(They will pick a player each.
There will be a vote for the 2 players.)

106
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:04,710
The player with the most votes
and the two bottom players...

107
00:05:05,210 --> 00:05:08,010
In other words, a total of three players
will participate in...

108
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:10,010
a three-way Deathmatch.

109
00:05:10,550 --> 00:05:13,620
Excluding the winner of the Deathmatch,
the other two players will be eliminated.

110
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,420
They will have to leave Bloody Game X.

111
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:18,420
- There's only one survivor.
- Today's Money Challenge...

112
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,730
will be revealed now.

113
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:23,430
- Please.
- Today's Money Challenge is...

114
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:26,260
(Project Galaxy)

115
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:29,070
Project Galaxy.

116
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,900
Do you know this game?

117
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:33,640
Not at all.

118
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:37,440
Project Galaxy is an individual match,

119
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,840
featuring ten players.

120
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:40,910
Players must guess the location...

121
00:05:40,910 --> 00:05:43,210
of the hidden celestial objects
through observations.

122
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:45,080
Their goal is
to score the highest points...

123
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,450
while utilizing the variable,
the black hole.

124
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,890
The game board consists
of 16 circular sectors,

125
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:54,230
numbered 1 through 16.

126
00:05:54,930 --> 00:05:58,730
A comet, a planet, a satellite,

127
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:02,170
twin clouds, a dwarf planet, a star,

128
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,970
and cosmic dust.

129
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:05,900
A total of seven celestial objects
are hidden...

130
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:08,070
across the sectors,
each governed by its own rules.

131
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:11,480
The locations of the celestial objects
will be confidential.

132
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,480
The game consists of ten rounds.

133
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:17,420
Each round will last 30 minutes.

134
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:21,090
Players must guess the locations
of the celestial objects.

135
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:24,220
To find celestial objects
that yield higher points,

136
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,430
they must choose a sector
to stay in for the round.

137
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:29,390
Before Round One begins,

138
00:06:29,530 --> 00:06:32,630
a basic hint will be revealed
to help the players guess the locations.

139
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:34,970
Before each odd-numbered round begins,

140
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:38,100
an additional hint will be revealed
for one minute.

141
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,370
All players will receive 30 coins...

142
00:06:41,370 --> 00:06:43,140
as starting capital.

143
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,780
Players will enter the Voting Room
every round...

144
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:50,010
and can choose
to do 1 of the 4 following actions.

145
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:52,980
The first action is observing.

146
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:54,820
Players can designate...

147
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:57,560
up to eight consecutive sectors
once per round...

148
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:01,630
and ask how many celestial objects
are located within the selected range.

149
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,900
When doing so, players are allowed...

150
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,160
to narrow down the search range
by spending coins.

151
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:09,270
One coin is required for each sector
narrowed down.

152
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:11,970
From Rounds 1 through 8,

153
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,270
the observation ranges
are already specified.

154
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:16,810
Starting from Round Nine,
players can freely choose...

155
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:20,550
any eight consecutive sectors
without being restricted to any set range.

156
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:24,250
However, stars will be excluded
from the observation targets.

157
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:27,020
When observed,
they will be seen as cosmic dust.

158
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:30,020
The second action is moving a sector.

159
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:33,560
Players are required
to pick a sector to stay in...

160
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,160
each round.

161
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:39,130
In Round One,
they can freely pick any sector they want.

162
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:42,570
But starting from Round Two,
they can only move their sector,

163
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:44,970
adjacent to the one
they occupied in the previous round.

164
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:47,670
To move beyond adjacent sectors,

165
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:50,740
players must pay one coin
per sector skipped.

166
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:54,610
If a player fails to pick a sector
within the time limit,

167
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,480
the player will lose five points
for the round.

168
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:00,120
By the end of the round,

169
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,750
only players who are lined up...

170
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:03,390
in front of the Voting Room
will be allowed.

171
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,260
The third action is
betting on a black hole.

172
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:10,390
A black hole exists in a sector
every round.

173
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:14,930
A black hole reverses the point values...

174
00:08:15,230 --> 00:08:18,240
of the current sector
and the two adjacent ones.

175
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,440
A black hole will start off
in the first sector.

176
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:24,140
The black hole advances one sector
clockwise every round.

177
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:28,380
Players can shift the black hole
additional sectors by betting their coins.

178
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:32,180
At the end of the round, the black hole...

179
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:35,750
moves additional sectors,
selected by the player...

180
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:37,320
with the highest bet.

181
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:41,530
If two or more players tie
for the highest bet,

182
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:43,460
the choice...

183
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:45,630
of the next highest bidder will apply.

184
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:49,200
The fourth action is checking the score.

185
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,370
Players can check...

186
00:08:51,370 --> 00:08:53,940
their cumulative score by spending coins.

187
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:57,640
In Round 1, players must spend 10 coins.

188
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,910
With each passing round,
the cost decreases by one coin.

189
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:04,150
At the end of the round,
points earned in the round...

190
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,720
will be revealed, which will also
reflect the effect of the black hole.

191
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:09,450
The earned points will be revealed...

192
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:13,220
anonymously under designated letters
from A to J.

193
00:09:13,790 --> 00:09:17,900
The assigned letters will remain unchanged
until the game ends.

194
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:22,530
At the end of 10 rounds,
the 2 players with the lowest scores...

195
00:09:22,730 --> 00:09:24,340
will participate in the Deathmatch.

196
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,800
(They will participate in the Deathmatch.)

197
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,770
The player with the highest score...

198
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:30,040
will receive
two elimination immunity passes.

199
00:09:30,470 --> 00:09:34,050
One of the passes can be transferred
to another player.

200
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:36,750
Two players heading to the Deathmatch...

201
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:39,080
will choose one player each...

202
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:41,690
from those
without an elimination immunity pass.

203
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:46,190
Then they'll vote to pick the last player
for the Deathmatch.

204
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:50,460
If players tie,
the player with more coins...

205
00:09:50,730 --> 00:09:53,700
or the player with more personal funds
will win.

206
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:58,040
Three items are available
in Project Galaxy.

207
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:01,770
The first item is
the Player Location Check Card.

208
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:04,410
Players can pick one player...

209
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:07,040
and find out the sector
the player stayed in the previous round.

210
00:10:08,010 --> 00:10:10,110
The second item is extra coins.

211
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:13,220
Players can buy five extra coins.

212
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,820
The third item is a hidden item.

213
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:19,420
It will be revealed
before the start of Round Six.

214
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,800
In the second season, I cursed Pi out...

215
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,270
while playing the Money Challenge.

216
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,630
This is a similar Money Challenge.

217
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:33,800
I need to be in the sector
with the highest points...

218
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:36,070
and earn as many points as possible
in that round.

219
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:38,340
The key point is widening...

220
00:10:38,510 --> 00:10:40,750
the point difference every round.

221
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:43,010
Forming an alliance is
the ultimate winning strategy.

222
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:45,480
I thought that forming a solid alliance...

223
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:47,890
would give me an upper hand.

224
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:49,950
If I were to win, I could use
one immunity pass for myself...

225
00:10:49,950 --> 00:10:51,690
- and transfer one to someone else.
- You could transfer the other one.

226
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,760
My gosh. In the end,
playing as an alliance will be tricky.

227
00:10:56,230 --> 00:10:57,960
Let's say we form a three-player alliance.

228
00:10:58,330 --> 00:10:59,830
There are only
two elimination immunity passes.

229
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:02,300
- One of them won't be protected. Right?
- Yes.

230
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,270
We can save the third player
through the vote.

231
00:11:05,570 --> 00:11:07,300
The benefit for the winning player...

232
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,710
was two elimination immunity passes.

233
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:13,040
I thought that one of the passes
could be transferred.

234
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:16,910
During this season, we rarely got
these elimination immunity passes.

235
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:18,280
I was surprised to hear this benefit.

236
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:21,590
This is the perfect card
to drive people to betray one another.

237
00:11:22,190 --> 00:11:23,820
In the end,
this game requires an alliance.

238
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:24,860
- Yes.
- Right.

239
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:27,860
- It's a game of information.
- It's all about information.

240
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,400
We can ask one question each.

241
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,030
With 4 people, that's 4 questions.

242
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:36,600
With 6 people, that's 6 questions.

243
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:40,370
There are so many things
you can figure out with just one question.

244
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,270
An extra player could make
two differences.

245
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:45,810
Go and get YunB.

246
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:48,710
We spread out to earn points.
We picked a specific sector...

247
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:50,650
to earn 2 or 4 points.
Do you remember that?

248
00:11:51,950 --> 00:11:55,550
Ji Hoo, Seung Yong, Sung Joo, and me.
It was the four of us.

249
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:57,920
We just needed to recruit one more player.

250
00:11:57,920 --> 00:12:00,690
We had Sung Joo on our side.
YunB came back.

251
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,090
I thought we could form a team with YunB.

252
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,560
It could be a 5-on-5 match.

253
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:11,670
(Beom is on the move to recruit YunB.)

254
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,200
(Securing a spot next to him)

255
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,270
- Oh, that?
- Yes, the legend.

256
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,640
My goodness. Hold on.

257
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:21,780
Will they bring in the board?

258
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,920
No. You have to get on a spaceship
and leave Earth.

259
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,380
- For real?
- There's a telescope.

260
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:29,850
My gosh.
I have to visualize this in my head.

261
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,790
Can I rely on you, Ji Min?

262
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,630
You weren't there for this game
in the second season.

263
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,890
It's easier than you think.

264
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:37,930
- Wait, I'll play with you then.
- Okay.

265
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:39,000
You know,

266
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:41,800
- we need to team up with the majority.
- Seriously.

267
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:43,600
You know that, right?

268
00:12:44,070 --> 00:12:47,440
Once we pool our information,
we know everyone's locations and bets.

269
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,540
We just have to avoid the worst.

270
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,640
You've got to be James Bond.

271
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,980
- Me?
- What's your name?

272
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:56,210
James Bond.

273
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:00,750
- We have to team up for this, right?
- Definitely.

274
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:01,950
- The more people, the better?
- Yes.

275
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:03,420
That's because...

276
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,490
You...

277
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,890
need to pretend
that you're teaming up with us.

278
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:10,090
As for what you're asking,

279
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,530
I can do it. But I don't have the talent
to pull it off.

280
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:16,430
There are aspects of a card game too.
This is crazy.

281
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:25,440
I thought, "What's going on?"

282
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,150
"What's Sung Joo doing there?"

283
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:29,650
"Wait."

284
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,790
If we play with Seung Yong today,
we'll be doomed.

285
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:36,520
Why?

286
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,690
Destroying him is their plan.

287
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:43,060
You should run.

288
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:50,370
The overall consensus was that
they wanted to eliminate Seung Yong.

289
00:13:50,470 --> 00:13:52,300
So many people mentioned that to me.

290
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,510
Actually, I wasn't the only one.

291
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:58,280
Everyone showed strong hostility
toward them.

292
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:02,050
As it so happened,
many of us were in the same boat.

293
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:03,550
Seong Beom and Hye Seon...

294
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:06,680
had to say goodbye to Xitsuh
who was like a mom to them.

295
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:11,060
For someone who had to watch
Xitsuh and Tae Gyun leave the show,

296
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:15,460
there was a clear target to blame.

297
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,600
So I tried to drive the narrative
against them.

298
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:21,300
I said, "Having more people
on our team would be better."

299
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:22,830
"We should play together."

300
00:14:22,970 --> 00:14:25,170
I was determined to recruit Sung Joo.

301
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:27,610
I think YunB might be good at this.

302
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:29,970
I think he played a similar game
in the second season.

303
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:32,040
He did. And he played well.

304
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:33,810
He won first place.

305
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:36,410
(Clueless of the current situation,
they're hoping to play a 5-on-5 match.)

306
00:14:38,850 --> 00:14:39,950
- Seung Yong.
- Yes?

307
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:41,220
Are you busy with the rules?

308
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:43,320
- What is it?
- Are you busy now?

309
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,690
I think you're their target.

310
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:47,490
Okay.

311
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,960
Let's think about that
while going over the rules.

312
00:14:56,570 --> 00:14:58,170
They discussed it.

313
00:14:58,800 --> 00:14:59,900
- Targeting me?
- Yes.

314
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:01,810
There's nothing I can do.

315
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:05,440
If we recruit YunB,
a 5-on-5 match won't be a bad deal for us.

316
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,940
If it's a 5-on-5 match...

317
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,080
As long as we're not outnumbered,

318
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,780
- It's good.
- we won't lose.

319
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:11,020
- It will be tough...
- But a 6-on-4 match...

320
00:15:11,020 --> 00:15:12,080
if it becomes a 6-on-4 match.

321
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:15,550
- Do you have a lighter?
- It's so uncomfortable.

322
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:17,520
- I have a lighter.
- Are you anxious?

323
00:15:17,690 --> 00:15:20,220
I'm stuck in the middle.
I don't know which side to join.

324
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,490
You have to join my side.

325
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:24,190
- Your side? As in Ji Min's side?
- There's a reason for it.

326
00:15:24,330 --> 00:15:26,100
Yes. Ji Min and Jin Ho.

327
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:27,800
The perfect place to become wallpaper.

328
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,100
- But it's nice.
- I think we'd win, though.

329
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,540
But the other team is pretty good too.

330
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:35,540
One of them is like a supercomputer.

331
00:15:35,970 --> 00:15:37,040
What will you do?

332
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,140
- I'm doomed.
- What?

333
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:40,780
- I need to give up on our alliance.
- Why?

334
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,050
I need to join the other team.

335
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,520
So you want to join them too?

336
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,520
I'm in a position
where I have that option.

337
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:48,250
I have that option.

338
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:49,290
But...

339
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,120
we can have a 5-on-5 match
if you join us, YunB.

340
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,390
- That's true.
- Yes.

341
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:56,090
Isn't it better to even the playing field
by making it a 5-on-5 match?

342
00:15:56,730 --> 00:15:58,630
But from what I heard...

343
00:15:58,630 --> 00:15:59,860
after coming back to the show,

344
00:16:00,430 --> 00:16:02,800
things got out of hand on the Heist Day.

345
00:16:03,370 --> 00:16:06,170
Seung Yong now has a giant target
on his back.

346
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:07,840
There's nothing we can do about it.

347
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:10,070
- It's pretty bad.
- After the Heist Day?

348
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:11,940
It's that bad?

349
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,480
- We didn't know. But we found out later.
- Yes.

350
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,050
And yesterday's game didn't help either.

351
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,610
They're pretty upset...

352
00:16:17,150 --> 00:16:20,050
because they tried
to send Jin Ho and Xitsuh home.

353
00:16:20,050 --> 00:16:22,120
That only added fuel to the fire.

354
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,350
Right. I can see that.

355
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,520
- Yes. But...
- But as for me,

356
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,320
- You'll play with him?
- I'll play with him.

357
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,030
If I switch teams too,

358
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,130
it will crush Seung Yong.

359
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,500
- Right. I understand your position.
- So... Yes.

360
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:35,630
- Switching teams now...
- Okay.

361
00:16:36,730 --> 00:16:37,970
just to save my own neck...

362
00:16:37,970 --> 00:16:39,700
- isn't right.
- Okay.

363
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,810
You also think it's important
to have more people on your team, right?

364
00:16:41,810 --> 00:16:42,840
- Of course.
- Of course.

365
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:44,910
- This game is about information.
- It's all about information.

366
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:46,240
But...

367
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,880
now that I talked to you guys,

368
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:53,920
- You should join us.
- it looks like it will be 7 against 3.

369
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,790
I'll still play with the minority.

370
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:58,660
Tell them I tried to recruit YunB,
but I failed,

371
00:16:58,660 --> 00:16:59,660
so I'm joining them instead.

372
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:02,130
- What?
- Tell them I failed to recruit YunB,

373
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:03,960
- so I'm joining them instead.
- You don't want a target on your back?

374
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:08,330
For me to ditch Teams R and C
and join the other team,

375
00:17:08,630 --> 00:17:10,430
I need some kind of insurance...

376
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:12,400
because of the elimination system.

377
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,700
- You'll play with us?
- Yes.

378
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,210
I still have a problem if I join you.

379
00:17:15,210 --> 00:17:16,240
They can pick two players.

380
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,310
- They'll pick me for sure.
- What?

381
00:17:17,310 --> 00:17:19,380
They'll see me as a traitor.
I did betray them.

382
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:21,410
Our team only gets two immunity passes.

383
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:23,850
- Right. We'll give you the pass.
- Can I get the pass?

384
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:26,450
In return, I won't play a double agent.

385
00:17:26,450 --> 00:17:28,550
- Right. I know that you're not that type.
- Then...

386
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:30,250
- those two have to agree too.
- Okay.

387
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,890
- Yes. Or I...
- Yes.

388
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:34,860
He's saying that...

389
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,830
if he betrays them and joins us,
they will pick him for sure.

390
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:40,500
I hate to say this,
but those three are cowards.

391
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,000
So they'll pick the weakest players.

392
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:44,230
You have a point,
but Sung Joo feels nervous about it.

393
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,400
So he said if he gets the immunity pass,

394
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,970
he'll do his best to win the game.

395
00:17:49,010 --> 00:17:50,910
If you promise me the pass,

396
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:52,910
I won't sabotage the team.

397
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:56,010
Were you coming to join us to sabotage us?

398
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:57,920
- Of course, not.
- If you didn't get the pass?

399
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,820
It's obvious what's going to happen to me.

400
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:01,520
I have a 50 percent chance
of getting chosen if we win.

401
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,250
I have a 50 percent chance
of getting chosen if I join them and lose.

402
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:06,690
I don't think they would pick you...

403
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:09,560
even if you were to join us
and we were to win.

404
00:18:09,730 --> 00:18:10,930
I do agree with them.

405
00:18:10,930 --> 00:18:12,330
It's iffy.

406
00:18:12,330 --> 00:18:14,430
If we were to decide that now,

407
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:16,500
it would distract me
from focusing on the game.

408
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,940
- There are other variables.
- We should talk when everyone's here.

409
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:22,440
Here's what's most important.
One of us will be the winner.

410
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:25,080
When I asked them
to give me the immunity pass,

411
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:28,050
it seemed like too big of a benefit
although I was joining them...

412
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:30,150
to help them.

413
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,950
So we had to meet in the middle
to make a deal.

414
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,650
That's why I came up with this deal.

415
00:18:34,850 --> 00:18:36,890
All right.
So when it comes to making the decision...

416
00:18:36,890 --> 00:18:39,420
I know that I'm switching teams now.

417
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:42,060
I hope you'd treat me the same way...

418
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:43,830
as the rest of them.

419
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:44,900
- Absolutely.
- Of course.

420
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:47,430
- Don't try to get me eliminated.
- You don't have to worry about that.

421
00:18:47,730 --> 00:18:49,800
We're not like that. I don't know
what kind of team you've been playing...

422
00:18:49,930 --> 00:18:51,470
We had a level-headed discussion.

423
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:53,570
I made a compromise and wasn't so greedy.

424
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,140
That's how it started.

425
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:57,770
I also think the immunity pass is
a bit too much for me.

426
00:18:57,770 --> 00:19:00,640
- So I want to be treated equally.
- Of course.

427
00:19:00,810 --> 00:19:03,710
First of all, we're outnumbered.

428
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,020
- You must know that.
- It's 6 against 4?

429
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:07,350
It's not even 6 against 4.

430
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:09,020
- Then?
- It will be 7 against 3.

431
00:19:09,150 --> 00:19:10,320
- Because of Sung Joo?
- Yes.

432
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,290
- Really?
- Why?

433
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,390
If you think about it,
Sung Joo is a member of Team P2.

434
00:19:15,630 --> 00:19:16,960
- Okay.
- He did join our team...

435
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,300
later in the competition.

436
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:21,700
It's iffy to leave YunB
all alone with them.

437
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:22,930
We can't recruit YunB?

438
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:24,070
I don't think so. Their alliance...

439
00:19:24,070 --> 00:19:25,570
- is too solid.
- What did you hear?

440
00:19:25,570 --> 00:19:28,370
- Let me be completely honest.
- Okay.

441
00:19:28,810 --> 00:19:30,070
Seung Yong is their target.

442
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:33,040
Their discussion dates back
to the Heist Day.

443
00:19:34,650 --> 00:19:38,020
- Come on.
- You're everyone's target now.

444
00:19:38,150 --> 00:19:41,290
- Really?
- This whole game is built on that.

445
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:43,020
- Darn.
- This is their quest.

446
00:19:43,190 --> 00:19:45,390
Their quest is...

447
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:48,890
to destroy Shin Seung Yong,
the Public Enemy.

448
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:52,560
Sung Joo was trying to recruit...

449
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,360
- even me, but I said it wasn't right.
- Okay.

450
00:19:54,970 --> 00:19:57,870
I told them I would play with you
even if I ended up going home for it.

451
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,540
On the Heist Day,

452
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:02,610
I got carried away during the game.

453
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:04,240
My behavior that night...

454
00:20:04,610 --> 00:20:06,780
gave them a reason to come after me.

455
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:10,650
So they talked about targeting me
and that's how it happened.

456
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,750
- So that's how it happened.
- Yes. They...

457
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,220
- Okay.
- already...

458
00:20:16,950 --> 00:20:19,060
finished forming an alliance.

459
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:20,890
- I see. It's already done.
- Yes.

460
00:20:22,530 --> 00:20:25,060
Sung Joo, so you've switched sides?

461
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:28,400
I told Beom everything.

462
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,130
My gosh, this one is going to be hard.

463
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,310
Let's think about that together.

464
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:39,840
I thought you were going to join us.

465
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:44,410
- I wanted to join you.
- Okay.

466
00:20:44,510 --> 00:20:46,320
- I do want to play with you.
- Okay.

467
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:49,250
I want to play with Beom too.

468
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,950
To be honest with you,

469
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,290
I still have to consider justification.

470
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,690
So it's a bit iffy.

471
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,500
Do you have an issue
with Seung Yong as well?

472
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:01,900
No. Not at all.

473
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:05,400
If it's a 5-on-5 match,
it will be a lot more fun.

474
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,600
But...

475
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:09,410
I have to consider my position too.

476
00:21:09,910 --> 00:21:11,740
I just made it back into the mansion.

477
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,280
I'm neutral.

478
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:17,050
They came to me first
and tried to win me over to their side.

479
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,080
I tried my best to change their mind.

480
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:22,620
With Sung Joo and YunB on our side,

481
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:24,820
it would be a 5-on-5 match
and we'd have a shot.

482
00:21:24,990 --> 00:21:27,790
We'd be able to win no matter what
if I did the math right.

483
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:30,430
But...

484
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,060
- the thing is,
- Yes.

485
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:35,130
- they fooled me.
- What do you mean?

486
00:21:35,270 --> 00:21:36,330
"Fool" isn't the right word.

487
00:21:36,330 --> 00:21:37,830
I ended up joining their alliance.

488
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:39,540
(Inhaling sharply)

489
00:21:39,570 --> 00:21:42,040
- Why, though?
- Well, you know...

490
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:43,870
Why don't you hear Seung Yong out?

491
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:45,910
We even pleaded to them.

492
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,110
We pleaded to them.

493
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:50,610
I also talked to Keun Woo.

494
00:21:50,610 --> 00:21:52,150
But he wouldn't even budge.

495
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:53,180
Keun Woo.

496
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,890
So you're joining them, right?

497
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:56,590
- I'm with Ji Min.
- Right.

498
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:59,120
- How about playing separately for once?
- No way.

499
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:00,860
- I never switch sides.
- Are you sure?

500
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:02,830
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

501
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:06,430
Gosh, it was crazy.
I had never talked to Hye Seon before.

502
00:22:06,530 --> 00:22:08,300
We barely talked during games.

503
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,530
I begged Hye Seon to join us.

504
00:22:10,630 --> 00:22:13,070
They can just admit that they want
to destroy us by outnumbering us.

505
00:22:13,070 --> 00:22:14,940
But they keep coming up
with a weird excuse.

506
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:18,440
I don't think it will be a fair fight.

507
00:22:18,710 --> 00:22:20,840
Honestly, I don't get it. Yesterday,

508
00:22:21,010 --> 00:22:23,480
everyone said it was just a game
and tomorrow was a different day.

509
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,980
They told us to do our best
although it got tough yesterday.

510
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,550
But all of a sudden today,

511
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,720
they got so petty
and changed their stance.

512
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,420
This doesn't look right.

513
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,220
If we're talking
about people's past mistakes,

514
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:35,260
should I mention their mistakes
outside the show too?

515
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:36,560
They're basically saying,
"We don't like him."

516
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:38,300
"So we want to eliminate him."

517
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:40,200
- That's how I see it.
- Okay.

518
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:43,800
I want to have a fair fight.

519
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:45,500
Would you?

520
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,770
Give me some time.

521
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:55,510
- I'll think about it.
- Yes, think about it.

522
00:22:55,510 --> 00:22:57,080
They do have a reason to do this.

523
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,980
But this is a cowardly move.

524
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:00,380
- I know what you mean.
- Yes.

525
00:23:00,450 --> 00:23:01,690
So...

526
00:23:01,690 --> 00:23:03,950
So we might be able to turn it
into a fair game of 5 against 5.

527
00:23:03,950 --> 00:23:06,520
- You should go and...
- We have a lot of time left.

528
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,630
They were talking a lot
with the other team.

529
00:23:08,730 --> 00:23:11,530
I don't know what there could possibly be
to talk about.

530
00:23:11,630 --> 00:23:13,360
I tried to focus on the game instead.

531
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:16,730
Taking the reasons into account,
I'm completely neutral.

532
00:23:16,830 --> 00:23:18,540
Excluding the backstory
and everything else,

533
00:23:18,570 --> 00:23:22,640
probability-wise, I think
the other team has a better chance...

534
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,970
at winning the game.

535
00:23:23,970 --> 00:23:25,710
But if I were to fluff up...

536
00:23:25,710 --> 00:23:27,680
and rationalize
what's happening right now,

537
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:30,010
they're forcing this whole justification.

538
00:23:30,150 --> 00:23:33,280
Who do you think will get chosen
by the bottom two players?

539
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:35,820
I'm pretty sure it'd be me
even if I were to join your team.

540
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:38,120
No. If my team ends up losing,

541
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:39,320
I'll have the lowest score.

542
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:40,820
Come on.

543
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,390
No. I...

544
00:23:42,890 --> 00:23:43,990
That's my point.

545
00:23:43,990 --> 00:23:45,630
- I need a bargaining chip too.
- I see.

546
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,400
(Hesitant)

547
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:48,900
- I'm offering you a deal.
- Right.

548
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:50,870
- But...
- As for my reason behind joining them,

549
00:23:50,870 --> 00:23:54,040
there's only one.
It has to do with Sung Joo.

550
00:23:54,070 --> 00:23:56,770
If I were to explain my decision
in terms of backstories and history,

551
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:58,980
both of us came back from elimination.

552
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:01,750
So it only makes sense
that I join the team he joins.

553
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:03,210
That's why.

554
00:24:03,210 --> 00:24:04,920
Parting ways with Sung Joo...

555
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:06,520
doesn't feel right to me.

556
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:09,590
When I talked to YunB,
he told me it was Sung Joo's decision.

557
00:24:09,590 --> 00:24:11,720
When I talked to Sung Joo,
he said it was YunB's decision.

558
00:24:11,990 --> 00:24:13,890
I started to get angry at that point.

559
00:24:13,890 --> 00:24:15,990
So what do you want to do?
Do you want to play with them?

560
00:24:16,190 --> 00:24:18,930
I can't switch sides again
like a turncoat.

561
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:20,800
- I should join them.
- No, you can join us.

562
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:23,370
- Well...
- We have a lot of time. Don't back down.

563
00:24:24,070 --> 00:24:25,970
- It's uncomfortable.
- Come here, Sung Joo.

564
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:27,240
So you'll stick with them no matter what?

565
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,540
I can't switch sides again.

566
00:24:29,170 --> 00:24:30,240
It was a tough decision.

567
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:34,540
Having more people would allow us to ask
more questions, and that'd be nice.

568
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:35,980
Darn it. We can only ask three questions.

569
00:24:43,490 --> 00:24:46,190
Well, Beom is coming down.

570
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,930
(I see.)

571
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:52,260
- It's okay. Don't worry about that.
- Okay.

572
00:24:52,730 --> 00:24:54,730
My gosh, it's uncomfortable.

573
00:24:56,030 --> 00:24:58,340
What if I were to persuade Hye Seon
by telling her you'd join us?

574
00:24:58,440 --> 00:24:59,640
It would be 5 against 5 then.

575
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:02,210
That might change things...

576
00:25:02,210 --> 00:25:03,610
if you could persuade Hye Seon.

577
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:05,640
Beom. But here's your chance
of persuading her.

578
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:07,880
It's 0.01 percent.

579
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:08,880
I'll make...

580
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,280
- that 0.01 percent chance happen.
- Okay.

581
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:12,020
You should keep an open mind then, YunB.

582
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,680
- Okay.
- You said you were neutral.

583
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:14,920
- Leave a 50 percent chance open for us.
- I...

584
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,420
I'll keep an open mind.

585
00:25:17,490 --> 00:25:18,590
Let me keep trying.

586
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:20,960
There was nothing I could do.

587
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,090
If I were to recruit you,

588
00:25:23,690 --> 00:25:25,360
YunB might join us too.

589
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:26,500
(Beom tries to persuade Hye Seon.)

590
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,470
We can make it into a 5-on-5 match.

591
00:25:28,700 --> 00:25:30,170
- Mr. YunB.
- Yes?

592
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:34,940
I'll go to the Deathmatch.

593
00:25:35,310 --> 00:25:37,110
That has to be our strategy.
There's no other way.

594
00:25:37,370 --> 00:25:39,280
They're going out to talk now.
I'm trying to recruit them.

595
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:41,480
I made a deal with them...

596
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:43,910
telling them that I'd go to the
Deathmatch. That's what I offered them.

597
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,750
To win, we should use my coins
in the beginning.

598
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:49,720
The best strategy is
making one of us win the whole thing.

599
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,390
That's the best strategy.

600
00:25:52,190 --> 00:25:53,960
- Here's what crossed my mind.
- Yes.

601
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,890
I don't feel good about this either.

602
00:25:55,890 --> 00:25:57,790
- We're ganging up on them?
- Yes. So...

603
00:25:58,060 --> 00:25:59,400
It is what it is.

604
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:03,330
Think about the probability.
Survival is important to you too.

605
00:26:03,930 --> 00:26:05,000
- It is what it is.
- This is annoying.

606
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,670
You have the biggest reason...

607
00:26:07,070 --> 00:26:09,940
to stay with them.

608
00:26:10,540 --> 00:26:12,310
- You do have a point.
- Yes.

609
00:26:12,410 --> 00:26:14,740
- I was so sad to see Xitsuh go.
- Right.

610
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:16,180
And I'll be honest.

611
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:19,480
I didn't have to think about this
even for 0.0001 percent.

612
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:22,650
Telling him I'd think about his offer...

613
00:26:22,650 --> 00:26:23,820
was also my strategy.

614
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,390
I didn't want any bad blood between us.

615
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:27,990
There's even one percent chance that
they might pick me for the Deathmatch.

616
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:30,990
So I kept turning him down politely...

617
00:26:30,990 --> 00:26:32,030
not to get on his bad side.

618
00:26:32,030 --> 00:26:34,500
- Twenty percent from the Heist Day.
- Yes.

619
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:37,230
Another 20 percent
because you were on Team P3...

620
00:26:37,230 --> 00:26:39,800
and played
with Seong Beom and Jin Ho before.

621
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,170
- Yes, you're right.
- Right.

622
00:26:42,340 --> 00:26:43,810
Considering everything,

623
00:26:44,810 --> 00:26:45,880
I don't see any point to switch.

624
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:47,910
Don't you agree?

625
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:51,650
I'm looking for the lowest chance
of getting eliminated.

626
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:53,550
My goal is to survive.

627
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:55,890
Of course, I'd join the majority.

628
00:26:56,420 --> 00:26:57,420
It's a no brainer.

629
00:26:57,420 --> 00:26:58,490
I see. You're right.

630
00:26:58,490 --> 00:27:00,060
So that's why I decided like this.

631
00:27:00,060 --> 00:27:02,360
I see. Great. Thank you.

632
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:04,260
- You helped me clear things up.
- Okay.

633
00:27:05,130 --> 00:27:07,060
It's important to justify our decisions.

634
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:08,930
What should we do?

635
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:15,740
Well, we've made our decision.

636
00:27:15,740 --> 00:27:19,740
I don't think Hye Seon can be persuaded.

637
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:24,010
Well, I can't switch teams
for the same reasons I told you earlier.

638
00:27:24,710 --> 00:27:26,750
- I can't force you. Games are just games.
- Right.

639
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:29,420
What was that? Oh, the Heist Day. Even if
we exclude the things of the Heist Day...

640
00:27:29,820 --> 00:27:31,820
- That's it.
- There's nothing we can do.

641
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:35,260
- Let's have a good game then.
- Okay.

642
00:27:35,290 --> 00:27:37,260
- Can I talk to you one last time?
- Sure.

643
00:27:37,460 --> 00:27:40,130
You don't have any personal funds.

644
00:27:40,130 --> 00:27:41,300
- What?
- You don't have any personal funds.

645
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:42,770
- Right. I have no money.
- I can...

646
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:44,200
- Yes.
- Money?

647
00:27:44,900 --> 00:27:47,470
Well, that doesn't make
a lot of difference.

648
00:27:48,070 --> 00:27:49,140
Money doesn't matter.

649
00:27:49,140 --> 00:27:50,910
Well, you can buy items with the money.

650
00:27:50,970 --> 00:27:54,210
I told everything to Beom.

651
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:56,380
I was transparent with him.

652
00:27:56,380 --> 00:27:58,110
- I see.
- So he could understand my situation.

653
00:27:58,110 --> 00:28:01,120
I'm trying to join the team
with the lowest chance of elimination.

654
00:28:01,120 --> 00:28:02,220
I don't have any money.

655
00:28:02,220 --> 00:28:03,820
Joining the majority is the simplest
for me.

656
00:28:04,050 --> 00:28:05,760
I'm still neutral.

657
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:09,560
We can play together tomorrow
if there's a chance.

658
00:28:09,660 --> 00:28:10,830
- Good luck.
- Okay.

659
00:28:12,260 --> 00:28:13,530
I'll teach you how to rap too.

660
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:17,830
Good.

661
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:18,840
(The Majority Alliance has been finalized
with 7 players.)

662
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:20,140
I'll just sit here. It's okay.

663
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,570
(The Minority Alliance has been finalized
with 3 players.)

664
00:28:21,570 --> 00:28:23,910
- There's nothing we can do.
- Right. This is how it will go.

665
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:26,010
- We can do it.
- We can do it.

666
00:28:26,880 --> 00:28:28,410
I don't know.

667
00:28:28,750 --> 00:28:33,450
I just think it's a group of petty people.

668
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:34,880
They kept coming up with excuses.

669
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,950
By that logic,
people can start killing each other...

670
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:38,920
just for looking at them.

671
00:28:39,390 --> 00:28:42,260
It's like they want to eliminate us for
not following them back on social media.

672
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:45,500
How far will they go back in time
to come up with an excuse?

673
00:28:45,930 --> 00:28:48,300
"He glared at me on the day
when we untied the rope."

674
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:49,970
"I'll kill him."
How about that for an excuse?

675
00:28:51,270 --> 00:28:52,900
It was super infuriating.

676
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:56,140
I couldn't let my anger show.

677
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:57,670
There's nothing we can do.

678
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,280
I'll make you advance no matter what.

679
00:29:01,280 --> 00:29:02,480
- What?
- I'll make you advance.

680
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,820
What should we do?

681
00:29:09,990 --> 00:29:13,690
The 1st hint will be revealed
for 1 minute.

682
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:15,160
(Revealing the first hint)

683
00:29:15,890 --> 00:29:18,760
"At least one pair of twin clouds is..."

684
00:29:19,130 --> 00:29:20,960
"adjacent to a satellite."

685
00:29:22,570 --> 00:29:23,930
Let's go and check.

686
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:30,970
To a satellite?

687
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:33,710
It's adjacent to a satellite.

688
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:36,810
There are four pairs of twin clouds.

689
00:29:37,110 --> 00:29:39,480
At least two or more pairs are adjacent
to one another.

690
00:29:40,450 --> 00:29:43,390
Depending on the number
of twin clouds sectors players occupy,

691
00:29:43,650 --> 00:29:47,660
all the players can earn up
to three points.

692
00:29:48,090 --> 00:29:52,300
However, if all four twin clouds sectors
are occupied with players,

693
00:29:52,430 --> 00:29:55,030
all the players will lose three points.

694
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,070
Planets and satellites are next.

695
00:29:58,940 --> 00:30:01,570
There is only 1 planet.
And there are 2 satellites.

696
00:30:01,940 --> 00:30:05,010
They are located
in the eight consecutive sectors.

697
00:30:05,940 --> 00:30:07,880
The number of players
in the planet sector...

698
00:30:07,980 --> 00:30:10,680
is compared to the total number
of players across both satellite sectors.

699
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:14,720
Everyone in the majority sector
receives three points each.

700
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:17,920
If the player counts are tied,

701
00:30:18,220 --> 00:30:21,660
everyone in both sectors
will lose three points each.

702
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:24,160
(At least 1 pair of twin clouds is
adjacent to a satellite.)

703
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,830
Taking the first hint into consideration,

704
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:30,100
satellites are located
next to the twin clouds.

705
00:30:30,100 --> 00:30:31,600
(Twin clouds, satellite)

706
00:30:32,370 --> 00:30:34,600
Okay. That's a big piece of information.

707
00:30:34,600 --> 00:30:37,410
It means satellites are situated
next to the twin clouds.

708
00:30:37,710 --> 00:30:38,810
The three of them come as a set.

709
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:43,550
You know what I think?

710
00:30:44,210 --> 00:30:46,420
Teaming up in the beginning
might be tough.

711
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:47,580
- Yes.
- That won't be easy.

712
00:30:47,580 --> 00:30:48,820
- Splitting up might be better.
- Playing as a team might be hard.

713
00:30:48,820 --> 00:30:49,820
We should do that.

714
00:30:49,820 --> 00:30:51,920
That way, we'll see how people score
on their own.

715
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:53,020
That will give us more information.

716
00:30:53,020 --> 00:30:54,360
You're right. We should split up.

717
00:30:54,490 --> 00:30:56,360
Round One begins now.

718
00:30:57,590 --> 00:31:00,730
In Round 1,
players can observe Sectors 1 through 8.

719
00:31:01,260 --> 00:31:04,070
The black hole is in Sector One.

720
00:31:06,300 --> 00:31:08,710
- We can see where it is on the screen.
- It tells us where it is.

721
00:31:10,040 --> 00:31:11,980
Which sector do we want?

722
00:31:12,340 --> 00:31:13,380
What?

723
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:15,380
We should avoid losing points for now.

724
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:17,210
Winning 1st place? Well, to win 1st place,

725
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:19,750
getting the star sector would be best.

726
00:31:20,220 --> 00:31:21,620
If we know where it is,

727
00:31:22,020 --> 00:31:23,920
we'll place the black hole in that sector.

728
00:31:24,890 --> 00:31:27,020
We have to start betting
on the black hole.

729
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:28,860
What should we do?

730
00:31:30,260 --> 00:31:31,330
Well...

731
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:37,070
It's tough
since we don't have a lot of coins.

732
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:40,200
Asking a question
seems like the right move.

733
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:42,810
Let's go in order...

734
00:31:43,540 --> 00:31:45,610
and take one object each. One at a time...

735
00:31:45,610 --> 00:31:47,010
Our strategy in the beginning was simple.

736
00:31:47,010 --> 00:31:48,580
We had a lot of people on our team.

737
00:31:48,580 --> 00:31:50,310
There were seven of us.
So we asked about all of them.

738
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:51,880
We started from the top.

739
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:54,850
A satellite, a comet, a star,
a dwarf planet, and so on.

740
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:57,890
The range was from Sectors 1 through 8.
So we each asked a question.

741
00:31:58,020 --> 00:31:59,260
Hye Seon, you take the comet.

742
00:31:59,260 --> 00:32:00,520
- Okay.
- You take...

743
00:32:00,820 --> 00:32:02,060
- Go ahead. We can't waste time.
