00:52:09,260 --> 00:52:10,830
(4: Twin clouds, 5: Twin clouds,
16: Twin clouds might exist.)

1242
00:52:10,830 --> 00:52:12,830
It's not twin clouds,
so it can only be the comet.

1243
00:52:12,830 --> 00:52:15,300
You're right. It can only be that.

1244
00:52:16,040 --> 00:52:18,370
Observing Round One,

1245
00:52:18,810 --> 00:52:21,480
the two who came in last...

1246
00:52:21,480 --> 00:52:25,550
might not come from our team
if we put a bit more effort.

1247
00:52:25,550 --> 00:52:29,180
Work hard, and we might overcome it.

1248
00:52:29,180 --> 00:52:30,550
That was what I thought.

1249
00:52:30,820 --> 00:52:31,890
Then...

1250
00:52:32,920 --> 00:52:34,920
Let's ask about the dwarf planet.

1251
00:52:35,620 --> 00:52:37,890
There are two dwarf planets in total,

1252
00:52:38,190 --> 00:52:39,900
and they are not adjacent to a star.

1253
00:52:40,730 --> 00:52:44,130
Players lose two points
if they remain in a dwarf planet sector.

1254
00:52:44,130 --> 00:52:46,100
(Dwarf planet:
2, neither is adjacent to a star)

1255
00:52:46,200 --> 00:52:49,800
Where you definitely lose points is
where the dwarf planet is.

1256
00:52:49,910 --> 00:52:53,240
Figuring out where
the dwarf planet is fast seemed important,

1257
00:52:53,240 --> 00:52:56,780
so we asked many questions to find it.

1258
00:52:56,880 --> 00:52:58,610
(Observation: Dwarf planet)

1259
00:52:58,610 --> 00:53:00,480
There is one dwarf planet.

1260
00:53:00,820 --> 00:53:01,880
Thank you.

1261
00:53:02,280 --> 00:53:05,620
There is 1 dwarf planet in Sectors 3 to 7.

1262
00:53:06,760 --> 00:53:09,590
There are 2 satellites in Sectors 3 to 10.

1263
00:53:10,430 --> 00:53:11,890
(Celestial object information)

1264
00:53:11,890 --> 00:53:13,430
(Majority Alliance)

1265
00:53:13,430 --> 00:53:14,930
(Minority Alliance)

1266
00:53:15,030 --> 00:53:16,630
Where do we relocate to?

1267
00:53:16,830 --> 00:53:19,000
The other team must've used two...

1268
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:20,570
- Player Location Check Cards...
- Yes?

1269
00:53:20,570 --> 00:53:23,770
and found out we were in the twin clouds.

1270
00:53:24,140 --> 00:53:25,870
- Twin clouds?
- They would've found out...

1271
00:53:25,870 --> 00:53:29,440
the twin clouds are in Sectors 4, 5, or 6.

1272
00:53:30,050 --> 00:53:32,510
They'll probably move the black hole
to Sector Five.

1273
00:53:32,710 --> 00:53:34,020
- After going around once?
- Yes.

1274
00:53:34,650 --> 00:53:36,550
The other team will surely find out...

1275
00:53:36,750 --> 00:53:39,390
that our teammates are trying
to score points...

1276
00:53:39,750 --> 00:53:43,020
by finding out two twin clouds
and the satellite nearby.

1277
00:53:43,160 --> 00:53:46,630
The simplest and most straightforward
strategy the other team could play is...

1278
00:53:47,030 --> 00:53:48,530
to send the black hole to that area.

1279
00:53:48,530 --> 00:53:50,500
By doing so, all of our teammates...

1280
00:53:51,000 --> 00:53:54,670
in the twin clouds and satellite
would lose points.

1281
00:53:55,300 --> 00:53:56,710
But...

1282
00:53:56,710 --> 00:53:59,980
Sectors 4 and 5 are crowded with players.

1283
00:53:59,980 --> 00:54:00,980
Correct.

1284
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:03,240
Isn't it best to be among them?

1285
00:54:03,240 --> 00:54:04,710
Will they all run away?

1286
00:54:05,380 --> 00:54:07,620
I took it further.

1287
00:54:07,750 --> 00:54:12,120
Wouldn't they think we'd go
for that straightforward strategy...

1288
00:54:12,350 --> 00:54:14,220
and send it somewhere else instead?

1289
00:54:14,720 --> 00:54:16,630
The probability was 50-50.

1290
00:54:16,890 --> 00:54:19,260
I ended up choosing to save my coins
and stay there.

1291
00:54:19,660 --> 00:54:21,330
(Sector relocation: Sector 5)

1292
00:54:21,330 --> 00:54:23,670
- How may I help you?
- I'd like to move to Six.

1293
00:54:24,330 --> 00:54:26,800
You've been relocated to Sector Six.

1294
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:28,740
- Please head to the main hall.
- Thank you.

1295
00:54:29,870 --> 00:54:31,440
What is it? You wanted to talk, right?

1296
00:54:31,440 --> 00:54:34,610
Hold on. Those who asked earlier.

1297
00:54:35,180 --> 00:54:36,210
Keun Woo.

1298
00:54:36,210 --> 00:54:37,980
There's a planet
in Sectors 3 to 10, right?

1299
00:54:37,980 --> 00:54:39,080
- Yes.
- Okay.

1300
00:54:39,080 --> 00:54:40,720
Did you ask about the dwarf planet?

1301
00:54:40,720 --> 00:54:41,950
- One.
- What?

1302
00:54:41,950 --> 00:54:43,280
- There's 1 in Sectors 3 to 10.
- Okay, 1.

1303
00:54:43,490 --> 00:54:44,590
When you checked,

1304
00:54:44,590 --> 00:54:45,690
- the dwarf planet was in Seven, right?
- Yes.

1305
00:54:46,020 --> 00:54:50,190
(Jin Ho checked if the dwarf planet was
in Sectors 3 to 7.)

1306
00:54:50,530 --> 00:54:54,500
There is 1 dwarf planet in Sectors 3 to 7.

1307
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:55,630
Got it.

1308
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:56,770
Look.

1309
00:54:56,770 --> 00:54:59,500
Sector 1 is cosmic dust,
and Sector 8 is a planet.

1310
00:55:00,270 --> 00:55:01,800
I asked just now.

1311
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:04,010
My question was how many cosmic dusts
there were from 3 to 10.

1312
00:55:04,010 --> 00:55:05,070
She said two.

1313
00:55:05,070 --> 00:55:06,810
- Nine and ten are both cosmic dusts.
- You're right.

1314
00:55:07,540 --> 00:55:09,610
(The Majority Alliance
successfully pinpointed...)

1315
00:55:09,610 --> 00:55:11,280
(all objects aside from 5 sectors.)

1316
00:55:12,050 --> 00:55:14,080
The other team has
double the information...

1317
00:55:14,750 --> 00:55:16,350
that we have.

1318
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:19,450
Technically speaking,
it's more than double.

1319
00:55:20,120 --> 00:55:22,720
That team must've figured out
the whole celestial object.

1320
00:55:24,730 --> 00:55:27,200
The observation of Round Two
has just ended.

1321
00:55:27,830 --> 00:55:30,070
The number of questions
both teams asked...

1322
00:55:30,600 --> 00:55:32,400
is 14 to 6.

1323
00:55:33,070 --> 00:55:35,570
We're totally lost.
Once they figure out the objects,

1324
00:55:35,570 --> 00:55:39,240
the members would go to different sectors
and find their scores out.

1325
00:55:41,140 --> 00:55:43,650
You can literally go anywhere.

1326
00:55:43,980 --> 00:55:45,110
Yes, by using many coins.

1327
00:55:45,680 --> 00:55:47,980
I want to go to Two
to check out the comet.

1328
00:55:49,720 --> 00:55:52,290
We need such a move. What's good
about playing it conservatively?

1329
00:55:52,520 --> 00:55:54,190
It's just slowing us down.

1330
00:55:54,560 --> 00:55:56,060
Beom...

1331
00:55:56,220 --> 00:55:58,960
wanted to go explore.

1332
00:55:59,430 --> 00:56:03,200
We shouldn't be playing this game
conservatively.

1333
00:56:03,470 --> 00:56:05,630
If we don't have enough information,
we should use our coins...

1334
00:56:05,630 --> 00:56:06,870
and make a move from behind.

1335
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:09,570
If we go too slow
and the score gap gets too big,

1336
00:56:09,570 --> 00:56:11,370
it'll be over before we know it.

1337
00:56:13,840 --> 00:56:18,080
(Kwak Beom, who wants to explore,
enters the Voting Room.)

1338
00:56:18,350 --> 00:56:19,850
How may I help you?

1339
00:56:20,120 --> 00:56:21,620
As for me...

1340
00:56:22,080 --> 00:56:23,490
I'd like to relocate.

1341
00:56:24,020 --> 00:56:26,020
Which sector would you like to move to?

1342
00:56:26,020 --> 00:56:27,090
Two, please.

1343
00:56:27,720 --> 00:56:28,790
You've been relocated...

1344
00:56:28,790 --> 00:56:30,960
- to Sector Two.
- Great.

1345
00:56:31,260 --> 00:56:32,760
Please head to the main hall.

1346
00:56:32,760 --> 00:56:34,100
(Exploring for the comet)

1347
00:56:35,660 --> 00:56:37,370
Round Two has ended.

1348
00:56:38,370 --> 00:56:41,670
The 2nd hint will be revealed
for the next 1 minute.

1349
00:56:44,440 --> 00:56:48,010
At least one dwarf planet
is adjacent to a planet.

1350
00:56:48,010 --> 00:56:51,680
(At least 1 dwarf planet
is adjacent to a planet.)

1351
00:56:52,280 --> 00:56:54,450
Here are the results of Round Two.

1352
00:56:56,520 --> 00:56:58,220
(Points earned in Round 2)

1353
00:56:58,220 --> 00:57:01,120
(Points earned, total score)

1354
00:57:01,590 --> 00:57:05,060
Round 3 will now begin
and run for 30 minutes.

1355
00:57:06,330 --> 00:57:08,930
The black hole was moved to Five?

1356
00:57:08,930 --> 00:57:10,030
That's a big move.

1357
00:57:10,400 --> 00:57:14,040
(Majority Alliance's black hole
strategy meeting during Round 2)

1358
00:57:14,200 --> 00:57:15,870
Because the other team earned points,

1359
00:57:15,870 --> 00:57:17,470
they might maintain their strategy.

1360
00:57:17,640 --> 00:57:21,010
We will drop the bomb
in Sectors 4, 5, or 6 just like before.

1361
00:57:21,310 --> 00:57:22,580
Look.

1362
00:57:22,940 --> 00:57:24,580
The black hole is in Seven right now.

1363
00:57:24,580 --> 00:57:25,880
- It's in 8.
- In 8, right?

1364
00:57:25,880 --> 00:57:28,820
We'd have to use a bunch of coins
to get it over here from Eight.

1365
00:57:29,080 --> 00:57:33,120
Can't one person bet on the black hole
multiple times?

1366
00:57:33,190 --> 00:57:34,460
- Like the Mute Card.
- True.

1367
00:57:34,460 --> 00:57:36,290
Let's say we have 35 coins.

1368
00:57:36,490 --> 00:57:38,160
We could send the black hole 2 to 3 times.

1369
00:57:38,430 --> 00:57:40,260
Since the other team has no information,

1370
00:57:40,260 --> 00:57:43,530
I'm sure the orders are Kwak Beom, Ji Hoo,
and then Seung Yong.

1371
00:57:43,530 --> 00:57:46,070
- I want to crush them.
- You do?

1372
00:57:50,310 --> 00:57:53,410
Hyun Sung Joo,
you have submitted 13 coins.

1373
00:57:53,410 --> 00:57:55,140
(Relocated the black hole to Sector 5)

1374
00:57:56,240 --> 00:57:58,610
I shouldn't have gotten too far ahead.

1375
00:57:59,410 --> 00:58:02,320
Luckily, I remained in that location.

1376
00:58:02,980 --> 00:58:04,650
So I was the only one
who got caught by it,

1377
00:58:04,750 --> 00:58:06,650
and the other two had already fled.

1378
00:58:07,020 --> 00:58:08,620
That was a relief.

1379
00:58:11,830 --> 00:58:16,400
(Ji Min enters the Voting Room.)

1380
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:18,030
How may I help you?

1381
00:58:18,030 --> 00:58:19,230
I'd like to ask a question.

1382
00:58:19,530 --> 00:58:23,540
Is the twin cloud anywhere
between Sectors 5 and 12?

1383
00:58:23,540 --> 00:58:24,770
(Black hole: Twin clouds)

1384
00:58:24,770 --> 00:58:27,010
There's 1 pair of twin clouds
in Sectors 5 to 12.

1385
00:58:27,280 --> 00:58:29,740
- There's 1 pair of it in Sectors 5 to 12?
- Yes.

1386
00:58:29,740 --> 00:58:31,180
That means it's in Five.

1387
00:58:31,410 --> 00:58:34,420
It's 15 and 16.

1388
00:58:34,580 --> 00:58:37,590
The clues fell into place
one after the other.

1389
00:58:37,820 --> 00:58:41,390
Looking at the celestial objects,
we got most of the locations.

1390
00:58:41,860 --> 00:58:44,460
We simply had to figure out
who went to which sector...

1391
00:58:44,460 --> 00:58:46,360
as quickly as possible.

1392
00:58:46,530 --> 00:58:49,160
Calculate your score
and tell me which sector you were in,

1393
00:58:49,160 --> 00:58:51,700
as well as what you would've needed
in this round.

1394
00:58:52,670 --> 00:58:54,670
I'm letter E for sure.

1395
00:58:55,440 --> 00:58:57,740
Sung Joo and Ji Min are probably
B and I, respectively.

1396
00:58:58,140 --> 00:59:02,180
We moved to the satellite
and scored three points.

1397
00:59:02,640 --> 00:59:04,180
Three points? That makes sense.

1398
00:59:05,010 --> 00:59:06,950
He's on a comet,

1399
00:59:07,420 --> 00:59:10,590
and someone else landed on a comet,
so you couldn't score points.

1400
00:59:10,920 --> 00:59:13,090
Then I'm likely 1 of these 2.

1401
00:59:13,450 --> 00:59:16,490
I'm probably on twin clouds. Sector 16.

1402
00:59:16,660 --> 00:59:18,190
Does that mean only you scored?

1403
00:59:18,190 --> 00:59:20,160
I got one point.

1404
00:59:20,300 --> 00:59:22,060
Nobody was on Sectors 4 and 5
for twin clouds.

1405
00:59:22,460 --> 00:59:23,830
That's how I got the points by myself.

1406
00:59:23,830 --> 00:59:26,170
I don't know
where the remaining one point came from.

1407
00:59:26,300 --> 00:59:27,770
- Keun Woo and YunB...
- You're right.

1408
00:59:27,770 --> 00:59:29,770
shared the comet score. Two points each.

1409
00:59:31,370 --> 00:59:33,170
(The Majority Alliance deduced
many alphabets.)

1410
00:59:33,170 --> 00:59:34,640
(Jin Ho, Ji Min or Sung Joo,
YunB or Keun Woo, Hye Seon,)

1411
00:59:34,640 --> 00:59:36,340
(Ji Hoo or Kwak Beom, Seung Yong,
Ji Min or Sung Joo, Seong Beom)

1412
00:59:36,780 --> 00:59:38,780
How did he score one point?

1413
00:59:39,250 --> 00:59:40,450
- Seung Yong?
- Yes.

1414
00:59:41,250 --> 00:59:44,190
(Majority Alliance deduced G
to be Seung Yong.)

1415
00:59:44,450 --> 00:59:45,950
G, one point.

1416
00:59:47,820 --> 00:59:48,990
How did this happen?

1417
00:59:50,290 --> 00:59:52,090
Seung Yong could've moved
to either Sector 5 or Sector 7.

1418
00:59:52,090 --> 00:59:53,960
Sector 7 is minus 2,
but that wasn't his score.

1419
00:59:54,160 --> 00:59:55,330
He can't have been in Sector 7.

1420
00:59:55,330 --> 00:59:56,330
- Exactly.
- Four or five.

1421
00:59:56,330 --> 00:59:57,870
He must've jumped.

1422
00:59:58,130 --> 01:00:00,600
He neither went here nor there.

1423
01:00:00,600 --> 01:00:01,840
Where did he go to?

1424
01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:04,370
Maybe this isn't Seung Yong.

1425
01:00:07,680 --> 01:00:09,940
What are the ways
for 2 people to score 1 point?

1426
01:00:10,950 --> 01:00:13,110
Two people in the same twin clouds sector.

1427
01:00:15,050 --> 01:00:16,650
It makes sense if two people were...

1428
01:00:16,650 --> 01:00:18,520
in the same twin clouds sector.

1429
01:00:19,490 --> 01:00:21,220
Someone else came to your sector.

1430
01:00:21,990 --> 01:00:23,120
He jumped that much?

1431
01:00:23,120 --> 01:00:25,290
- That's why I said it didn't make sense.
- That doesn't make sense.

1432
01:00:25,290 --> 01:00:27,260
But that's the only explanation.

1433
01:00:27,560 --> 01:00:28,830
(10 minutes ago)

1434
01:00:28,830 --> 01:00:31,070
I'll relocate the sector.

1435
01:00:31,730 --> 01:00:33,770
Which sector would you like to move to?

1436
01:00:34,400 --> 01:00:36,600
Sector 16.

1437
01:00:37,040 --> 01:00:38,740
If we stay in the same sector,

1438
01:00:39,070 --> 01:00:41,140
we cannot learn new information.

1439
01:00:41,140 --> 01:00:43,810
Since Seung Yong already had
a lot of points deducted,

1440
01:00:44,180 --> 01:00:46,650
we decided to send him
to another side to explore...

1441
01:00:46,650 --> 01:00:47,750
the uncharted territory.

1442
01:00:48,020 --> 01:00:50,120
Which means Seung Yong was
in Sector 16 this round.

1443
01:00:50,120 --> 01:00:51,350
From 6 to 16.

1444
01:00:53,420 --> 01:00:54,660
Who hasn't asked a question yet?

1445
01:00:54,660 --> 01:00:55,720
- Have you?
- Not yet.

1446
01:00:55,720 --> 01:00:56,890
Then go...

1447
01:00:57,090 --> 01:00:59,660
and ask about dwarf planets
between Sectors 5 and 11.

1448
01:00:59,660 --> 01:01:01,200
Sectors 5 to 11, dwarf planet.

1449
01:01:01,500 --> 01:01:05,330
How many dwarf planets are there
from Sectors 5 to 11?

1450
01:01:08,970 --> 01:01:10,470
- So?
- Two.

1451
01:01:10,470 --> 01:01:12,110
- Two? Got them.
- Right.

1452
01:01:12,110 --> 01:01:13,170
(2 dwarf planets)

1453
01:01:13,170 --> 01:01:16,610
By the time we asked 1 to 2 questions
in the beginning of Round 3,

1454
01:01:17,110 --> 01:01:18,780
we identified the 16 sectors...

1455
01:01:18,780 --> 01:01:21,020
of Project Galaxy,
the most important part of the game.

1456
01:01:21,020 --> 01:01:22,920
(They've identified every celestial object
except the star in 3 rounds.)

1457
01:01:24,090 --> 01:01:26,620
Did they go to cosmic dust
to get zero points?

1458
01:01:26,920 --> 01:01:28,690
- That's possible.
- Definitely.

1459
01:01:28,690 --> 01:01:30,430
They are...

1460
01:01:30,430 --> 01:01:32,130
(Cosmic dust, no change in scores)

1461
01:01:32,130 --> 01:01:35,460
searching for the star as well.

1462
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:38,300
Figuring out the star's location
as soon as possible...

1463
01:01:38,500 --> 01:01:41,200
before the opponents do...

1464
01:01:41,200 --> 01:01:42,700
and moving the black hole there...

1465
01:01:42,700 --> 01:01:45,710
to give them minus five points...

1466
01:01:45,840 --> 01:01:48,380
could turn the tables.

1467
01:01:48,610 --> 01:01:51,380
We need to find the star quickly.

1468
01:01:51,610 --> 01:01:53,280
The moment we find the star,

1469
01:01:53,280 --> 01:01:56,220
we'll all go to the sector with it.
Then the game ends.

1470
01:01:56,420 --> 01:01:58,950
- The star isn't here.
- Definitely not.

1471
01:01:59,190 --> 01:02:01,060
- Why not Sector 1?
- Because I got 0 points.

1472
01:02:01,060 --> 01:02:03,260
She was here, and she got zero points.

1473
01:02:03,360 --> 01:02:05,030
We need to send YunB on a business trip.

1474
01:02:05,260 --> 01:02:07,430
You need to go to Sector 13,
the one nearby.

1475
01:02:08,500 --> 01:02:09,960
How may I help you?

1476
01:02:10,130 --> 01:02:12,530
I'll relocate to Sector 13.

1477
01:02:12,530 --> 01:02:13,700
(YunB goes on a journey to find the star.)

1478
01:02:13,700 --> 01:02:15,540
I'll keep going as is.

1479
01:02:16,070 --> 01:02:18,810
You've chosen Sector 13.

1480
01:02:19,010 --> 01:02:20,840
Should I go to 15 this time?

1481
01:02:20,840 --> 01:02:22,410
You're going to 15? Then I'll go to 16.

1482
01:02:22,410 --> 01:02:23,740
Then I'll go to 16.

1483
01:02:23,740 --> 01:02:25,180
I'll just go to 15.

1484
01:02:25,180 --> 01:02:26,450
I didn't check that.

1485
01:02:26,910 --> 01:02:29,850
Round 3 ends in 5 minutes.

1486
01:02:30,350 --> 01:02:32,220
There are so many things to do
for this game.

1487
01:02:32,620 --> 01:02:34,220
How may I help you?

1488
01:02:34,620 --> 01:02:36,420
I'll relocate to Sector 15.

1489
01:02:36,690 --> 01:02:38,630
I'll relocate to Sector 16.

1490
01:02:39,190 --> 01:02:40,760
How may I help you?

1491
01:02:40,900 --> 01:02:42,400
I'll relocate.

1492
01:02:43,260 --> 01:02:44,830
I'll relocate to Sector 14.

1493
01:02:48,800 --> 01:02:50,540
They might move the black hole,
don't you think?

1494
01:02:51,210 --> 01:02:52,270
- Right.
- Yes.

1495
01:02:52,270 --> 01:02:53,770
They'll aim for the twin clouds, right?

1496
01:02:54,640 --> 01:02:55,640
The twins?

1497
01:02:55,640 --> 01:02:57,040
Don't you think
they'll aim for the twin clouds?

1498
01:02:57,410 --> 01:02:58,610
- Here?
- Sectors 15 and 16.

1499
01:02:58,880 --> 01:03:00,110
Will they attack this?

1500
01:03:00,950 --> 01:03:02,780
Should we...

1501
01:03:02,950 --> 01:03:04,990
Is it time for us to gamble here?

1502
01:03:04,990 --> 01:03:06,420
Should we bet on the black hole?

1503
01:03:06,620 --> 01:03:08,390
But it's too early to use it.

1504
01:03:08,390 --> 01:03:09,520
No.

1505
01:03:09,690 --> 01:03:11,590
Using it now to stir them up
could be a way.

1506
01:03:11,790 --> 01:03:13,560
But we have seven more rounds left.

1507
01:03:13,560 --> 01:03:15,600
If we move the back hole now
by placing a bet,

1508
01:03:15,600 --> 01:03:16,800
we can't do it anymore later.

1509
01:03:17,600 --> 01:03:18,730
I'm torn.

1510
01:03:18,730 --> 01:03:21,500
I can't decide which move to make.

1511
01:03:22,240 --> 01:03:24,570
It was a really crucial moment.

1512
01:03:25,110 --> 01:03:28,110
We had the same scores as them
in Round One,

1513
01:03:28,480 --> 01:03:30,440
and we were slightly behind in Round Two.

1514
01:03:30,880 --> 01:03:32,980
If we played our cards right
in Round Three,

1515
01:03:32,980 --> 01:03:34,380
we could win.

1516
01:03:37,320 --> 01:03:39,550
Here are the results of Round 3.

1517
01:03:41,260 --> 01:03:42,990
(Points earned in Round 3)

1518
01:03:42,990 --> 01:03:47,530
(Points earned, total score)

1519
01:03:48,160 --> 01:03:51,670
Round 4 will now begin
and run for 30 minutes.

1520
01:03:51,670 --> 01:03:54,200
(Points earned in Round 3)

1521
01:03:54,200 --> 01:03:55,600
(F and H, minus 5)

1522
01:03:55,600 --> 01:03:57,770
(Surprised)

1523
01:04:02,340 --> 01:04:04,180
There are 2 minus 5?

1524
01:04:04,980 --> 01:04:07,280
We expected it could be possible
to get minus 2 or 3 points...

1525
01:04:07,380 --> 01:04:10,080
after the attack.

1526
01:04:10,450 --> 01:04:12,450
And out of nowhere, we got minus 5.

1527
01:04:13,960 --> 01:04:15,120
What happened?

1528
01:04:16,120 --> 01:04:17,160
I was...

1529
01:04:17,160 --> 01:04:19,330
so confused when I saw it.

1530
01:04:19,590 --> 01:04:21,860
Why did we get minus five?

1531
01:04:21,860 --> 01:04:24,700
That's only possible
if they were in the star sector...

1532
01:04:24,700 --> 01:04:27,300
and got black holed.

1533
01:04:27,700 --> 01:04:30,440
Minus five happens...

1534
01:04:30,870 --> 01:04:33,440
when the initial 5 points turn
into minus 5 points...

1535
01:04:33,440 --> 01:04:35,210
due to the black hole's effect.

1536
01:04:35,880 --> 01:04:40,210
You can score five points
on the comet and the star.

1537
01:04:40,210 --> 01:04:41,350
(Comet)

1538
01:04:41,350 --> 01:04:45,450
But only one person is allowed
in the sectors with comets...

1539
01:04:45,690 --> 01:04:47,620
to be able to score five points
to themselves.

1540
01:04:48,660 --> 01:04:51,090
Which means there cannot be
multiple five-point scorers.

1541
01:04:51,090 --> 01:04:52,760
(Comet)

1542
01:04:53,390 --> 01:04:55,100
How come there are 2 minus 5 scorers?

1543
01:05:00,400 --> 01:05:01,500
The only way to score five...

1544
01:05:01,500 --> 01:05:03,140
is staying in a comet by yourself, right?

1545
01:05:03,140 --> 01:05:04,140
This doesn't make sense.

1546
01:05:04,140 --> 01:05:06,440
(You can't have multiple 5-point scorers
with a comet.)

1547
01:05:06,440 --> 01:05:08,140
So that's the star, not a comet.

1548
01:05:09,580 --> 01:05:10,980
How did the five points come about?

1549
01:05:10,980 --> 01:05:12,480
(Majority Alliance gathers
in the pantry quickly.)

1550
01:05:12,980 --> 01:05:15,180
The black hole is the only thing...

1551
01:05:15,180 --> 01:05:16,920
- that can result in minus five.
- Right.

1552
01:05:18,420 --> 01:05:19,790
But that doesn't make sense...

1553
01:05:20,190 --> 01:05:22,260
because 3 people can't score 5 points.

1554
01:05:23,260 --> 01:05:25,390
You score from a comet
if you're on a comet alone.

1555
01:05:29,200 --> 01:05:31,500
What if, by sheer luck,

1556
01:05:31,500 --> 01:05:33,130
all three of them were on the star?

1557
01:05:33,130 --> 01:05:34,970
Or we got the whole thing wrong.

1558
01:05:34,970 --> 01:05:36,370
It's one or the other.

1559
01:05:38,140 --> 01:05:40,110
There's only one possibility,
going by the rule.

1560
01:05:40,170 --> 01:05:44,050
If we move the black hole
to the sector with the star,

1561
01:05:44,380 --> 01:05:47,150
plus 5 will reverse to become minus 5.

1562
01:05:49,880 --> 01:05:54,560
(Jin Ho checks the black hole's location
for Round 3.)

1563
01:05:54,560 --> 01:05:57,220
They wouldn't know where the star is...

1564
01:05:57,360 --> 01:05:58,730
when even we don't know yet.

1565
01:05:58,730 --> 01:06:01,030
We know where the black hole is,

1566
01:06:01,030 --> 01:06:02,200
and there's no star there.

1567
01:06:02,430 --> 01:06:03,960
So it's not that case.

1568
01:06:04,900 --> 01:06:06,370
Gosh, what's happening?

1569
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:08,340
Why doesn't it make sense?

1570
01:06:09,870 --> 01:06:11,410
The black hole...

1571
01:06:11,410 --> 01:06:13,840
The star didn't explode
from the black hole.

1572
01:06:13,840 --> 01:06:14,980
That's right.

1573
01:06:14,980 --> 01:06:17,240
(No matter what scores they plug in,
they get an error.)

1574
01:06:17,450 --> 01:06:19,610
I had a mental breakdown.

1575
01:06:20,080 --> 01:06:23,350
We might've gotten
the whole planisphere wrong.

1576
01:06:23,750 --> 01:06:25,690
If we'd calculated wrongly from the start,

1577
01:06:26,090 --> 01:06:28,220
where do we need to restart from?

1578
01:06:28,620 --> 01:06:30,930
It was so daunting.

1579
01:06:31,460 --> 01:06:33,890
If we need to redo the whole thing,
where did we get it wrong?

1580
01:06:35,800 --> 01:06:37,970
I might've missed a spy.

1581
01:06:38,970 --> 01:06:41,170
We might have a rat among us.

1582
01:06:44,410 --> 01:06:47,480
They got really confused because of us.

1583
01:06:51,550 --> 01:06:52,780
(10 minutes ago)

1584
01:06:52,780 --> 01:06:55,050
Since we mostly figured it out...

1585
01:06:55,050 --> 01:06:57,120
It all comes down to placing bets
in the later rounds.

1586
01:06:57,390 --> 01:06:58,420
Yes.

1587
01:06:58,420 --> 01:06:59,550
Let's go.

1588
01:07:04,160 --> 01:07:05,760
How many coins do you have left?

1589
01:07:05,760 --> 01:07:07,900
Or would it be better
for you to relocate the black hole?

1590
01:07:07,900 --> 01:07:10,100
I can do that. Where to?

1591
01:07:10,530 --> 01:07:11,930
How many coins did you use?

1592
01:07:12,270 --> 01:07:14,300
I used quite a lot. Wait, I didn't.

1593
01:07:14,300 --> 01:07:15,700
- You used four.
- Yes.

1594
01:07:16,900 --> 01:07:19,640
I queued up after the round ended,

1595
01:07:19,640 --> 01:07:21,040
so I can't enter. That's what she said.

1596
01:07:24,480 --> 01:07:25,510
Kang Ji Hoo.

1597
01:07:25,510 --> 01:07:28,120
You've queued up after the round ended,

1598
01:07:28,120 --> 01:07:29,250
so you may not enter.

1599
01:07:32,590 --> 01:07:34,120
She said the time was up.

1600
01:07:34,490 --> 01:07:36,790
So there was nothing I could do.

1601
01:07:37,320 --> 01:07:38,730
- But we were in line here.
- Yes.

1602
01:07:38,960 --> 01:07:40,690
Is it because I went down
to fetch the note?

1603
01:07:41,600 --> 01:07:42,830
Wait.

1604
01:07:43,400 --> 01:07:44,730
I have a question.

1605
01:07:46,870 --> 01:07:50,170
Does lining up behind Seong Beom
not count?

1606
01:07:50,670 --> 01:07:52,670
You have lined up
after the announcement...

1607
01:07:52,670 --> 01:07:54,380
that the round has ended.

1608
01:07:57,550 --> 01:08:00,750
(1 minute before Round 3 ended)

1609
01:08:00,750 --> 01:08:03,350
Round 3 ends in 1 minute.

1610
01:08:04,650 --> 01:08:05,750
This.

1611
01:08:06,490 --> 01:08:07,520
What's that?

1612
01:08:07,890 --> 01:08:09,590
Shall we move to Sector 13?

1613
01:08:09,890 --> 01:08:11,760
- Sounds like a plan.
- I'll go here.

1614
01:08:11,760 --> 01:08:13,430
I'll relocate the black hole to Sector 15.

1615
01:08:13,430 --> 01:08:15,100
(Glancing)

1616
01:08:15,100 --> 01:08:16,460
We should bet on both...

1617
01:08:16,730 --> 01:08:17,730
Yes.

1618
01:08:17,730 --> 01:08:19,700
We still have enough coins.

1619
01:08:19,700 --> 01:08:21,500
We should try and gamble.

1620
01:08:21,500 --> 01:08:24,170
We must try what we can in this round.

1621
01:08:24,170 --> 01:08:27,140
- Good idea.
- Round Three has ended.

1622
01:08:31,110 --> 01:08:32,380
That sounds like a good idea.

1623
01:08:32,580 --> 01:08:34,250
So two of us will go to Sector 3?

1624
01:08:34,250 --> 01:08:36,050
(Minority Alliance did not relocate
to another sector.)

1625
01:08:36,050 --> 01:08:37,350
- Both of you?
- Yes.

1626
01:08:37,620 --> 01:08:38,920
Do you want to go
to the same or different sector?

1627
01:08:40,520 --> 01:08:42,090
Let's line up.

1628
01:08:42,690 --> 01:08:43,820
Shall we?

1629
01:08:44,590 --> 01:08:47,390
We were discussing
the locations of the stars...

1630
01:08:47,390 --> 01:08:49,760
and the sector relocations.

1631
01:08:50,060 --> 01:08:51,870
We were too focused...

1632
01:08:51,870 --> 01:08:53,770
that we missed the announcement.

1633
01:08:53,770 --> 01:08:55,800
So we couldn't relocate.

1634
01:08:56,040 --> 01:08:58,770
(Minority Alliance has exceeded
the time limit.)

1635
01:08:58,770 --> 01:09:00,940
"There must be a mistake."

1636
01:09:00,940 --> 01:09:03,380
That was what I thought at first.

1637
01:09:03,980 --> 01:09:07,780
When I found out that wasn't the case,

1638
01:09:08,650 --> 01:09:11,420
I realized I'd made a mistake.

1639
01:09:11,750 --> 01:09:14,050
We were definitely lined up.

1640
01:09:14,660 --> 01:09:16,020
Did we line up after the time was up?

1641
01:09:16,520 --> 01:09:17,560
We were confused.

1642
01:09:18,730 --> 01:09:20,260
It felt like the sky was falling.

1643
01:09:20,730 --> 01:09:21,830
I was so upset.

1644
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:23,630
We can't relocate either.

1645
01:09:23,630 --> 01:09:25,030
We can't enter the room at all.

1646
01:09:25,100 --> 01:09:26,530
We can't take any action.

1647
01:09:26,700 --> 01:09:27,900
Darn it.

1648
01:09:28,500 --> 01:09:30,200
It'll be minus five for us.

1649
01:09:31,510 --> 01:09:32,640
If we can't move.

1650
01:09:32,940 --> 01:09:34,070
That's a rule?

1651
01:09:34,340 --> 01:09:36,710
"If you do not relocate to
a different sector before the round ends,"

1652
01:09:36,710 --> 01:09:39,610
"five points will be deducted
from the round's points."

1653
01:09:40,310 --> 01:09:42,180
I'm sorry. We're stuck.

1654
01:09:42,880 --> 01:09:44,350
We messed up badly.

1655
01:09:44,690 --> 01:09:46,250
We didn't queue up.

1656
01:09:46,990 --> 01:09:50,260
I checked the rule book,
and it was minus five points.

1657
01:09:50,820 --> 01:09:53,230
It's hard to get just one point,

1658
01:09:53,460 --> 01:09:54,630
but minus five?

1659
01:09:55,700 --> 01:09:57,770
Pretend that we relocated.

1660
01:09:57,970 --> 01:09:59,030
Pretend.

1661
01:09:59,030 --> 01:10:01,470
- Okay.
- Pretend that we relocated.

1662
01:10:01,970 --> 01:10:03,500
We have no other choice.

1663
01:10:03,600 --> 01:10:06,110
This is how we'll shake them up.

1664
01:10:06,110 --> 01:10:07,270
We need to make them think,

1665
01:10:07,270 --> 01:10:09,610
"How did they get minus five
when they relocated?"

1666
01:10:10,680 --> 01:10:11,980
We hardened our resolves.

1667
01:10:11,980 --> 01:10:14,080
"We can do it." We couldn't give up.

1668
01:10:14,180 --> 01:10:16,380
Let's stay mentally strong.

1669
01:10:16,720 --> 01:10:18,590
The other team must be confused too.

1670
01:10:19,020 --> 01:10:20,420
Let's not show how upset we are.

1671
01:10:20,590 --> 01:10:22,190
They can see we got minus five,

1672
01:10:22,420 --> 01:10:24,330
but they don't know why.

1673
01:10:24,530 --> 01:10:26,190
We must never let it show
that we couldn't go in.

1674
01:10:26,560 --> 01:10:29,100
Let's pretend that we landed on the star
and got hit by the black hole.

1675
01:10:31,870 --> 01:10:33,270
That means I'm H.

1676
01:10:34,340 --> 01:10:36,340
We can use the black hole
in the next round.

1677
01:10:36,800 --> 01:10:38,010
You can go on a challenge without worries.

1678
01:10:38,010 --> 01:10:39,510
(Minority Alliance
discusses enthusiastically.)

1679
01:10:39,510 --> 01:10:42,210
We need to find out the exact location
of the star and everything.

1680
01:10:42,210 --> 01:10:43,440
(Round 4, total score)

1681
01:10:43,440 --> 01:10:44,680
(Comet, satellite, twin clouds, satellite,
dwarf planet, planet, comet, twin clouds)

1682
01:10:44,680 --> 01:10:46,110
What do we still not know?

1683
01:10:46,450 --> 01:10:47,680
- Dwarf planet.
- Okay.

1684
01:10:49,050 --> 01:10:50,450
Dwarf planet, star,

1685
01:10:50,450 --> 01:10:51,720
- cosmic dust.
- Cosmic dust.

1686
01:10:52,850 --> 01:10:54,690
("Dwarf planet is not adjacent
to a star.")

1687
01:10:54,690 --> 01:10:55,690
Sector 14 is...

1688
01:10:55,690 --> 01:10:57,090
(Using this rule,
you can specify the star's location.)

1689
01:10:57,290 --> 01:10:59,430
All we can do is ask for the dwarf planet.

1690
01:11:00,330 --> 01:11:01,600
Will you go and ask?

1691
01:11:01,600 --> 01:11:04,000
Four are cosmic dusts
and one is a dwarf planet, right?

1692
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:05,000
Yes.

1693
01:11:05,000 --> 01:11:07,030
We haven't found the star yet,

1694
01:11:07,230 --> 01:11:11,370
so if we find it
at least a round before the opponents,

1695
01:11:11,470 --> 01:11:13,370
we could make up for the loss.

1696
01:11:13,570 --> 01:11:17,010
I thought we should do our best
to find the star...

1697
01:11:17,010 --> 01:11:18,980
in the next round.

1698
01:11:20,210 --> 01:11:21,750
From Sectors 7 to 14,

1699
01:11:23,650 --> 01:11:24,990
how many dwarf planets are there?

1700
01:11:25,320 --> 01:11:29,260
There are 2 dwarf planets
from Sectors 7 to 14.

1701
01:11:29,920 --> 01:11:31,230
There are two dwarf planets.

1702
01:11:31,230 --> 01:11:32,760
(Dwarf planet, planet, comet)

1703
01:11:32,760 --> 01:11:34,260
Sector One is cosmic dust, confirmed.

1704
01:11:34,260 --> 01:11:37,460
(Sector 1, cosmic dust)

1705
01:11:38,000 --> 01:11:39,170
Hello.

1706
01:11:40,670 --> 01:11:45,210
How many dwarf planets are there
from Sectors 10 to 14?

1707
01:11:45,470 --> 01:11:49,840
There is 1 dwarf planet
from Sectors 10 to 14.

1708
01:11:49,840 --> 01:11:50,980
(Observation: Dwarf planet, 1)

1709
01:11:50,980 --> 01:11:53,110
One.

1710
01:11:53,410 --> 01:11:55,080
This is confirmed as cosmic dust.

1711
01:11:55,080 --> 01:11:57,850
(Sector 9, cosmic dust)

1712
01:11:57,850 --> 01:12:00,920
A dwarf planet from Sectors 10 to 14.

1713
01:12:01,520 --> 01:12:02,790
What question should I ask?

1714
01:12:03,090 --> 01:12:04,860
Why don't we...

1715
01:12:05,590 --> 01:12:06,790
Yes, make it less.

1716
01:12:07,230 --> 01:12:08,300
To check smaller sectors,

1717
01:12:08,300 --> 01:12:09,530
- you need to use more coins.
- Use them.

1718
01:12:09,700 --> 01:12:11,530
And I'll buy more coins.

1719
01:12:15,540 --> 01:12:17,770
Think about a risky move.

1720
01:12:20,070 --> 01:12:21,680
What risky move should we make?

1721
01:12:21,880 --> 01:12:23,780
I have 15 coins left.

1722
01:12:23,940 --> 01:12:25,580
Should I make a risky move this round?

1723
01:12:27,310 --> 01:12:29,520
Shall we just stand there and talk,
just to be safe?

1724
01:12:29,520 --> 01:12:30,550
Okay.

1725
01:12:30,950 --> 01:12:32,390
That sounds about right.

1726
01:12:32,720 --> 01:12:34,560
This is our turf now.

1727
01:12:34,560 --> 01:12:35,560
Goodness.

1728
01:12:36,290 --> 01:12:37,930
- That was terrible.
- I agree.

1729
01:12:38,490 --> 01:12:40,930
- Let's discuss here.
- Okay.

1730
01:12:40,930 --> 01:12:43,000
(They moved to a cozier meeting space.)

1731
01:12:44,400 --> 01:12:47,800
How many dwarf planets are there
from Sectors 7 to 10?

1732
01:12:48,270 --> 01:12:52,410
There is 1 dwarf planet
from Sectors 7 to 10.

1733
01:12:52,410 --> 01:12:53,610
Darn it.

1734
01:12:53,610 --> 01:12:56,480
(Observation: Dwarf planet, 1)

1735
01:12:56,510 --> 01:12:57,580
I'll buy coins.

1736
01:12:57,580 --> 01:12:59,350
- Would you like to purchase coins?
- Yes.

1737
01:13:00,110 --> 01:13:01,850
You get five coins.

1738
01:13:01,850 --> 01:13:04,280
(He purchased a 5-coin item
at 10,000 dollars.)

1739
01:13:04,280 --> 01:13:07,520
(The dwarf planet candidates
and the star candidates...)

1740
01:13:07,520 --> 01:13:10,860
(were narrowed down
with the observations.)

1741
01:13:13,030 --> 01:13:14,190
It...

1742
01:13:14,430 --> 01:13:15,500
Hi.

1743
01:13:16,160 --> 01:13:18,070
I bought coins, so I have 25 now.

1744
01:13:18,470 --> 01:13:21,140
