So I felt a lot more helpless.

1999
01:23:30,780 --> 01:23:34,250
We did our best until Round Four.

2000
01:23:34,510 --> 01:23:35,880
But the score gap increased so much...

2001
01:23:35,880 --> 01:23:37,420
that we couldn't catch up.

2002
01:23:37,420 --> 01:23:40,250
The game is as good as finished.

2003
01:23:40,890 --> 01:23:43,160
The opponents decide
where the black hole goes too.

2004
01:23:43,390 --> 01:23:45,490
I've already scored minus five,

2005
01:23:45,630 --> 01:23:47,330
so there was no way I could win.

2006
01:23:47,630 --> 01:23:49,730
The more we played,

2007
01:23:50,660 --> 01:23:51,930
the deeper we dug our grave.

2008
01:23:52,270 --> 01:23:54,400
Ji Hoo must've finished his calculation.

2009
01:23:54,400 --> 01:23:55,970
He would've known in his head.

2010
01:23:55,970 --> 01:23:57,040
We can't...

2011
01:23:59,470 --> 01:24:00,770
win this game.

2012
01:24:01,070 --> 01:24:02,080
We've started...

2013
01:24:03,210 --> 01:24:05,510
to accept defeat.

2014
01:24:06,310 --> 01:24:08,310
I don't think
they'll relocate the black hole...

2015
01:24:08,310 --> 01:24:09,420
to where the star is.

2016
01:24:09,420 --> 01:24:10,950
We're locked into last places.

2017
01:24:10,950 --> 01:24:12,550
Last place has been decided.

2018
01:24:12,620 --> 01:24:14,320
No matter how much we struggle,

2019
01:24:14,820 --> 01:24:16,490
we can't catch up.

2020
01:24:18,730 --> 01:24:21,760
They've divided themselves into groups.

2021
01:24:22,000 --> 01:24:23,160
"You go here."

2022
01:24:23,430 --> 01:24:25,030
"I went here. You scored this much,
and I scored this much."

2023
01:24:25,030 --> 01:24:26,800
That's what they're doing.

2024
01:24:26,800 --> 01:24:27,800
Yes.

2025
01:24:28,230 --> 01:24:30,570
We can try to go to certain sectors...

2026
01:24:30,770 --> 01:24:33,310
and get 2 scores instead of 3,

2027
01:24:33,540 --> 01:24:35,980
but nothing will change.

2028
01:24:36,880 --> 01:24:39,610
They made the game so boring.

2029
01:24:41,650 --> 01:24:44,020
We now need to... Seung Yong.

2030
01:24:46,220 --> 01:24:48,660
We'll just score minuscule points...

2031
01:24:48,790 --> 01:24:50,120
and go for the Deathmatch.

2032
01:24:51,460 --> 01:24:52,590
It's meaningless.

2033
01:24:54,030 --> 01:24:55,560
When Round Four ends,

2034
01:24:55,730 --> 01:24:57,560
it's impossible for us to win,

2035
01:24:57,560 --> 01:24:58,930
no matter how we calculate.

2036
01:24:59,300 --> 01:25:02,340
We couldn't identify
all the celestial objects until then.

2037
01:25:02,600 --> 01:25:04,100
We'll be splitting...

2038
01:25:04,100 --> 01:25:06,140
and sharing...

2039
01:25:06,140 --> 01:25:07,540
the small points.

2040
01:25:07,740 --> 01:25:09,540
"You score five points this time."

2041
01:25:09,540 --> 01:25:12,050
"I'll score 1. I'll score 3."

2042
01:25:12,610 --> 01:25:14,910
You take it.

2043
01:25:14,910 --> 01:25:15,980
Losers.

2044
01:25:30,830 --> 01:25:33,070
Sung Joo must've known yesterday.

2045
01:25:34,870 --> 01:25:37,370
- That was him distancing himself from us.
- What?

2046
01:25:37,540 --> 01:25:39,640
He was distancing himself from us.

2047
01:25:40,210 --> 01:25:42,080
We did have a talk yesterday.

2048
01:25:44,440 --> 01:25:46,510
I didn't know.

2049
01:25:47,780 --> 01:25:49,980
He suddenly moved his things out.

2050
01:25:50,880 --> 01:25:52,820
"Team P2 needs to sleep together."

2051
01:25:53,320 --> 01:25:55,520
I think that was also a lie.

2052
01:25:56,990 --> 01:25:58,490
All the puzzle pieces...

2053
01:25:59,330 --> 01:26:02,400
It feels like
Hye Seon's laugh is fake too.

2054
01:26:03,300 --> 01:26:06,170
Since when did they start to plot?

2055
01:26:06,330 --> 01:26:08,470
"Let's kill Seung Yong."

2056
01:26:08,940 --> 01:26:11,240
But they couldn't kill him
in the Mafia Game.

2057
01:26:11,370 --> 01:26:12,940
Because killing him would kill them too.

2058
01:26:13,670 --> 01:26:15,510
This is the real Killer Game.

2059
01:26:18,950 --> 01:26:21,080
I do want to find out...

2060
01:26:21,580 --> 01:26:25,550
who started the whole
"Seung Yong is the target" thing.

2061
01:26:25,920 --> 01:26:27,020
Who do you think?

2062
01:26:27,020 --> 01:26:29,090
I need to play the Deathmatch anyway.

2063
01:26:29,090 --> 01:26:30,190
So I want to pick that person.

2064
01:26:30,590 --> 01:26:31,860
Ji Min?

2065
01:26:32,860 --> 01:26:35,560
No. High chance it's Seong Beom.

2066
01:26:35,930 --> 01:26:39,200
Either Seong Beom or Ji Min?

2067
01:26:39,200 --> 01:26:40,870
In Round Five,

2068
01:26:41,330 --> 01:26:43,240
Project Galaxy was over for us.

2069
01:26:43,500 --> 01:26:46,240
We started the Mafia Game
to find out who had instigated this.

2070
01:26:46,640 --> 01:26:49,940
When we voted for the Deathmatch
yesterday...

2071
01:26:49,940 --> 01:26:51,010
- Yes.
- Yes.

2072
01:26:51,140 --> 01:26:53,110
We merely discussed among ourselves,

2073
01:26:53,110 --> 01:26:56,480
but since you're
technically our team leader,

2074
01:26:56,480 --> 01:26:57,750
you became the target.

2075
01:26:59,790 --> 01:27:01,420
- To eliminate me?
- What?

2076
01:27:01,420 --> 01:27:02,590
To eliminate me?

2077
01:27:02,890 --> 01:27:04,190
Well, you know...

2078
01:27:04,420 --> 01:27:06,130
- Should I be honest?
- Yes.

2079
01:27:06,130 --> 01:27:07,360
I won't beat around the bush.

2080
01:27:07,360 --> 01:27:08,560
They don't like you.

2081
01:27:08,700 --> 01:27:10,230
- Who? Seong Beom?
- I don't know.

2082
01:27:10,860 --> 01:27:12,770
Someone among them.

2083
01:27:13,400 --> 01:27:14,400
They just don't like you.

2084
01:27:14,630 --> 01:27:16,340
They talked about the narrative whatnot,

2085
01:27:16,340 --> 01:27:18,270
so I told them to quit the nonsense.

2086
01:27:19,140 --> 01:27:20,940
What kind of narrative
are you talking about?

2087
01:27:21,110 --> 01:27:22,480
They go,

2088
01:27:22,480 --> 01:27:24,610
"It's just a game, no hard feelings."

2089
01:27:25,110 --> 01:27:26,550
"This was today. Tomorrow we start anew."

2090
01:27:26,550 --> 01:27:29,250
They say all that,
but after so many games,

2091
01:27:29,520 --> 01:27:32,490
they're talking about the Heist Day.
That's nonsense.

2092
01:27:32,650 --> 01:27:35,320
(YunB had told him about
how they were using the Heist Day...)

2093
01:27:35,320 --> 01:27:37,890
(to come together.)

2094
01:27:38,060 --> 01:27:40,830
Seung Yong now has a giant target
on his back.

2095
01:27:40,830 --> 01:27:42,530
There's nothing we can do about it.

2096
01:27:42,530 --> 01:27:44,660
Until yesterday,

2097
01:27:44,660 --> 01:27:46,570
when someone did something in the game,

2098
01:27:46,570 --> 01:27:48,200
they said, "It's just a game."

2099
01:27:48,370 --> 01:27:50,440
"It was a game, so it's fine."

2100
01:27:50,440 --> 01:27:52,710
But now, because they want to survive,

2101
01:27:52,770 --> 01:27:54,340
they came up with a pretext.

2102
01:27:54,340 --> 01:27:55,680
They're liars.

2103
01:27:55,840 --> 01:27:59,750
They're purely a group of liars.

2104
01:28:00,650 --> 01:28:03,150
I rarely get angry.

2105
01:28:03,450 --> 01:28:06,690
But I get angry when someone does
something really below the belt.

2106
01:28:20,030 --> 01:28:22,240
Can I just check one thing?

2107
01:28:22,870 --> 01:28:26,470
Two of us will be playing the Deathmatch.

2108
01:28:27,070 --> 01:28:31,210
Whoever first suggested...

2109
01:28:31,210 --> 01:28:32,480
to kill Seung Yong,

2110
01:28:32,480 --> 01:28:35,080
why don't you proudly go
to the Deathmatch with us?

2111
01:28:36,120 --> 01:28:38,180
Don't hide behind the group.

2112
01:28:38,690 --> 01:28:40,890
Someone must've suggested it first.

2113
01:28:41,920 --> 01:28:44,920
The person who suggested
to kill Shin Seung Yong.

2114
01:28:48,860 --> 01:28:50,400
I just wanted to hear it.

2115
01:28:50,400 --> 01:28:53,130
"I said it,
and I suggested to kill him..."

2116
01:28:53,330 --> 01:28:54,570
"because I didn't like Seung Yong."

2117
01:28:54,570 --> 01:28:56,970
Just one sentence,
and everything can be resolved.

2118
01:28:57,370 --> 01:28:59,770
I'm offering to make you a ring,
so why won't you fight?

2119
01:29:01,740 --> 01:29:03,310
- It's me.
- Don't be... Sorry?

2120
01:29:03,310 --> 01:29:04,510
- It's me.
- Let's go, then.

2121
01:29:04,510 --> 01:29:05,650
Let's go. I'll play.

2122
01:29:05,750 --> 01:29:06,910
- Okay.
- Yes.

2123
01:29:07,010 --> 01:29:08,180
Keun Woo.

2124
01:29:08,920 --> 01:29:10,950
You keep hiding,

2125
01:29:10,950 --> 01:29:12,950
and there's nothing fun about it.

2126
01:29:13,450 --> 01:29:15,420
- It's me.
- We never hid it to begin with.

2127
01:29:15,420 --> 01:29:17,190
I heard that this group was formed...

2128
01:29:17,190 --> 01:29:19,760
because someone had suggested it.

2129
01:29:20,730 --> 01:29:22,730
You've played it out nicely...

2130
01:29:22,730 --> 01:29:23,730
and killed him off.

2131
01:29:23,730 --> 01:29:26,300
- Why don't you fight head-on, man to man?
- Sure. I'll go.

2132
01:29:27,200 --> 01:29:28,300
- Then you, Keun Woo?
- Yes.

2133
01:29:28,300 --> 01:29:29,540
- Okay.
- Okay.

2134
01:29:34,610 --> 01:29:36,910
Let's do this.
When we go to the Deathmatch,

2135
01:29:36,910 --> 01:29:39,850
let's bring with us the guy
who suggested...

2136
01:29:39,850 --> 01:29:40,880
targeting Seung Yong.

2137
01:29:41,050 --> 01:29:42,050
And who is that?

2138
01:29:42,180 --> 01:29:43,550
I'm going to find that now.

2139
01:29:44,520 --> 01:29:45,590
You'll find...

2140
01:29:45,590 --> 01:29:47,350
Keun Woo played a big role.

2141
01:29:47,450 --> 01:29:50,790
Thanks to that, I became certain...

2142
01:29:50,790 --> 01:29:53,330
that Ji Min had planned this.

2143
01:29:58,030 --> 01:30:00,070
You won't go. Don't worry.

2144
01:30:03,070 --> 01:30:04,770
They just need to pick...

2145
01:30:04,770 --> 01:30:06,070
who they want.

2146
01:30:06,070 --> 01:30:07,210
But the fact...

2147
01:30:07,270 --> 01:30:09,110
they were trying to deduce it...

2148
01:30:09,110 --> 01:30:10,940
I just couldn't understand.

2149
01:30:11,210 --> 01:30:13,450
Who suggested killing Seung Yong?

2150
01:30:14,780 --> 01:30:15,920
What will they do if they find out?

2151
01:30:16,920 --> 01:30:18,450
What will they do if we say it's Jin Ho?

2152
01:30:18,450 --> 01:30:19,490
Exactly.

2153
01:30:19,490 --> 01:30:21,220
Let's see if they'll do the same
to stronger players.

2154
01:30:21,620 --> 01:30:24,190
They think Seung Yong is the common enemy.

2155
01:30:24,190 --> 01:30:25,790
He's not even a common enemy.

2156
01:30:25,790 --> 01:30:27,090
It's just karma.

2157
01:30:27,090 --> 01:30:29,100
He should just accept
that the time has come.

2158
01:30:29,100 --> 01:30:30,830
They don't understand that.

2159
01:30:30,830 --> 01:30:32,130
They just think...

2160
01:30:32,270 --> 01:30:35,230
we didn't play fair today...

2161
01:30:35,230 --> 01:30:37,400
- and rounded up on him to kill him.
- What exactly is fair play?

2162
01:30:37,640 --> 01:30:39,640
Did we make a mistake? No, they made it.

2163
01:30:40,110 --> 01:30:41,940
They just don't understand it.

2164
01:30:42,140 --> 01:30:43,840
I didn't get them from the start.

2165
01:30:44,180 --> 01:30:46,180
"We're the minority."

2166
01:30:46,180 --> 01:30:48,110
"We can't play this game well."

2167
01:30:48,110 --> 01:30:49,580
They put on a grumpy face...

2168
01:30:49,580 --> 01:30:51,850
from the start until the end.

2169
01:30:51,850 --> 01:30:53,920
"I won't play.
It's so disadvantageous for us."

2170
01:30:54,050 --> 01:30:56,020
Then go home.

2171
01:30:56,190 --> 01:30:57,760
Why are you still here?

2172
01:30:58,090 --> 01:30:59,190
But I thought, "Who knows?"

2173
01:30:59,560 --> 01:31:01,530
"They could've come up..."

2174
01:31:01,530 --> 01:31:03,660
"with a jaw-dropping plan."

2175
01:31:03,660 --> 01:31:05,900
I told myself...

2176
01:31:05,900 --> 01:31:08,600
I'd secure a perfect win.

2177
01:31:09,040 --> 01:31:10,040
Let's go line up.

2178
01:31:10,040 --> 01:31:11,840
Remember your sectors?

2179
01:31:18,140 --> 01:31:20,480
Let's discuss where to relocate to.

2180
01:31:25,050 --> 01:31:27,890
I'll use one and go to Sector 14.

2181
01:31:28,590 --> 01:31:31,220
Then I'll go to Sector Ten.

2182
01:31:32,530 --> 01:31:34,230
You're going to Sector Ten?

2183
01:31:36,230 --> 01:31:37,300
Then...

2184
01:31:38,400 --> 01:31:39,500
I'll go to Sector Nine.

2185
01:31:40,630 --> 01:31:41,670
Let's line up.

2186
01:31:42,370 --> 01:31:43,370
Let's go.

2187
01:31:44,240 --> 01:31:45,840
Isn't it better to go together?

2188
01:31:45,840 --> 01:31:48,980
(Minority Alliance splits up
and goes to Sectors 9 and 10.)

2189
01:31:49,840 --> 01:31:51,640
If we can't find it, that's that.

2190
01:31:55,310 --> 01:31:56,850
How may I help you?

2191
01:31:57,020 --> 01:31:58,890
I'll move to Sector Ten.

2192
01:31:58,890 --> 01:31:59,890
(Shin Seung Yong relocates to Sector 10,
which is either the star or cosmic dust.)

2193
01:31:59,890 --> 01:32:01,050
I'll move to Sector Nine.

2194
01:32:01,050 --> 01:32:02,520
(Kang Ji Hoo relocates to Sector 9,
which is either the star or cosmic dust.)

2195
01:32:02,860 --> 01:32:05,460
I'll move to Sector 14.

2196
01:32:05,460 --> 01:32:06,460
(Kwak Beom relocates to Sector 14.)

2197
01:32:06,460 --> 01:32:09,600
- You've been relocated to Sector 14.
- Okay.

2198
01:32:09,600 --> 01:32:11,160
(The 3 players of Minority Alliance
have relocated.)

2199
01:32:12,060 --> 01:32:13,700
How may I help you?

2200
01:32:13,770 --> 01:32:15,700
I'll relocate.

2201
01:32:16,000 --> 01:32:17,970
I'll move from Sector 6 to Sector 9.

2202
01:32:18,440 --> 01:32:20,870
I'll move to Sector Nine.

2203
01:32:21,110 --> 01:32:22,110
Sector Nine.

2204
01:32:22,110 --> 01:32:23,110
(They move to the sector with the star.)

2205
01:32:23,110 --> 01:32:24,180
Sector Nine.

2206
01:32:25,140 --> 01:32:28,010
Choi Hye Seon,
which sector would you like to move to?

2207
01:32:28,080 --> 01:32:29,420
I'll move to Sector Eight.

2208
01:32:29,650 --> 01:32:33,190
I'll move to Sector Eight.

2209
01:32:33,750 --> 01:32:35,050
I'll move to Sector 12.

2210
01:32:35,050 --> 01:32:36,490
(Jin Ho relocates to defend the comets.)

2211
01:32:36,490 --> 01:32:38,160
(Sector relocation: Sector 9 to Sector 12)

2212
01:32:38,960 --> 01:32:41,030
Round Five has ended.

2213
01:32:47,670 --> 01:32:50,300
Keun Woo, you volunteered...

2214
01:32:50,300 --> 01:32:52,240
- for the Deathmatch just now.
- Yes.

2215
01:32:52,340 --> 01:32:55,610
- I wasn't here for the Heist Day.
- Right.

2216
01:32:55,610 --> 01:32:57,980
This whole alliance is built...

2217
01:32:57,980 --> 01:33:00,380
on pretexts.

2218
01:33:00,550 --> 01:33:03,050
The fact I wasn't here on the Heist Day...

2219
01:33:03,250 --> 01:33:04,350
worked out very well for me.

2220
01:33:04,350 --> 01:33:05,990
They can't blame me.

2221
01:33:06,620 --> 01:33:08,990
They have no pretext to pick me...

2222
01:33:08,990 --> 01:33:10,260
for the Deathmatch.

2223
01:33:10,260 --> 01:33:13,230
I'm in a position
where I could control them,

2224
01:33:13,230 --> 01:33:15,230
which is fascinating.

2225
01:33:15,230 --> 01:33:17,230
Everything falls into place.

2226
01:33:17,500 --> 01:33:20,600
Regarding this situation,

2227
01:33:20,600 --> 01:33:22,870
those who brought the people together...

2228
01:33:22,870 --> 01:33:24,600
using Seung Yong as the common enemy...

2229
01:33:24,600 --> 01:33:27,210
were Seung Beom, Ji Min,

2230
01:33:27,210 --> 01:33:28,510
and Hye Seon.

2231
01:33:28,770 --> 01:33:30,480
When they were forced...

2232
01:33:30,480 --> 01:33:32,550
to ally with that team as citizens,

2233
01:33:32,550 --> 01:33:35,750
those who had the most conflict
and got most hurt...

2234
01:33:35,750 --> 01:33:38,020
were Seong Beom and Hye Seon as well.

2235
01:33:38,720 --> 01:33:41,990
(The voting situation the day before)

2236
01:33:41,990 --> 01:33:45,860
(Seong Beom and Hye Seon didn't agree
with the others in the winning team.)

2237
01:33:45,860 --> 01:33:49,760
(Seong Beom and Hye Seon didn't agree
with the others in the winning team.)

2238
01:33:50,360 --> 01:33:51,730
- What do you mean?
- We're also part of the winning team,

2239
01:33:51,730 --> 01:33:53,170
but they won't even include us
in their conversation.

2240
01:33:53,600 --> 01:33:55,940
Going by the pretexts,

2241
01:33:56,440 --> 01:33:59,570
Seong Beom, Hye Seon, and Ji Min are
on top of the list.

2242
01:34:00,040 --> 01:34:02,440
- That's also true.
- Yes.

2243
01:34:02,440 --> 01:34:05,880
But we can't...

2244
01:34:05,880 --> 01:34:08,210
- encourage them.
- We can't force them.

2245
01:34:08,210 --> 01:34:12,250
In that case, the first place...
There are Seong Beom, Ji Min,

2246
01:34:12,250 --> 01:34:15,250
and Hye Seon. The three victims.

2247
01:34:15,490 --> 01:34:18,490
If any of them don't win first place,

2248
01:34:18,720 --> 01:34:19,730
we have two remaining.

2249
01:34:19,730 --> 01:34:24,000
I think it gives them a better pretext...

2250
01:34:24,000 --> 01:34:26,230
- if 1 of the 2 plays the Deathmatch.
- Well, that team will decide.

2251
01:34:26,230 --> 01:34:29,370
- That's right.
- They'd think similarly.

2252
01:34:29,700 --> 01:34:30,800
If they're going to purge,

2253
01:34:30,800 --> 01:34:32,410
it'll be best for Ji Min or Seong Beom...

2254
01:34:32,410 --> 01:34:34,010
to chop Seung Yong's head off themselves.

2255
01:34:34,310 --> 01:34:36,880
When it comes to Bloody Game,

2256
01:34:37,540 --> 01:34:39,780
my priority is to survive...

2257
01:34:39,780 --> 01:34:41,710
no matter what method I need to use.

2258
01:34:41,850 --> 01:34:44,250
Halfway through,
I started to gaslight them...

2259
01:34:44,250 --> 01:34:46,090
about the importance of pretexts.

2260
01:34:48,220 --> 01:34:51,420
Before Round Six starts,
the hidden item will get revealed now.

2261
01:34:52,360 --> 01:34:54,830
The hidden item of Project Galaxy is...

2262
01:34:54,830 --> 01:34:56,230
(Black Hole Immunity: Defend once
against the effects of the black hole)

2263
01:34:56,230 --> 01:34:58,030
Black Hole Immunity.

2264
01:34:58,500 --> 01:34:59,900
Black Hole Immunity...

2265
01:34:59,900 --> 01:35:02,740
gives you the ability
to become immune to the black hole.

2266
01:35:02,740 --> 01:35:05,040
The user's score will not be reversed...

2267
01:35:05,040 --> 01:35:07,010
even if they are affected
by the black hole.

2268
01:35:07,770 --> 01:35:10,080
Once purchased,
it will be automatically used...

2269
01:35:10,240 --> 01:35:12,410
when you get affected by the black hole.

2270
01:35:12,810 --> 01:35:16,050
You can purchase it in the Voting Room
starting now,

2271
01:35:16,250 --> 01:35:18,980
and the number of available stock is one.

2272
01:35:20,520 --> 01:35:21,590
Buy it.

2273
01:35:22,150 --> 01:35:23,290
You understood, right?

2274
01:35:31,800 --> 01:35:33,570
How may I help you?

2275
01:35:37,170 --> 01:35:40,070
I think Ji Hoo bought Black Hole Immunity.

2276
01:35:40,710 --> 01:35:42,780
They might pretend to support Ji Hoo...

2277
01:35:42,780 --> 01:35:44,240
and bomb us with the black hole.

2278
01:35:44,580 --> 01:35:46,610
They could send Ji Hoo
with Black Hole Immunity...

2279
01:35:46,610 --> 01:35:47,980
to the star...

2280
01:35:48,310 --> 01:35:50,020
and send the black hole
to the star as well.

2281
01:35:50,480 --> 01:35:52,820
The hidden item was Black Hole Immunity.

2282
01:35:53,190 --> 01:35:56,490
You might think it's nothing much,
but when you think about it,

2283
01:35:56,660 --> 01:35:59,290
the moment five points from the star...

2284
01:35:59,290 --> 01:36:01,060
turns into minus five,

2285
01:36:01,130 --> 01:36:02,930
the score gap decreases by ten points.

2286
01:36:03,330 --> 01:36:05,600
This is huge.

2287
01:36:05,600 --> 01:36:07,200
I started to get worried then.

2288
01:36:08,970 --> 01:36:10,370
How may I help you?

2289
01:36:10,370 --> 01:36:11,800
I'll buy the hidden item.

2290
01:36:11,800 --> 01:36:14,870
Heo Seong Beom,
will you purchase Black Hole Immunity?

2291
01:36:14,940 --> 01:36:16,510
Was that a question?

2292
01:36:16,510 --> 01:36:17,580
Yes, it was.

2293
01:36:17,580 --> 01:36:19,110
I entered the Voting Room,

2294
01:36:19,110 --> 01:36:20,810
and the item was left for me to purchase.

2295
01:36:21,550 --> 01:36:23,720
"What's happening?
Why didn't they buy it?"

2296
01:36:23,920 --> 01:36:25,250
I thought...

2297
01:36:25,250 --> 01:36:27,850
they'd definitely buy the item.

2298
01:36:28,020 --> 01:36:30,160
(5 minutes ago)

2299
01:36:30,160 --> 01:36:31,620
How may I help you?

2300
01:36:33,190 --> 01:36:34,530
Nothing.

2301
01:36:34,890 --> 01:36:36,960
To bide my time, to get my revenge,

2302
01:36:36,960 --> 01:36:39,100
I decided to save my money.

2303
01:36:39,100 --> 01:36:41,430
We wanted to trick them to show them...

2304
01:36:41,430 --> 01:36:44,200
that we haven't completely given up.

2305
01:36:46,170 --> 01:36:47,240
I'll buy it.

2306
01:36:47,240 --> 01:36:48,240
(Heo Seong Beom purchases
Black Hole Immunity.)

2307
01:36:48,240 --> 01:36:51,240
Heo Seong Beom, 20,000 dollars
will be deducted from your funds.

2308
01:36:51,240 --> 01:36:52,950
When you're affected by the black hole,

2309
01:36:52,950 --> 01:36:54,750
it will automatically activate once.

2310
01:36:54,980 --> 01:36:56,450
To prevent the opponents from buying it...

2311
01:36:56,450 --> 01:36:58,950
and making an irregular move,

2312
01:36:58,950 --> 01:37:00,220
I decided to buy it myself.

2313
01:37:00,550 --> 01:37:02,960
I'll buy it
and take away their opportunity.

2314
01:37:04,220 --> 01:37:06,860
Here are the results of the last round.

2315
01:37:07,560 --> 01:37:10,630
(Points earned in Round 5)

2316
01:37:10,630 --> 01:37:14,170
Round 6 will now begin
and run for 30 minutes.

2317
01:37:15,500 --> 01:37:18,040
I think F found the star, right?

2318
01:37:18,040 --> 01:37:19,070
(F earned 5 points.)

2319
01:37:19,070 --> 01:37:22,210
(F is Kang Ji Hoo.)

2320
01:37:22,210 --> 01:37:24,440
In Round Five, we found out...

2321
01:37:24,440 --> 01:37:26,410
Sectors 9 and 10 were
cosmic dust and a star.

2322
01:37:26,410 --> 01:37:28,250
Seung Yong and I went...

2323
01:37:28,250 --> 01:37:29,880
to explore one each.

2324
01:37:29,880 --> 01:37:32,890
After Round Five ended,
I scored five points.

2325
01:37:33,220 --> 01:37:35,820
I could immediately identify Sector Nine
as the star.

2326
01:37:37,060 --> 01:37:39,390
One of them would be in last place.

2327
01:37:39,390 --> 01:37:40,430
(Beom, Seung Yong, Ji Hoo)

2328
01:37:40,430 --> 01:37:41,430
That's right.

2329
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:46,830
We've come a long way.

2330
01:37:47,170 --> 01:37:48,530
Yes, we did come a long way.

2331
01:37:48,530 --> 01:37:51,000
We started
from the outdoor survival grounds.

2332
01:37:51,000 --> 01:37:52,100
We've never met before.

2333
01:37:52,810 --> 01:37:53,910
That's right.

2334
01:38:00,950 --> 01:38:03,620
Ji Hoo is so reliable.
I'm glad he's with us.

2335
01:38:04,650 --> 01:38:07,220
(Nodding)

2336
01:38:07,220 --> 01:38:09,560
He's the best ally I found.

2337
01:38:10,460 --> 01:38:11,460
I agree.

2338
01:38:11,820 --> 01:38:14,060
We grew fond of him.

2339
01:38:14,060 --> 01:38:16,100
Ji Hoo is very smart,

2340
01:38:16,100 --> 01:38:18,300
so we could rely on him
when playing games.

2341
01:38:18,660 --> 01:38:19,870
That was when I decided.

2342
01:38:22,300 --> 01:38:23,540
Seung Yong, come here.

2343
01:38:25,070 --> 01:38:26,670
Let's save Ji Hoo.

2344
01:38:27,670 --> 01:38:28,940
- What?
- Let's save Ji Hoo.

2345
01:38:31,040 --> 01:38:32,750
Okay.

2346
01:38:32,950 --> 01:38:35,810
Ji Hoo wasn't even on my team.

2347
01:38:35,810 --> 01:38:38,980
But because he was seen around me,

2348
01:38:39,180 --> 01:38:41,490
he automatically got placed
in Minority Alliance.

2349
01:38:41,490 --> 01:38:45,190
So we decided to save Ji Hoo.

2350
01:38:45,790 --> 01:38:48,630
Our score difference is only one.

2351
01:38:48,960 --> 01:38:51,700
We could enter a satellite together.

2352
01:38:52,200 --> 01:38:54,300
I'll move to Sector Six.

2353
01:38:54,930 --> 01:38:56,400
I'll move to Sector Six.

2354
01:38:56,400 --> 01:38:57,770
(Sector relocation: Sector 9 to Sector 6)

2355
01:38:57,770 --> 01:39:00,870
(Shin Seung Yong and Kang Ji Hoo
moved to the same sector.)

2356
01:39:00,870 --> 01:39:02,470
You have submitted two coins.

2357
01:39:02,940 --> 01:39:05,440
How about this?
I hand over the black hole.

2358
01:39:05,540 --> 01:39:06,610
Okay.

2359
01:39:08,480 --> 01:39:10,220
- And send it there.
- What?

2360
01:39:11,050 --> 01:39:12,150
There.

2361
01:39:14,690 --> 01:39:16,060
- That's not so bad.
- We can defend,

2362
01:39:16,320 --> 01:39:17,560
- Not bad.
- and we can send Ji Hoo off.

2363
01:39:19,390 --> 01:39:20,690
I'll see you later, then.

2364
01:39:28,500 --> 01:39:29,970
How may I help you?

2365
01:39:29,970 --> 01:39:31,300
You see,

2366
01:39:31,300 --> 01:39:33,970
I'll try and move the black hole.

2367
01:39:35,240 --> 01:39:38,910
Yes. And I'm going to bet...

2368
01:39:46,120 --> 01:39:48,490
(Stopping)

2369
01:40:03,200 --> 01:40:04,240
One second.

2370
01:40:04,870 --> 01:40:07,610
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

2371
01:40:07,610 --> 01:40:09,540
I'm so stupid.

2372
01:40:10,610 --> 01:40:12,210
I thought I had more coins.

2373
01:40:14,250 --> 01:40:16,220
I was so stupid.

2374
01:40:18,580 --> 01:40:19,720
I apologize.

2375
01:40:21,750 --> 01:40:22,760
Here.

2376
01:40:24,790 --> 01:40:27,030
Please state the number of coins
you'd like to bet.

2377
01:40:31,460 --> 01:40:35,770
(Seong Beom counts the number of spaces.)

2378
01:40:38,100 --> 01:40:39,370
I spent quite a while in there.

2379
01:40:39,370 --> 01:40:41,140
That's all right. I just got here.

2380
01:40:48,550 --> 01:40:50,420
One thing I've learned
on Bloody Game X was...

2381
01:40:50,420 --> 01:40:52,790
that the honest one always loses.

2382
01:41:00,490 --> 01:41:03,030
I think Beom just bet on the black hole.

2383
01:41:03,300 --> 01:41:05,430
- This time?
- I heard him counting his coins.

2384
01:41:05,930 --> 01:41:08,470
I think he spent 8 or 10 coins.

2385
01:41:08,700 --> 01:41:11,340
I think he sent it
to where the star blows up.

2386
01:41:11,340 --> 01:41:12,370
- In this round?
- Yes.

2387
01:41:12,370 --> 01:41:13,370
(Black hole)

2388
01:41:13,370 --> 01:41:15,340
The black hole is in Sector Nine.

2389
01:41:16,010 --> 01:41:18,010
I'm betting on Sector Nine.

2390
01:41:18,010 --> 01:41:20,310
You've bet on the black hole
moving ten spaces.

2391
01:41:20,510 --> 01:41:22,750
- Yes.
- That means we can spend...

2392
01:41:22,750 --> 01:41:24,420
just over 10 or 11.

2393
01:41:24,550 --> 01:41:26,190
- We need 12.
- Okay.

2394
01:41:27,650 --> 01:41:29,820
I decided to keep the opposing team...

2395
01:41:29,820 --> 01:41:31,920
in check for sure.

2396
01:41:32,120 --> 01:41:33,790
How may I help you?

2397
01:41:34,030 --> 01:41:35,490
I'll bet on the black hole.

2398
01:41:35,690 --> 01:41:37,700
Please state the number of coins
you'd like to bet.

2399
01:41:37,800 --> 01:41:39,160
Twelve.

2400
01:41:40,300 --> 01:41:41,870
(Black hole, 12 coins)

2401
01:41:41,870 --> 01:41:44,140
(Seong Beom spent 12 coins
to bet the black hole in Sector 11.)

2402
01:41:44,140 --> 01:41:45,670
It moves to Sector 11.

2403
01:41:47,740 --> 01:41:50,740
Once we get through this part,
the game's over.

2404
01:41:50,740 --> 01:41:52,580
- Yes, it is.
- Yes.

2405
01:41:52,810 --> 01:41:54,350
(Star: YunB, Hye Seon, Jin Ho)

2406
01:41:54,350 --> 01:41:55,780
(Comet: Ji Min,
Planet: Sung Joo, Seong Beom, Keun Woo)

2407
01:41:56,480 --> 01:41:58,380
Round Six has ended.

2408
01:41:58,380 --> 01:42:00,420
(Round 6 has ended.)

2409
01:42:01,690 --> 01:42:04,160
Here are the results of the last round.

2410
01:42:06,120 --> 01:42:07,190
Please.

2411
01:42:10,300 --> 01:42:11,360
What?

2412
01:42:20,310 --> 01:42:21,870
(Points earned in Round 6)

2413
01:42:21,870 --> 01:42:24,440
(Jin Ho, B, YunB, Keun Woo, Hye Seon,
Ji Hoo, Seung Yong, Beom, I, Seong Beom)

2414
01:42:24,440 --> 01:42:26,040
(Except for Ji Min,
who moved to Sector 14,)

2415
01:42:26,040 --> 01:42:28,150
(and Seong Beom,
whose Black Hole Immunity was activated,)

2416
01:42:28,150 --> 01:42:33,120
(all members of the Majority Alliance
lost points.)

2417
01:42:33,450 --> 01:42:37,060
Round 7 will now begin
and run for 30 minutes.

2418
01:42:44,700 --> 01:42:45,860
That's good.

2419
01:42:46,060 --> 01:42:47,670
Great. That was cool.

2420
01:42:50,240 --> 01:42:53,040
I couldn't believe they pulled it off.

2421
01:42:53,440 --> 01:42:54,670
It actually worked.

2422
01:42:56,640 --> 01:42:58,380
I went in to sacrifice myself.

2423
01:43:01,510 --> 01:43:03,480
Please state the number of coins
you'd like to bet.

2424
01:43:03,480 --> 01:43:05,420
(He bet 15 coins...)

2425
01:43:05,420 --> 01:43:09,050
(on the black hole.)

2426
01:43:09,320 --> 01:43:12,220
(Seong Beom miscounted the coins.)

2427
01:43:15,690 --> 01:43:18,230
They still have to compete
for first place,

2428
01:43:18,230 --> 01:43:19,530
so we'll have to keep an eye on them.

2429
01:43:20,200 --> 01:43:21,300
One of them...

2430
01:43:21,370 --> 01:43:23,170
might betray them out of nowhere.

2431
01:43:24,070 --> 01:43:26,540
I wasn't trying to win.

2432
01:43:26,540 --> 01:43:28,540
I wanted to start an internal conflict.

2433
01:43:28,770 --> 01:43:31,910
The scores will be different
from their plan,

2434
01:43:32,110 --> 01:43:35,510
and one of them will want more points
and betray them.

2435
01:43:35,510 --> 01:43:39,450
(Ji Min is now the sole leader.)

2436
01:43:39,450 --> 01:43:43,790
(Sung Joo was tied for 1st place,
and now he's 3rd.)

2437
01:43:43,890 --> 01:43:47,060
I was naturally headed toward first place.

2438
01:43:47,490 --> 01:43:48,990
I thought, "I won."

2439
01:43:49,390 --> 01:43:50,700
I was tied for first place,

2440
01:43:50,700 --> 01:43:53,130
and I got incredibly unlucky.

2441
01:43:53,630 --> 01:43:54,970
That one...

2442
01:43:55,700 --> 01:43:57,700
might have been a naive judgment.

2443
01:43:57,770 --> 01:43:59,670
While spending 12 coins
to move the black hole,

2444
01:43:59,670 --> 01:44:02,510
I doubted they spent more than that.

2445
01:44:02,510 --> 01:44:04,310
But they did, in fact.

2446
01:44:05,340 --> 01:44:07,610
Round Six's results were announced.

2447
01:44:07,780 --> 01:44:11,150
Ji Hoo and Jin Ho's scores were...

2448
01:44:11,150 --> 01:44:12,520
only seven points apart.

2449
01:44:12,520 --> 01:44:15,590
So, I realized we were in a crisis.

2450
01:44:16,050 --> 01:44:18,920
The things we were worried about
did happen.

2451
01:44:19,020 --> 01:44:21,730
I had to play three times harder
from then on.

2452
01:44:24,100 --> 01:44:25,630
I went in to sacrifice myself.

2453
01:44:26,700 --> 01:44:28,800
Why would you follow me?

2454
01:44:29,030 --> 01:44:30,170
It's dangerous.

2455
01:44:32,140 --> 01:44:33,440
Those guys are so weird.

2456
01:44:34,470 --> 01:44:37,740
And I'll relocate to Sector Nine.

2457
01:44:37,740 --> 01:44:38,780
(He moved to Sector 9
where the black hole was.)

2458
01:44:38,780 --> 01:44:40,950
You have relocated to Sector Nine.

2459
01:44:40,950 --> 01:44:43,220
There was only one score
you could actually control.

2460
01:44:43,350 --> 01:44:44,480
Going down the ranks.

2461
01:44:45,120 --> 01:44:47,890
It's hard to climb up,
but it's easy to go down.

2462
01:44:49,220 --> 01:44:50,890
Who are you going to pick?

2463
01:44:53,890 --> 01:44:57,300
Let's say you and I are going
to the Deathmatch.

2464
01:44:57,700 --> 01:44:58,830
- Yes.
- And they have...

2465
01:44:58,830 --> 01:45:00,970
- an elimination immunity pass.
- Yes.

2466
01:45:00,970 --> 01:45:03,340
I think they'll give it to the one
who we might choose.

2467
01:45:03,540 --> 01:45:05,070
- Yes.
- They'll give them one.

2468
01:45:06,370 --> 01:45:09,110
I doubt they'll give it to Seong Beom.

2469
01:45:09,440 --> 01:45:11,080
Why? Because he's in first place?

2470
01:45:11,410 --> 01:45:13,050
No, because they think...

2471
01:45:13,050 --> 01:45:14,550
he'll win the Deathmatch.

2472
01:45:14,550 --> 01:45:16,110
I think they'll give it to Ji Min.

2473
01:45:18,320 --> 01:45:19,380
What should we do?

2474
01:45:19,750 --> 01:45:21,720
Who are your top three picks?

2475
01:45:24,160 --> 01:45:25,220
Me?

2476
01:45:25,860 --> 01:45:29,130
Seong Beom, Ji Min, and Sung Joo.

2477
01:45:33,130 --> 01:45:34,130
My list is pretty similar.

2478
01:45:34,130 --> 01:45:36,370
We'll see who gets the pass
and who places first.

2479
01:45:36,870 --> 01:45:40,140
Seong Beom might place first,

2480
01:45:40,140 --> 01:45:42,510
- and Ji Min might get the pass.
- Yes.

2481
01:45:42,510 --> 01:45:44,580
Then, we'll need to pick one more
other than Sung Joo.

2482
01:45:45,710 --> 01:45:46,780
Your fourth pick.

2483
01:45:46,880 --> 01:45:49,080
- Sung Joo and Jin Ho.
- Jin Ho?

2484
01:45:49,850 --> 01:45:50,920
Who else is there?

2485
01:45:52,820 --> 01:45:54,250
Sung Joo, let's at least have a talk.

2486
01:45:54,250 --> 01:45:56,150
It's like you're trying
to cut ties with us.

2487
01:45:56,150 --> 01:45:57,760
You're not going to talk to us at all?

2488
01:45:58,360 --> 01:46:00,390
Were you promised an immunity pass?

2489
01:46:00,860 --> 01:46:01,930
No.

2490
01:46:02,590 --> 01:46:04,100
Wasn't that the reason you joined them?

2491
01:46:04,600 --> 01:46:08,170
I was going to ask at first,
but I decided not to.

2492
01:46:09,200 --> 01:46:10,370
I knew they wouldn't say yes.

2493
01:46:10,640 --> 01:46:12,570
- Then, why did you join them?
- Why did you leave?

2494
01:46:13,410 --> 01:46:14,810
- I just...
- We're going to take you down with us.

2495
01:46:15,240 --> 01:46:16,240
You wanted to win?

2496
01:46:17,240 --> 01:46:19,240
You're lying, right?

2497
01:46:19,240 --> 01:46:20,350
Are you being for real?

2498
01:46:20,680 --> 01:46:22,210
- Of course, we are.
- Of course.

2499
01:46:22,210 --> 01:46:23,220
Who's the other one?

2500
01:46:24,050 --> 01:46:26,050
You're our only target.

2501
01:46:26,050 --> 01:46:27,390
They'll ask you to pick two.
You'll only pick me...

2502
01:46:27,390 --> 01:46:28,620
- so that they can't vote?
- Yes.

2503
01:46:29,350 --> 01:46:31,120
Just tell us...

2504
01:46:31,120 --> 01:46:32,190
if they're trying to put Ji Min
in the first place.

2505
01:46:32,190 --> 01:46:33,560
All the other information...

2506
01:46:34,560 --> 01:46:36,290
- The two of us will surely place last.
- Yes.

2507
01:46:36,530 --> 01:46:38,700
- The least you can do is tell us that.
- Well...

2508
01:46:39,030 --> 01:46:41,030
We had an agreement,
so I won't be doing that.

2509
01:46:41,930 --> 01:46:43,030
- But...
- What was the agreement?

2510
01:46:43,030 --> 01:46:44,640
Just tell us that.

2511
01:46:45,000 --> 01:46:46,400
We haven't decided on anything yet.

2512
01:46:46,740 --> 01:46:49,310
We won't pick you if you tell us that.

2513
01:46:49,980 --> 01:46:51,140
What do you say?

2514
01:46:52,310 --> 01:46:53,350
Who do they want to put in first place?

2515
01:46:53,350 --> 01:46:55,110
Yes, their plan.

2516
01:46:55,110 --> 01:46:57,320
We know we're going to lose.

2517
01:46:57,320 --> 01:46:59,550
I'll need to see how it goes.
They haven't decided on it yet.

2518
01:47:00,650 --> 01:47:01,850
They haven't?

2519
01:47:02,520 --> 01:47:03,760
If...

2520
01:47:03,960 --> 01:47:07,190
this offer works for you,

2521
01:47:07,930 --> 01:47:09,160
feel free to tell us.

2522
01:47:09,390 --> 01:47:10,530
No.

2523
01:47:18,070 --> 01:47:22,540
(Wandering around)

2524
01:47:22,540 --> 01:47:25,010
(Round 7, total score)

2525
01:47:25,010 --> 01:47:27,710
(Jin Ho, Ji Min, YunB,
Keun Woo, Hye Seon,)

2526
01:47:27,710 --> 01:47:30,480
(Ji Hoo, Seung Yong, Beom,
Sung Joo, Seong Beom)

2527
01:47:34,150 --> 01:47:35,320
Smoke break?

2528
01:47:39,960 --> 01:47:41,060
Oh, man.

2529
01:47:41,860 --> 01:47:43,500
I feel like you're just having fun...

2530
01:47:43,500 --> 01:47:44,800
- because you're bored.
- No, I'm not.

2531
01:47:45,600 --> 01:47:47,000
I just like you.

2532
01:47:48,630 --> 01:47:51,500
But I just want to tell you this.

2533
01:47:51,500 --> 01:47:52,770
We have...

2534
01:47:53,100 --> 01:47:55,770
already decided
on who'll go to the Deathmatch.

2535
01:47:57,080 --> 01:47:59,740
- Ji Hoo and I are tied,
- Yes.

2536
01:47:59,740 --> 01:48:02,380
so I just bet on the black hole
and went with it.

2537
01:48:03,050 --> 01:48:06,690
- I have one thing to tell you.
- Okay.

2538
01:48:06,690 --> 01:48:09,690
The last two players have to choose...

2539
01:48:10,090 --> 01:48:11,490
- the candidates.
- Right.

2540
01:48:12,120 --> 01:48:14,360
Say Seong Beom places first,

2541
01:48:14,460 --> 01:48:17,330
and he gives the immunity pass
to Ji Min or Hye Seon.

2542
01:48:17,760 --> 01:48:20,770
Then, the other one is
the only justified choice...

2543
01:48:20,800 --> 01:48:22,730
for this narrative to be persuasive.

2544
01:48:23,070 --> 01:48:26,470
Justification and narrative are
all important,

2545
01:48:26,470 --> 01:48:28,870
but this team has the right
to make the choice.

2546
01:48:28,870 --> 01:48:29,880
We just want some information...

2547
01:48:29,880 --> 01:48:31,010
- because we heard about the narrative...
- Yes.

2548
01:48:31,010 --> 01:48:32,640
- from YunB about why the team...
- Right.

2549
01:48:32,780 --> 01:48:35,180
- was divided in the first place.
- Yes.

2550
01:48:35,180 --> 01:48:36,650
That's how they formed a team.

2551
01:48:36,650 --> 01:48:38,980
- So, you can at least tell us that.
- Yes, I understand.

2552
01:48:38,980 --> 01:48:41,190
That way, we know
how the narrative started,

2553
01:48:41,190 --> 01:48:42,490
- which was because of Seung Yong.
- Yes.

2554
01:48:42,490 --> 01:48:44,120
There were victims
due to Seung Yong's actions,

2555
01:48:44,120 --> 01:48:45,890
- which divided the team,
- Yes.

2556
01:48:45,890 --> 01:48:47,890
- and it led to this Deathmatch.
- Yes.

2557
01:48:47,890 --> 01:48:51,060
So, we just want to know
what we're missing...

2558
01:48:51,060 --> 01:48:52,060
along the process.

2559
01:48:52,060 --> 01:48:54,400
We have the narrative,
and we have a justification...

2560
01:48:54,400 --> 01:48:55,600
to eliminate Seung Yong, right?

2561
01:48:55,600 --> 01:48:58,200
That's been building up until now.

2562
01:48:58,200 --> 01:49:00,440
And then, Xitsuh...

2563
01:49:01,070 --> 01:49:02,610
and Tae Gyun had to leave.

2564
01:49:02,610 --> 01:49:03,640
That's what you're missing.

2565
01:49:03,640 --> 01:49:06,850
Because those two meant so much to us.

2566
01:49:06,850 --> 01:49:08,910
So, that was the middle point.

2567
01:49:08,910 --> 01:49:10,120
Right. The only one.

2568
01:49:10,120 --> 01:49:12,420
- Yes, I understand it all.
- Yes.

2569
01:49:12,420 --> 01:49:14,750
You were all talking
about narratives and justifications,

2570
01:49:14,750 --> 01:49:16,390
so I wanted to know
what the justification for today was.

2571
01:49:16,390 --> 01:49:18,320
Today,

2572
01:49:18,320 --> 01:49:19,960
other than the heist...

2573
01:49:19,960 --> 01:49:22,430
- I want to know who insisted on that.
- Yesterday's...

2574
01:49:22,660 --> 01:49:25,700
I have to know that
before I pick one for the Deathmatch.

2575
01:49:25,700 --> 01:49:27,570
- It's not that someone insisted.
- I can't just pick anyone.

2576
01:49:27,570 --> 01:49:29,630
Each team lost a teammate yesterday,

2577
01:49:29,630 --> 01:49:32,200
and everyone simultaneously felt that.

2578
01:49:32,200 --> 01:49:35,240
They were like, "We're going
to eliminate Seung Yong tomorrow."

2579
01:49:35,470 --> 01:49:38,480
- It's not...
- That's why I know it was Ji Min.

2580
01:49:38,480 --> 01:49:39,510
- Yes, you're right.
- Ji Min.

2581
01:49:39,510 --> 01:49:40,880
But she...

2582
01:49:41,110 --> 01:49:43,650
He said, "I don't care, YunB.
Just tell me."

2583
01:49:43,880 --> 01:49:47,650
"Who is alienating us?"

2584
01:49:47,820 --> 01:49:49,490
I told him right away...

2585
01:49:49,990 --> 01:49:51,160
that it was Ji Min.

2586
01:49:58,060 --> 01:50:00,600
Ji Min, are you getting
the elimination immunity pass today?

2587
01:50:01,400 --> 01:50:03,200
Me? We haven't talked about that yet.

2588
01:50:03,200 --> 01:50:04,900
Really? Why don't you go with us?

2589
01:50:04,900 --> 01:50:06,070
- To the Deathmatch.
- I'm fine with that.

2590
01:50:06,540 --> 01:50:07,940
- I like that idea.
- I'm all right with that.

2591
01:50:08,270 --> 01:50:09,940
We don't care who goes.

2592
01:50:11,480 --> 01:50:13,010
Then, you'll be at a disadvantage.

2593
01:50:13,010 --> 01:50:14,380
We'll beat you to death.

2594
01:50:14,650 --> 01:50:16,680
I can beat you by myself too.

2595
01:50:18,720 --> 01:50:20,650
So, you're going to the Deathmatch
with us.

2596
01:50:20,650 --> 01:50:21,990
- Yes, that sounds fun.
- Okay?

2597
01:50:21,990 --> 01:50:24,860
He got under my skin,

2598
01:50:25,020 --> 01:50:26,520
and I was offended.

2599
01:50:27,030 --> 01:50:30,800
So, I was determined to defeat them.

2600
01:50:31,900 --> 01:50:33,370
How much are you spending
on the black hole?

2601
01:50:33,730 --> 01:50:35,670
We can't move the black hole.
I recommend getting the star.

2602
01:50:35,800 --> 01:50:37,700
I bet Ji Hoo and Seung Yong will
also come for the star.

2603
01:50:37,700 --> 01:50:40,240
Hye Seon, YunB, and I can't get
to the star, anyway.

2604
01:50:40,740 --> 01:50:42,040
With the rest of the members,

2605
01:50:42,040 --> 01:50:44,110
it's about who's placing first,

2606
01:50:44,110 --> 01:50:45,380
so that doesn't matter.

2607
01:50:45,380 --> 01:50:48,150
Hye Seon, YunB, and I need to go
where it's safe.

2608
01:50:48,150 --> 01:50:50,720
So, the three of us will go
to Sector Eight...

2609
01:50:50,720 --> 01:50:53,180
and stay safe.

2610
01:50:53,250 --> 01:50:54,450
One of us...

2611
01:50:54,820 --> 01:50:57,760
The one who has the most coins
can get the black hole...

2612
01:50:57,760 --> 01:50:58,760
(Dwarf planet, cosmic dust)

2613
01:50:58,760 --> 01:51:00,790
The three of us can't risk going down...

2614
01:51:00,790 --> 01:51:02,930
because they might move it again.

2615
01:51:02,930 --> 01:51:04,600
To prevent that,

2616
01:51:04,600 --> 01:51:07,570
we have to spend about 17 coins
to move it here.

2617
01:51:08,000 --> 01:51:11,240
That rules out the possibilities
of our loss.

2618
01:51:11,470 --> 01:51:14,740
I believe they moved the black hole
to the star.

2619
01:51:15,310 --> 01:51:17,210
Unfortunately,

2620
01:51:17,210 --> 01:51:18,880
I happened to be...

2621
01:51:18,880 --> 01:51:20,950
at the star's sector.

2622
01:51:20,950 --> 01:51:23,250
That's when we decided...

2623
01:51:23,250 --> 01:51:25,380
to control the black hole
as much as we can.

2624
01:51:25,380 --> 01:51:26,680
We had seven members,

2625
01:51:27,450 --> 01:51:29,250
so we could utilize most of the coins.

2626
01:51:34,960 --> 01:51:36,660
How may I help you?

2627
01:51:37,230 --> 01:51:39,300
I'll buy some coins.

2628
01:51:39,330 --> 01:51:42,170
Ji Min, 10,000 dollars will be deducted
from your funds.

2629
01:51:42,170 --> 01:51:43,200
Okay.

2630
01:51:43,300 --> 01:51:45,240
I'll bet 18 coins on the black hole...

2631
01:51:45,240 --> 01:51:47,470
and send it to Sector 13.

2632
01:51:47,470 --> 01:51:48,810
(Black hole, 18 coins, Sector 13)

2633
01:51:48,810 --> 01:51:51,240
(She spent all her coins.)

2634
01:51:51,240 --> 01:51:53,240
I've received 18 coins.

2635
01:51:54,010 --> 01:51:55,210
(Points earned in Round 7)

2636
01:51:55,210 --> 01:51:57,050
Round Seven has ended.

2637
01:51:57,580 --> 01:51:59,120
Round Eight will now begin...

2638
01:51:59,120 --> 01:52:01,150
and run for 30 minutes.

2639
01:52:01,150 --> 01:52:03,120
(Points earned, total score)

2640
01:52:03,120 --> 01:52:06,320
The star's energy is now four,
and it's turned into a supernova.

2641
01:52:06,390 --> 01:52:09,760
The players in the supernova's sector...

2642
01:52:09,760 --> 01:52:11,760
will lose five points
starting in this round.

2643
01:52:12,200 --> 01:52:13,260
Now,

2644
01:52:14,170 --> 01:52:18,040
to blow up the black hole,

2645
01:52:18,040 --> 01:52:19,600
we need 12 more coins.

2646
01:52:19,600 --> 01:52:22,340
We spend 13 coins or more
one more time, and it's game over.

2647
01:52:22,570 --> 01:52:24,380
Are you worried that they'll send it
to the supernova sector?

2648
01:52:25,810 --> 01:52:27,580
One variable was...

2649
01:52:27,750 --> 01:52:29,510
that they could move to the supernova...

2650
01:52:29,680 --> 01:52:31,480
while sending the black hole...

2651
01:52:31,480 --> 01:52:32,680
to themselves.

2652
01:52:32,680 --> 01:52:34,220
Then, the supernova's negativity
becomes positivity,

2653
01:52:34,220 --> 01:52:35,250
so they all earn five points.

2654
01:52:35,250 --> 01:52:37,490
These new strategies could come up,

2655
01:52:37,490 --> 01:52:39,560
so we tried to stop their extra plans...

2656
01:52:39,560 --> 01:52:41,290
in the remaining rounds.

2657
01:52:41,860 --> 01:52:44,260
Here are the results of the last round.

2658
01:52:44,260 --> 01:52:45,800
(Points earned in Round 8)

2659
01:52:45,800 --> 01:52:47,330
(Points earned, total score)

2660
01:52:47,330 --> 01:52:48,930
(Points earned in Round 8)

2661
01:52:49,230 --> 01:52:50,700
Beom didn't even enter, right?

2662
01:52:50,870 --> 01:52:52,440
I don't think so.

2663
01:52:52,500 --> 01:52:55,210
I don't think Beom entered.

2664
01:52:55,340 --> 01:52:57,180
That's the only way we get those results.

2665
01:52:57,410 --> 01:52:59,840
He's decided to go to the Deathmatch.

2666
01:53:00,250 --> 01:53:01,810
He's trying to pick between the two.

2667
01:53:04,050 --> 01:53:05,820
The game is already over.

2668
01:53:05,820 --> 01:53:07,850
I don't know what they're calculating now.

2669
01:53:07,850 --> 01:53:09,690
Me neither.

2670
01:53:10,520 --> 01:53:13,120
Why are they still gathering
to have a discussion?

2671
01:53:14,160 --> 01:53:15,390
Are they coming up with a new comedy skit?

2672
01:53:17,100 --> 01:53:19,160
I talked to Beom,

2673
01:53:19,330 --> 01:53:20,870
and they already agreed...

2674
01:53:21,230 --> 01:53:23,130
that Seung Yong and Beom...

2675
01:53:23,130 --> 01:53:25,070
would go to the Deathmatch.

2676
01:53:25,070 --> 01:53:27,910
The round ends in one minute.

2677
01:53:27,940 --> 01:53:30,240
- Already.
- It's going to be a problem.

2678
01:53:34,150 --> 01:53:35,450
That's why they're resting.

2679
01:53:41,150 --> 01:53:43,090
- They're resting already.
- They gave up.

2680
01:53:43,660 --> 01:53:45,460
Yes, those two already made up
their minds...

2681
01:53:45,460 --> 01:53:46,560
to go to the Deathmatch.

2682
01:53:46,560 --> 01:53:47,830
That way, they can save Ji Hoo.

2683
01:53:48,830 --> 01:53:50,430
I mean, Ji Hoo didn't do anything wrong.

2684
01:53:50,530 --> 01:53:52,900
You either leave tomorrow or today.

2685
01:53:53,530 --> 01:53:55,030
There's no one's fault here.

2686
01:53:55,030 --> 01:53:56,770
- Exactly.
- That's the game we're playing,

2687
01:53:56,770 --> 01:53:58,340
so we're only trying to justify ourselves.

2688
01:53:58,400 --> 01:54:00,840
- We at least need the justification.
- Exactly.

2689
01:54:00,840 --> 01:54:03,470
This way, we get revenge for yesterday.

2690
01:54:03,470 --> 01:54:04,780
- We're finishing...
- Right.

2691
01:54:06,080 --> 01:54:07,080
a story.

2692
01:54:08,080 --> 01:54:09,880
They're hopeless now.

2693
01:54:09,880 --> 01:54:11,050
It's almost over.

2694
01:54:12,420 --> 01:54:13,950
It's finally over.

2695
01:54:15,550 --> 01:54:16,690
Finally.

2696
01:54:18,360 --> 01:54:19,860
I hope it's a memorization game.

2697
01:54:20,630 --> 01:54:21,730
Memorization?

2698
01:54:22,390 --> 01:54:23,700
I have a good memory.

2699
01:54:23,700 --> 01:54:26,760
Really? I'll count on you.

2700
01:54:27,470 --> 01:54:28,630
You do that.

2701
01:54:31,070 --> 01:54:33,440
Thinking about going to the Deathmatch,

2702
01:54:33,740 --> 01:54:37,310
I started accepting my fate.

2703
01:54:37,740 --> 01:54:41,210
I felt more lethargic.

2704
01:54:42,210 --> 01:54:44,180
I was just hoping it would end soon.

2705
01:54:44,180 --> 01:54:46,680
It was so exhausting.

2706
01:54:47,090 --> 01:54:48,850
I just lay there with them.

2707
01:54:56,230 --> 01:54:58,030
Team R wasn't there...

2708
01:54:58,030 --> 01:55:00,930
when we joined forces
and attacked Team P1.

2709
01:55:01,030 --> 01:55:02,030
Right.

2710
01:55:02,030 --> 01:55:03,400
They had so much fun...

2711
01:55:03,400 --> 01:55:06,770
when they gathered all the others
to attack Team P2 and us.

2712
01:55:07,010 --> 01:55:09,170
They're dispirited since it's their
first time being on the receiving end.

2713
01:55:09,170 --> 01:55:11,610
That happens the first time. Also,

2714
01:55:12,310 --> 01:55:13,580
it's their first time
on a survival show...

2715
01:55:13,580 --> 01:55:14,950
and getting ganged up on.

2716
01:55:15,610 --> 01:55:18,220
Naturally, their attitude goes,
"Why are we playing this..."

2717
01:55:18,220 --> 01:55:20,290
- "in the first place?"
- Right.

2718
01:55:20,790 --> 01:55:21,850
I understand them.

2719
01:55:21,990 --> 01:55:23,490
It's not exactly an appropriate reaction.

2720
01:55:23,490 --> 01:55:26,060
You ought to do your best
even when you're losing.

2721
01:55:26,390 --> 01:55:28,230
When you're on a survival show,

2722
01:55:28,830 --> 01:55:31,860
you're put in such unfair situations.

2723
01:55:32,030 --> 01:55:34,230
And Bloody Game tells you
from the get-go...

2724
01:55:34,230 --> 01:55:37,100
that it's an irrational and unfair game.

2725
01:55:37,100 --> 01:55:38,740
If we hadn't started it,
they would have done it to us.

2726
01:55:38,740 --> 01:55:41,040
And this happens frequently...

2727
01:55:41,040 --> 01:55:42,210
on survival shows.

2728
01:55:42,670 --> 01:55:45,810
YunB is so cute. He went to them...

2729
01:55:45,810 --> 01:55:49,280
and tried to sway them by talking
about justifications and narratives.

2730
01:55:49,350 --> 01:55:51,750
- While he did that,
- He hinted to them about Ji Min.

2731
01:55:51,750 --> 01:55:53,990
he ruled out the possibility...

2732
01:55:53,990 --> 01:55:56,820
of being chosen.

2733
01:55:57,060 --> 01:55:58,260
People are so funny.

2734
01:55:58,260 --> 01:56:00,290
In the end, they formed a team to win.

2735
01:56:00,290 --> 01:56:01,860
But he flattered the opponents...

2736
01:56:01,860 --> 01:56:04,530
- so that they wouldn't pick him.
- Now that it's nearing the end,

2737
01:56:04,530 --> 01:56:06,700
he went and made sure
that he wouldn't be picked.

2738
01:56:06,930 --> 01:56:08,070
You have every right to do that.

2739
01:56:08,070 --> 01:56:09,400
- But I can clearly see how he's doing.
- Right.

2740
01:56:09,400 --> 01:56:10,740
It's cute, though.

2741
01:56:13,070 --> 01:56:15,440
There are many survival methods.

2742
01:56:16,310 --> 01:56:18,340
Round Nine has ended.

2743
01:56:18,540 --> 01:56:22,180
Round 10 will now begin
and run for 30 minutes.

2744
01:56:24,920 --> 01:56:25,980
It's over.

2745
01:56:26,920 --> 01:56:28,520
The leader has been decided.

2746
01:56:29,790 --> 01:56:31,360
Where do you want to go?

2747
01:56:31,460 --> 01:56:33,360
I'll go where I want to go this time.

2748
01:56:33,360 --> 01:56:35,690
- Okay.
- We can all go wherever we want.

2749
01:56:35,690 --> 01:56:36,690
It's the last round, after all.

2750
01:56:36,960 --> 01:56:40,060
(Majority Alliance's victory
has been decided.)

2751
01:56:42,570 --> 01:56:43,700
I'll go and transfer.

2752
01:56:44,770 --> 01:56:46,740
The funds? You both have to go in.

2753
01:56:47,110 --> 01:56:48,840
- What?
- You both have to go in for that.

2754
01:56:49,970 --> 01:56:51,810
We're giving all the remaining energy...

2755
01:56:51,810 --> 01:56:53,210
to Ji Hoo.

2756
01:56:53,210 --> 01:56:55,680
We decided to hand him over...

2757
01:56:55,780 --> 01:56:58,480
our entire strength and perish...

2758
01:56:59,650 --> 01:57:00,650
like the stars.

2759
01:57:01,250 --> 01:57:02,490
Kwak Beom would like to transfer...

2760
01:57:03,550 --> 01:57:05,160
his entire funds...

2761
01:57:05,160 --> 01:57:07,020
to Kang Ji Hoo.

2762
01:57:07,330 --> 01:57:10,330
Kwak Beom's personal funds
of 20,000 dollars...

2763
01:57:10,330 --> 01:57:11,400
will be transferred to Kang Ji Hoo.

2764
01:57:12,100 --> 01:57:13,360
I'd like to transfer my funds.

2765
01:57:14,570 --> 01:57:16,900
(Seung Yong gives Ji Hoo 20,000 dollars.)

2766
01:57:19,100 --> 01:57:21,210
Round Ten has ended.

2767
01:57:21,570 --> 01:57:24,740
The final results will be announced soon.

2768
01:57:25,940 --> 01:57:27,680
Who should we pick?

2769
01:57:27,680 --> 01:57:30,720
But I heard
that Sung Joo had already earned...

2770
01:57:30,720 --> 01:57:31,780
an elimination immunity pass.

2771
01:57:31,850 --> 01:57:33,220
- Really?
- He was promised.

2772
01:57:33,220 --> 01:57:34,950
Hye Seon and YunB said so.

2773
01:57:35,220 --> 01:57:36,220
They said that was the team's opinion.

2774
01:57:36,220 --> 01:57:38,060
But it might not be true. Keun Woo...

2775
01:57:38,560 --> 01:57:40,190
will suggest giving it to Ji Min.

2776
01:57:40,760 --> 01:57:42,930
Then, what's our list?

2777
01:57:43,330 --> 01:57:45,360
I'm still torn.

2778
01:57:45,660 --> 01:57:47,300
I honestly want to play with Ji Min.

2779
01:57:47,300 --> 01:57:48,300
So do I.

2780
01:57:48,300 --> 01:57:51,800
She was the primary reason
that led to all of this.

2781
01:57:52,100 --> 01:57:55,110
She had formed a majority alliance,
so it'll teach her...

2782
01:57:55,110 --> 01:57:57,140
a good lesson for her life
to be attacked by one.

2783
01:57:58,140 --> 01:58:01,080
An eye for an eye,
and a tooth for a tooth, right?

2784
01:58:01,080 --> 01:58:02,310
That's true.

2785
01:58:02,980 --> 01:58:04,620
She caused our loss,

2786
01:58:05,020 --> 01:58:07,720
so it's only fair
that she also risks something.

2787
01:58:07,720 --> 01:58:09,950
She should have risked
one of her fingers, at least.

2788
01:58:11,420 --> 01:58:12,690
I don't know how it will go.

2789
01:58:13,220 --> 01:58:17,330
I need to take Ji Min to the Deathmatch.

2790
01:58:17,800 --> 01:58:20,160
But what we're worried about is...

2791
01:58:20,200 --> 01:58:21,570
We had talked about it until Round Ten.

2792
01:58:21,800 --> 01:58:25,470
If Ji Min places first, we can't pick her.

2793
01:58:25,700 --> 01:58:27,470
Or she made a deal with someone...

2794
01:58:27,710 --> 01:58:29,840
to receive the immunity pass.

2795
01:58:29,840 --> 01:58:31,610
Then, our plan won't work.

2796
01:58:32,380 --> 01:58:33,540
What are you...

2797
01:58:34,880 --> 01:58:36,050
staring at, Beom?

2798
01:58:36,450 --> 01:58:38,780
It just looks like it's been decided.

2799
01:58:38,780 --> 01:58:39,820
Yes.

2800
01:58:40,120 --> 01:58:41,750
- You didn't go in?
- There are six points apart...

2801
01:58:42,190 --> 01:58:44,190
Why aren't you going to the Voting Room?

2802
01:58:44,190 --> 01:58:45,790
My work is done.

2803
01:58:45,790 --> 01:58:47,160
I've already given him everything.

2804
01:58:47,160 --> 01:58:48,960
I gave him my entire funds.

2805
01:58:49,230 --> 01:58:50,700
This is all meaningless.

2806
01:58:50,700 --> 01:58:54,570
Even if I make a move,
it's only one sector at a time.

2807
01:58:54,930 --> 01:58:56,700
We also haven't chosen number one.

2808
01:58:56,700 --> 01:58:59,470
It's going to be random.

2809
01:59:02,040 --> 01:59:04,540
Who are you going to pick
for the Deathmatch?

2810
01:59:04,680 --> 01:59:07,110
I'm not sure yet.

2811
01:59:07,650 --> 01:59:09,110
Could you share it with us...

2812
01:59:09,380 --> 01:59:10,720
if you decide who to pick?

2813
01:59:11,880 --> 01:59:13,750
We also...

2814
01:59:14,050 --> 01:59:15,150
have no idea.

2815
01:59:15,790 --> 01:59:20,690
We want to know who you'd pick and why.

2816
01:59:20,690 --> 01:59:22,230
But when it's announced...

2817
01:59:22,230 --> 01:59:23,490
You're right.

2818
01:59:23,490 --> 01:59:25,630
- We'll have to share anyway.
- You're right.

2819
01:59:27,700 --> 01:59:29,970
For now... I don't know.

2820
01:59:31,140 --> 01:59:32,400
This is Bloody Game.

2821
01:59:32,740 --> 01:59:34,140
A game with no fair play.

2822
01:59:34,470 --> 01:59:35,840
I'll pay them back in kind.

2823
01:59:39,180 --> 01:59:40,980
This is the situation we're in.

2824
01:59:41,310 --> 01:59:43,280
We're deciding who to put in first place.

2825
01:59:43,580 --> 01:59:44,950
As a matter of fact,

2826
01:59:45,480 --> 01:59:47,120
it's either Seong Beom...

2827
01:59:47,890 --> 01:59:48,990
or Ji Min.

2828
01:59:49,990 --> 01:59:52,820
Darn it, seriously.
Why is he the one planning all this?

2829
01:59:52,820 --> 01:59:54,330
That punk.

2830
01:59:55,260 --> 01:59:56,530
I don't get it.

2831
01:59:57,660 --> 01:59:59,300
YunB doesn't want to go to Deathmatch.

2832
01:59:59,300 --> 02:00:00,460
Right.

2833
02:00:00,460 --> 02:00:02,530
- Okay.
- He can't say that. Darn it.

2834
02:00:03,100 --> 02:00:06,740
That's why he is racking his brain
right now.

2835
02:00:07,040 --> 02:00:09,410
He's spewing nonsense.

2836
02:00:09,670 --> 02:00:10,880
He doesn't want to go?

2837
02:00:11,080 --> 02:00:12,840
Who here wants to go to Deathmatch?

2838
02:00:13,580 --> 02:00:18,180
I told you. Why talk about that
in the middle of the game?

2839
02:00:18,180 --> 02:00:21,490
He'd check others here and there
to build a justification.

2840
02:00:21,490 --> 02:00:23,350
You've got to be kidding me. Darn.

2841
02:00:23,350 --> 02:00:25,760
That doesn't make sense.
Why doesn't he step forward, then?

2842
02:00:26,520 --> 02:00:27,660
And he doesn't want to go.

2843
02:00:28,960 --> 02:00:30,530
I felt upset because...

2844
02:00:30,800 --> 02:00:32,700
YunB was talking about...

2845
02:00:32,700 --> 02:00:36,870
who the perpetrators and victims were.

2846
02:00:36,870 --> 02:00:40,640
And I was like,
"Who are you to talk about that?"

2847
02:00:41,340 --> 02:00:43,340
He doesn't have the right to say that.

2848
02:00:43,940 --> 02:00:44,940
Still,

2849
02:00:45,440 --> 02:00:48,480
you went through a lot,
overcoming an unexpected obstacle.

2850
02:00:48,910 --> 02:00:49,910
- Seriously.
- Yes.

2851
02:00:50,080 --> 02:00:51,580
- Right.
- Well done.

2852
02:00:51,580 --> 02:00:54,350
- Well done.
- We did well.

2853
02:00:54,690 --> 02:00:56,890
Honestly, I think that team lost...

2854
02:00:56,890 --> 02:00:58,760
because they gave up in the middle.

2855
02:00:58,760 --> 02:01:00,090
- They had a high chance of winning too.
- Right.

2856
02:01:00,090 --> 02:01:01,260
They could've changed their supernova.

2857
02:01:01,260 --> 02:01:02,430
Yes, there was a rule...

2858
02:01:02,430 --> 02:01:03,590
- about supernova turning the tables.
- Right.

2859
02:01:03,590 --> 02:01:04,930
They had a way to win,

2860
02:01:04,930 --> 02:01:06,630
- but they didn't. That's why they lost.
- You're rubbing salt in their wound.

2861
02:01:07,200 --> 02:01:09,870
That's what I honestly think.
You never know until the end,

2862
02:01:09,870 --> 02:01:11,270
but they lost.

2863
02:01:11,270 --> 02:01:13,170
That's why they got
the zero percent chance of winning.

2864
02:01:13,170 --> 02:01:14,570
- That's right.
- So,

2865
02:01:14,570 --> 02:01:16,270
what I'm saying is,

2866
02:01:17,070 --> 02:01:18,510
we don't have to try and understand them.

2867
02:01:18,510 --> 02:01:20,210
We just need to stick to our plan.

2868
02:01:22,880 --> 02:01:25,480
He's right. Based on the structure
of Bloody Game,

2869
02:01:25,820 --> 02:01:27,350
if you planned the game,

2870
02:01:27,590 --> 02:01:29,150
you should take responsibility to the end.

2871
02:01:30,820 --> 02:01:32,360
Ji Hoo, what's your thought?

2872
02:01:32,360 --> 02:01:33,360
I agree.

2873
02:01:42,430 --> 02:01:45,640
The Money Challenge results
will now be announced.

2874
02:01:46,300 --> 02:01:49,940
The bottom player
of the Money Challenge is...

2875
02:01:50,440 --> 02:01:51,980
(Kwak Beom)

2876
02:01:51,980 --> 02:01:52,980
Kwak Beom.

2877
02:01:53,680 --> 02:01:54,810
So cool.

2878
02:01:54,810 --> 02:01:56,710
Your name was announced
for the first time.

2879
02:01:57,850 --> 02:01:59,250
(Shin Seung Yong)

2880
02:01:59,250 --> 02:02:01,190
It's Shin Seung Yong.

2881
02:02:02,420 --> 02:02:03,420
Gosh.

2882
02:02:04,090 --> 02:02:05,860
- It's a fight between two titans.
- Next,

2883
02:02:05,860 --> 02:02:08,830
today's Money Challenge winner
will now be announced.

2884
02:02:09,360 --> 02:02:11,530
The winner of today's Money Challenge...

2885
02:02:17,840 --> 02:02:21,070
It was important to see
who won first place.

2886
02:02:21,340 --> 02:02:24,210
The most important thing was to avoid
Ji Min from getting first place.

2887
02:02:24,210 --> 02:02:26,780
That's what I prayed for.
That's what I kept praying for.

2888
02:02:27,450 --> 02:02:28,750
"Please don't come in first."

2889
02:02:30,680 --> 02:02:32,380
It's Heo Seong Beom.

2890
02:02:32,380 --> 02:02:37,720
(The winner of Money Challenge,
Heo Seong Beom)

2891
02:02:38,090 --> 02:02:40,290
You go to the comet,
and Sung Joo, come to the satellite.

2892
02:02:40,620 --> 02:02:42,990
That's because even if Sung Joo
wins 5 points, he can't win 1st place.

2893
02:02:43,330 --> 02:02:45,100
- It's impossible.
- Okay.

2894
02:02:45,100 --> 02:02:47,000
Sung Joo, come to the satellite.

2895
02:02:47,770 --> 02:02:49,300
The strategy was to make...

2896
02:02:49,300 --> 02:02:51,000
the one who won first place...

2897
02:02:51,000 --> 02:02:52,500
to join first place.

2898
02:02:52,500 --> 02:02:56,240
Seong Beom and I had similar scores.

2899
02:02:56,240 --> 02:02:59,040
But Seong Beom had coins
he could use to move,

2900
02:02:59,040 --> 02:03:02,410
so that's why I think
Seong Beom went first.

2901
02:03:02,410 --> 02:03:03,910
I'll move to Sector Two.

2902
02:03:03,910 --> 02:03:05,320
I'll move my sector.

2903
02:03:05,550 --> 02:03:06,780
You need three coins.

2904
02:03:06,780 --> 02:03:08,620
- Will you use them?
- Yes.

2905
02:03:08,850 --> 02:03:11,760
(He earned 5 points in Round 9.)

2906
02:03:11,760 --> 02:03:13,320
You have submitted three coins.

2907
02:03:14,130 --> 02:03:16,730
You've been relocated to Sector One.

2908
02:03:16,730 --> 02:03:18,130
(Won 1st place in Round 10
with 31 points in total)

2909
02:03:18,130 --> 02:03:19,330
(Project Galaxy Final Results)

2910
02:03:19,330 --> 02:03:20,560
(Seong Beom: 31, Ji Min: 30,
Keun Woo: 22, Sung Joo: 19, YunB: 17,)

2911
02:03:20,560 --> 02:03:21,770
(Hye Seon: 14, Jin Ho: 14, Ji Hoo: minus
2, Seung Yong: minus 3, Beom: minus 30)

2912
02:03:21,770 --> 02:03:25,000
The winner, Heo Seong Beom,
enter the Voting Room right now...

2913
02:03:25,000 --> 02:03:27,870
and receive 20,000 dollars,
your personal funds.

2914
02:03:28,470 --> 02:03:33,910
Also, choose a player you can transfer
the elimination immunity pass to.

2915
02:03:34,980 --> 02:03:36,710
It made me think a lot.

2916
02:03:36,910 --> 02:03:40,480
At first, I thought of Sung Joo naturally,

2917
02:03:40,890 --> 02:03:43,720
and that's because he joined us
after abandoning his team.

2918
02:03:44,090 --> 02:03:48,460
And regarding that, his former team
could target him.

2919
02:03:49,030 --> 02:03:51,100
And Ji Min.

2920
02:03:51,330 --> 02:03:55,070
Ji Min's been too much focused
by the opponents as a target,

2921
02:03:55,330 --> 02:03:58,840
so I kept wondering who I should
give the elimination immunity pass to...

2922
02:03:59,040 --> 02:04:00,870
until the end.

2923
02:04:10,680 --> 02:04:13,280
(Grunting)

2924
02:04:13,650 --> 02:04:16,350
This is 20,000 dollars, the winning prize
of the Money Challenge.

2925
02:04:16,690 --> 02:04:19,190
We'll store the funds you received
in the safe.

2926
02:04:19,690 --> 02:04:20,930
Thank you.

2927
02:04:21,790 --> 02:04:26,230
Except for Beom and Seung Yong,
who are at the bottom,

2928
02:04:26,230 --> 02:04:30,030
choose a player who will be exempt
from the elimination, just like you.

2929
02:04:39,810 --> 02:04:40,880
My choice...

2930
02:04:41,180 --> 02:04:44,780
(He's done choosing the player who's
exempted by using the immunity pass.)

2931
02:04:44,780 --> 02:04:46,820
(Sighing)

2932
02:04:50,520 --> 02:04:53,590
Those who are excluded
from getting eliminated...

2933
02:04:53,820 --> 02:04:55,760
through being given
the elimination immunity pass...

2934
02:04:55,760 --> 02:04:58,000
from the winner of today's
Money Challenge, Heo Seong Beom is...

2935
02:05:00,030 --> 02:05:01,570
"Please don't get
the elimination immunity pass."

2936
02:05:01,770 --> 02:05:02,770
Now,

2937
02:05:03,030 --> 02:05:04,900
we've got to kill Ji Min.

2938
02:05:07,400 --> 02:05:09,240
It's Hong Jin Ho.

2939
02:05:11,310 --> 02:05:12,310
That's only right.

2940
02:05:12,640 --> 02:05:13,640
Well done.

2941
02:05:14,010 --> 02:05:15,010
For one,

2942
02:05:15,180 --> 02:05:18,820
I voted for Jin Ho
who showed great performance today.

2943
02:05:19,780 --> 02:05:22,020
I respect Sung Joo's decision,

2944
02:05:22,020 --> 02:05:24,150
and so do I respect Ji Min's.

2945
02:05:24,520 --> 02:05:28,330
But I concluded it'd be iffy
to side with either one.

2946
02:05:28,560 --> 02:05:30,960
If I gave it to one of them,

2947
02:05:31,300 --> 02:05:35,130
the other side can choose Jin Ho
for the Deathmatch.

2948
02:05:35,130 --> 02:05:36,670
I worried about that.

2949
02:05:36,670 --> 02:05:37,740
The biggest reason...

2950
02:05:37,970 --> 02:05:40,200
was him playing the biggest role
in today's game.

2951
02:05:40,200 --> 02:05:42,710
The bottom players
of today's Money Challenge,

2952
02:05:42,710 --> 02:05:44,980
Beom and Seung Yong,

2953
02:05:44,980 --> 02:05:46,810
please enter the Voting Room 1 by 1.

2954
02:05:46,810 --> 02:05:49,150
Then pick a person whom you'd like...

2955
02:05:49,150 --> 02:05:51,250
to join the Deathmatch.

2956
02:05:51,580 --> 02:05:53,850
Jin Ho got the elimination immunity pass,

2957
02:05:54,720 --> 02:05:55,720
and I thought, "Nice!"

2958
02:05:56,190 --> 02:05:59,020
"It's a vast expanse."

2959
02:05:59,590 --> 02:06:01,930
Nothing is involved with them.

2960
02:06:03,190 --> 02:06:04,190
Let's go.

2961
02:06:04,760 --> 02:06:06,560
But who was I to choose?

2962
02:06:06,930 --> 02:06:11,700
We wanted to drag Ji Min to Deathmatch,

2963
02:06:12,200 --> 02:06:13,900
but if we were to bring
an irrelevant person,

2964
02:06:13,900 --> 02:06:15,940
they'd join it.

2965
02:06:16,940 --> 02:06:18,610
Then, what should we do?

2966
02:06:18,610 --> 02:06:20,240
I was going to pick Jin Ho.

2967
02:06:20,240 --> 02:06:21,250
Darn.

2968
02:06:22,450 --> 02:06:23,510
What shall we do?

2969
02:06:25,250 --> 02:06:28,890
Honestly, I find Sung Joo annoying,

2970
02:06:28,890 --> 02:06:31,160
but I think it'll be better...

2971
02:06:31,160 --> 02:06:33,120
- if he advances.
- Yes, I think that'll be better too.

2972
02:06:33,620 --> 02:06:34,730
Let's go with Keun Woo and Ji Min.

2973
02:06:35,560 --> 02:06:36,560
- K and J?
- Yes.

2974
02:06:36,830 --> 02:06:38,230
Let's stick with ruining a team.

2975
02:06:38,430 --> 02:06:39,500
Otherwise, it'd get iffy.

2976
02:06:40,530 --> 02:06:42,670
If we choose both of them,
the votes will be split...

2977
02:06:43,170 --> 02:06:44,800
and we'll get the objective votes.

2978
02:06:45,200 --> 02:06:46,540
But if we go for Keun Woo and Ji Min,

2979
02:06:46,540 --> 02:06:49,210
Keun Woo would step forward.

2980
02:06:49,340 --> 02:06:51,140
- I'm certain.
- Keun Woo?

2981
02:06:51,140 --> 02:06:53,340
Yes. Wouldn't you think so too?

2982
02:06:53,840 --> 02:06:54,880
Can I hear
what you guys are talking about?

2983
02:06:54,880 --> 02:06:56,410
- Of course.
- Yes. Come here.

2984
02:06:56,410 --> 02:06:57,410
(Ji Hoo in the same alliance joins them.)

2985
02:06:57,410 --> 02:07:00,180
Ji Hoo, we were talking
about Keun Woo and Ji Min.

2986
02:07:00,680 --> 02:07:02,520
He expected
that Keun Woo would go ahead...

2987
02:07:02,720 --> 02:07:04,120
- and say they should choose him.
- For sure.

2988
02:07:04,120 --> 02:07:05,320
That's for sure.

2989
02:07:05,320 --> 02:07:06,690
But based on the others' minds...

2990
02:07:07,360 --> 02:07:08,890
There's a chance they won't pick Keun Woo.

2991
02:07:08,890 --> 02:07:09,890
That's right.

2992
02:07:10,130 --> 02:07:12,230
There's more than enough chance
for them to choose Ji Min.

2993
02:07:12,460 --> 02:07:13,460
I think...

2994
02:07:14,160 --> 02:07:17,070
I mean, we could pick Hye Seon and Ji Min,
for example.

2995
02:07:17,070 --> 02:07:19,900
Then P3 team will definitely vote
for Hye Seon.

2996
02:07:20,440 --> 02:07:24,340
Seeing the odds, Hye Seon barely has
a chance to be chosen.

2997
02:07:25,180 --> 02:07:27,580
- Well done. Good luck. But...
- Okay.

2998
02:07:28,550 --> 02:07:30,150
- What?
- If...

2999
02:07:30,150 --> 02:07:32,250
I want to strike a deal.

3000
02:07:33,120 --> 02:07:34,120
Well,

3001
02:07:34,720 --> 02:07:36,690
if you choose YunB...

3002
02:07:36,690 --> 02:07:38,260
Regardless of what has happened so far...

3003
02:07:38,260 --> 02:07:42,160
Even if we have to pay for you guys...

3004
02:07:42,160 --> 02:07:44,930
Ji Min and I can guide the right path
for you.

3005
02:07:45,330 --> 02:07:46,730
How much are you willing to give?

3006
02:07:47,100 --> 02:07:49,100
How much do you want from Ji Min and me?

3007
02:07:49,330 --> 02:07:52,040
- Me?
- I think 60,000 dollars will do.

3008
02:07:52,040 --> 02:07:53,870
- You want 60,000 dollars?
- Yes.

3009
02:07:53,870 --> 02:07:55,570
Then we can give you 20,000 dollars each
and make that 40,000 dollars.

3010
02:07:55,570 --> 02:07:57,470
For the first time,

3011
02:07:58,310 --> 02:08:00,540
I struck a deal with Beom and Seung Yong.

3012
02:08:01,350 --> 02:08:04,480
If they were to choose YunB,

3013
02:08:04,480 --> 02:08:06,920
Ji Min and I would give them
20,000 dollars each.

3014
02:08:06,920 --> 02:08:10,090
You're saying if I chose YunB,

3015
02:08:10,090 --> 02:08:12,460
you'd give me your money.

3016
02:08:12,460 --> 02:08:13,620
That can't be helped.

3017
02:08:16,130 --> 02:08:17,590
I'm sorry I couldn't choose you.

3018
02:08:18,060 --> 02:08:19,060
Not at all.

3019
02:08:19,060 --> 02:08:20,900
- You two carried the game,
- No.

3020
02:08:20,900 --> 02:08:22,230
so this is only right.

3021
02:08:22,230 --> 02:08:25,000
If it had been to be yielded between two,
I'd have picked one specifically.

3022
02:08:25,000 --> 02:08:27,070
- This is only right. Come here.
- But you both were...

3023
02:08:32,040 --> 02:08:33,710
Let's get some air.

3024
02:08:34,340 --> 02:08:36,480
Based on what I talked with Keun Woo,

3025
02:08:36,680 --> 02:08:38,980
I think it'd be best for us
if YunB leaves.

3026
02:08:39,750 --> 02:08:41,020
I'm not certain about that.

3027
02:08:41,020 --> 02:08:42,350
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

3028
02:08:42,350 --> 02:08:44,590
Shouldn't they pick YunB first?

3029
02:08:44,590 --> 02:08:46,360
I told Keun Woo to make a deal with them
about that.

3030
02:08:46,360 --> 02:08:47,360
I see.

3031
02:08:48,360 --> 02:08:51,100
If we were to make something fun...

3032
02:08:51,100 --> 02:08:52,360
(20 minutes ago)

3033
02:08:52,460 --> 02:08:55,230
It's to make them choose YunB.

3034
02:08:56,700 --> 02:08:59,240
Then we'll only need to vote
and make YunB gone.

3035
02:08:59,240 --> 02:09:00,240
You're right.

3036
02:09:01,910 --> 02:09:03,870
Do you think we could make a deal
with them?

3037
02:09:04,310 --> 02:09:05,310
To whom?

3038
02:09:05,310 --> 02:09:08,350
You're close to Beom,
so make a deal with Beom.

3039
02:09:09,250 --> 02:09:12,150
Tell them we'll abandon YunB.
If they choose him,

3040
02:09:12,150 --> 02:09:14,550
and if Seung Yong wins at the Deathmatch,

3041
02:09:14,550 --> 02:09:17,590
then we won't exclude him
from the next round...

3042
02:09:17,590 --> 02:09:19,490
and play with him as his team.
Tell them about that.

3043
02:09:19,490 --> 02:09:21,560
Okay, I'll talk to them.

3044
02:09:21,930 --> 02:09:23,860
If it doesn't work,
you could mention the funds.

3045
02:09:23,860 --> 02:09:25,830
- Okay.
- I have enough money too.

3046
02:09:26,130 --> 02:09:27,660
Let's get on with that.

3047
02:09:27,660 --> 02:09:30,930
(Based on what Ji Min asked,)

3048
02:09:30,930 --> 02:09:36,110
(Keun Woo made a deal.)

3049
02:09:36,610 --> 02:09:40,080
I was really bothered
by YunB playing politics at the end,

3050
02:09:40,080 --> 02:09:43,180
and it got on my nerves so much.

3051
02:09:43,180 --> 02:09:44,920
It ruined my mood completely.

3052
02:09:44,920 --> 02:09:48,890
So I thought it'd be better
to get rid of YunB...

3053
02:09:49,190 --> 02:09:50,490
who is stirring things up.

3054
02:10:00,230 --> 02:10:03,800
Choose a player
you'd like to play Deathmatch with.

3055
02:10:08,870 --> 02:10:11,240
You've chosen Park Ji Min.

3056
02:10:12,480 --> 02:10:13,480
I'm sorry.

3057
02:10:15,110 --> 02:10:17,650
Seung Yong,
please leave this area right now...

3058
02:10:17,650 --> 02:10:19,150
and prepare for the Deathmatch.

3059
02:10:19,150 --> 02:10:20,150
Okay.

3060
02:10:35,800 --> 02:10:39,400
Choose a player you'd like to
play Deathmatch with.

3061
02:10:45,410 --> 02:10:49,310
Beom, please leave this area right now
and prepare for the Deathmatch.

3062
02:10:49,310 --> 02:10:51,750
You're not allowed to talk
with other players.

3063
02:10:51,750 --> 02:10:52,750
Okay.

3064
02:10:57,250 --> 02:10:59,360
Here are the results.

3065
02:11:01,190 --> 02:11:03,490
The player chosen for Deathmatch is...

3066
02:11:10,770 --> 02:11:11,800
(Park Ji Min)

3067
02:11:11,800 --> 02:11:14,670
It's Park Ji Min.

3068
02:11:16,110 --> 02:11:18,380
I kind of expected it.

3069
02:11:18,380 --> 02:11:22,180
I thought they thought of me
as the leader.

3070
02:11:22,180 --> 02:11:25,080
If that's why they picked me,

3071
02:11:25,480 --> 02:11:26,780
then it's a bit...

3072
02:11:28,890 --> 02:11:30,820
of an ugly choice.

3073
02:11:31,490 --> 02:11:33,020
The second player chosen
for Deathmatch is...

3074
02:11:34,660 --> 02:11:36,530
(Jeong Keun Woo)

3075
02:11:36,530 --> 02:11:39,860
It's Jeong Keun Woo.

3076
02:11:41,530 --> 02:11:43,870
It happened to be...

3077
02:11:43,870 --> 02:11:47,640
Keun Woo, none other than others.

3078
02:11:49,540 --> 02:11:51,980
You've chosen Jeong Keun Woo.

3079
02:11:51,980 --> 02:11:54,010
(Beom chose Keun Woo.)

3080
02:11:54,280 --> 02:11:55,310
I think...

3081
02:11:55,310 --> 02:11:58,420
if I had to choose two people from P1,

3082
02:12:00,350 --> 02:12:01,390
then...

3083
02:12:02,150 --> 02:12:04,920
people wouldn't vote for Keun Woo.

3084
02:12:05,920 --> 02:12:08,990
Two members of Team P1 were chosen,

3085
02:12:08,990 --> 02:12:11,300
so I wasn't too glad.

3086
02:12:11,630 --> 02:12:14,500
Jeong Keun Woo and Park Ji Min.

3087
02:12:14,500 --> 02:12:17,570
You'll vote between the two candidates.

3088
02:12:17,570 --> 02:12:19,740
Players, please vote for one player...

3089
02:12:19,740 --> 02:12:22,340
to proceed to Deathmatch.

3090
02:12:23,110 --> 02:12:25,810
The vote will end in an hour.

3091
02:12:27,010 --> 02:12:30,480
(The vote begins.)

3092
02:12:30,950 --> 02:12:32,580
Well, this is...

3093
02:12:32,580 --> 02:12:34,120
My gosh.

3094
02:12:34,480 --> 02:12:35,650
- This is...
- It's funny.

3095
02:12:35,650 --> 02:12:37,950
Ji Min, I met you face-to-face.

3096
02:12:37,950 --> 02:12:38,960
Come here.

3097
02:12:39,120 --> 02:12:40,390
Don't see this.

3098
02:12:45,300 --> 02:12:48,270
Those old men would play politics.

3099
02:12:48,670 --> 02:12:50,600
They'd make crazy deals,

3100
02:12:50,600 --> 02:12:53,470
and Keun Woo and Ji Min would intervene.

3101
02:12:53,870 --> 02:12:55,940
Team P3 would calculate their moves.

3102
02:12:56,470 --> 02:12:58,910
Hye Seon would say,
pretending she's close to them.

3103
02:12:59,340 --> 02:13:00,710
I just didn't want any of that.

3104
02:13:02,910 --> 02:13:06,620
(He enters the Voting Room right away.)

3105
02:13:12,590 --> 02:13:13,890
(Park Ji Min, Jeong Keun Woo)

3106
02:13:15,190 --> 02:13:19,000
(Kang Ji Hoo votes for Park Ji Min.)

3107
02:13:19,230 --> 02:13:21,100
Just as Beom and Seung Yong wanted,

3108
02:13:21,100 --> 02:13:22,300
I wanted Ji Min...

3109
02:13:22,700 --> 02:13:25,340
and Seung Yong to have a face off.

3110
02:13:25,340 --> 02:13:27,840
I came out after voting for Ji Min.

3111
02:13:28,040 --> 02:13:30,840
(Sighing)

3112
02:13:30,840 --> 02:13:33,580
I mean, I didn't get to say goodbye.

3113
02:13:33,580 --> 02:13:34,750
But they just went in.

3114
02:13:37,350 --> 02:13:39,250
They must've not known
they'd be dragged right away.

3115
02:13:46,520 --> 02:13:47,960
I was so lonely and desolate.

3116
02:13:49,790 --> 02:13:51,700
I was so upset.

3117
02:13:58,840 --> 02:14:02,340
Gosh, this is hard.

3118
02:14:04,240 --> 02:14:05,510
I'm all alone now,

3119
02:14:05,740 --> 02:14:07,210
so there's no one talking to me,

3120
02:14:07,480 --> 02:14:08,610
and those who do...

3121
02:14:08,810 --> 02:14:11,180
don't really care for me...

3122
02:14:11,480 --> 02:14:14,020
nor do they show their affection.

3123
02:14:14,750 --> 02:14:17,890
I feel like I've actually lost
all my family.

3124
02:14:18,890 --> 02:14:21,360
Ji Hoo was on the other side,

3125
02:14:21,360 --> 02:14:22,690
so he'd follow their order.

3126
02:14:22,690 --> 02:14:25,830
Ji Min and Keun Woo, if you have anything
to say, say it now.

3127
02:14:25,830 --> 02:14:26,930
And please leave,

3128
02:14:26,930 --> 02:14:28,300
- so we can talk by ourselves.
- Okay.

3129
02:14:28,300 --> 02:14:30,400
If you stay,
they won't be able to say anything.

3130
02:14:30,400 --> 02:14:31,470
Shall we do that?

3131
02:14:32,340 --> 02:14:34,500
First, I...

3132
02:14:37,710 --> 02:14:38,940
I was there yesterday,

3133
02:14:40,340 --> 02:14:41,340
and today...

3134
02:14:42,150 --> 02:14:43,650
I might have to go.

3135
02:14:43,650 --> 02:14:46,080
That'll depend on you guys, though.

3136
02:14:47,120 --> 02:14:48,950
I have a winning strategy.

3137
02:14:49,290 --> 02:14:50,290
I'll come back.

3138
02:14:51,150 --> 02:14:52,920
- I'll be able to come back.
- I'll come back.

3139
02:14:52,990 --> 02:14:55,460
I got rid of Xitsuh and Tae Gyun.

3140
02:14:56,230 --> 02:14:58,860
Exactly. I feel like
he'll come back for sure.

3141
02:14:59,060 --> 02:15:00,130
I'll come back.

3142
02:15:00,130 --> 02:15:02,830
- I can also come back.
- I'm a gold medalist, you see.

3143
02:15:02,830 --> 02:15:04,600
- That hurts my pride.
- I'm the devil at second base.

3144
02:15:04,600 --> 02:15:05,600
Don't touch me.

3145
02:15:05,600 --> 02:15:07,300
You should give it a shot
and make it cool.

3146
02:15:09,240 --> 02:15:11,310
I'll throw Seung Yong away.

3147
02:15:13,610 --> 02:15:14,610
What?

3148
02:15:16,650 --> 02:15:18,720
- Hey, what is this?
- Come on.

3149
02:15:18,720 --> 02:15:19,820
She must have no credit...

3150
02:15:19,820 --> 02:15:21,320
that no one's responding.

3151
02:15:21,820 --> 02:15:24,820
- What...
- I can't do this because it's so cringe.

3152
02:15:24,820 --> 02:15:27,290
Don't make me do this.

3153
02:15:27,290 --> 02:15:29,730
I can't do things like this.

3154
02:15:29,730 --> 02:15:32,260
- Try it again.
- I can't.

3155
02:15:34,330 --> 02:15:35,500
Before time goes,

3156
02:15:35,500 --> 02:15:37,130
decide it quickly and tell us.

3157
02:15:37,130 --> 02:15:38,440
- Hang out by yourselves.
- Okay.

3158
02:15:38,440 --> 02:15:40,500
- Let's go to our room.
- Okay.

3159
02:15:40,500 --> 02:15:43,410
(Keun Woo and Ji Min exit.)

3160
02:15:45,680 --> 02:15:46,880
I feel so bad.

3161
02:15:46,880 --> 02:15:47,980
- I'm telling you.
- Do we look easy?

3162
02:15:47,980 --> 02:15:49,850
I think this is why...

3163
02:15:49,850 --> 02:15:51,150
they picked us.

3164
02:15:51,550 --> 02:15:54,550
Someone they think they can beat...

3165
02:15:54,550 --> 02:15:56,820
and the mastermind.

3166
02:15:56,820 --> 02:15:58,420
I think that's why they picked us.

3167
02:15:59,220 --> 02:16:00,660
Gosh, what do we do?

3168
02:16:00,660 --> 02:16:02,430
If it's two-thirds, the chance is high,

3169
02:16:02,430 --> 02:16:04,900
despite luck and skills.

3170
02:16:04,900 --> 02:16:06,800
It's one-thirds. Only one survives.

3171
02:16:06,800 --> 02:16:09,070
I know. Two-thirds of them go home.

3172
02:16:09,070 --> 02:16:11,170
Beom is smart too.

3173
02:16:11,170 --> 02:16:12,600
Everyone here is good at games.

3174
02:16:12,600 --> 02:16:14,200
He just says funny things, but he's smart.

3175
02:16:14,200 --> 02:16:15,540
No one is bad at games.

3176
02:16:15,540 --> 02:16:17,670
We don't know who will win
at the Deathmatch.

3177
02:16:17,670 --> 02:16:18,740
It's not surprising...

3178
02:16:18,740 --> 02:16:19,810
- if any of them survives.
- Right.

3179
02:16:20,110 --> 02:16:22,010
Then who should survive for us to benefit?

3180
02:16:23,010 --> 02:16:26,820
I don't want Ji Min to go, then.

3181
02:16:26,820 --> 02:16:29,320
The risk is too high. It's two-thirds.

3182
02:16:29,320 --> 02:16:31,450
Because today, Ji Min...

3183
02:16:32,120 --> 02:16:33,690
sacrificed herself.

3184
02:16:33,690 --> 02:16:35,090
- I know...
- That's true.

3185
02:16:35,090 --> 02:16:36,860
she threw a bomb in the middle,

3186
02:16:36,860 --> 02:16:38,930
but she used her coins...

3187
02:16:38,930 --> 02:16:41,770
- She bought five coins too.
- True.

3188
02:16:41,770 --> 02:16:44,300
She thought it'd be better
to have more people on her side,

3189
02:16:44,300 --> 02:16:45,940
so she took Sung Joo.

3190
02:16:45,940 --> 02:16:47,570
- That...
- She's a strategist.

3191
02:16:47,570 --> 02:16:50,570
It wasn't completely convincing,

3192
02:16:50,570 --> 02:16:53,480
but I think she'd have tried hard...

3193
02:16:53,480 --> 02:16:54,950
even if she failed.

3194
02:16:55,350 --> 02:16:58,880
So, I think she contributed more...

3195
02:16:58,880 --> 02:17:00,480
compared to Keun Woo.

3196
02:17:00,920 --> 02:17:02,350
That's for sure.

3197
02:17:02,820 --> 02:17:04,690
I gave it a thought.

3198
02:17:04,690 --> 02:17:07,220
If they have
a 1-in-3 chance of coming back,

3199
02:17:07,220 --> 02:17:09,630
the chance is slim.

3200
02:17:09,730 --> 02:17:14,130
I just didn't like the fact
that Ji Min was in that kind of danger.

3201
02:17:14,660 --> 02:17:18,570
I don't want to take any risk
of her going.

3202
02:17:18,570 --> 02:17:20,870
Her going to Deathmatch.

3203
02:17:20,870 --> 02:17:23,610
But we should vote with the thought
of one of them going home.

3204
02:17:23,610 --> 02:17:25,080
I know. That's why...

3205
02:17:25,480 --> 02:17:26,810
I've decided.

3206
02:17:30,010 --> 02:17:32,680
Me? Honestly speaking,

3207
02:17:32,680 --> 02:17:34,850
I'm leaning toward Ji Min.

3208
02:17:35,450 --> 02:17:38,360
I know it sounds brutal,

3209
02:17:39,220 --> 02:17:41,120
but even if she loses,

3210
02:17:41,360 --> 02:17:43,590
she has the chance to kill Seung Yong.

3211
02:17:43,960 --> 02:17:46,760
You want Ji Min to go and fight them?

3212
02:17:46,760 --> 02:17:49,200
Let her wield the knife herself.

3213
02:17:50,470 --> 02:17:52,700
I think that's...

3214
02:17:54,240 --> 02:17:55,540
- It's...
- I don't know.

3215
02:17:55,540 --> 02:17:57,640
We gather with a consensus...

3216
02:17:57,640 --> 02:17:59,880
and a great cause.

3217
02:17:59,880 --> 02:18:01,140
But when it comes to Deathmatch,

3218
02:18:01,140 --> 02:18:04,310
you let her hold the knife
and fight to survive.

3219
02:18:04,310 --> 02:18:05,620
It's too harsh on her.

3220
02:18:05,620 --> 02:18:06,620
It is.

3221
02:18:07,550 --> 02:18:09,720
But there's a chance of her winning too.

3222
02:18:09,720 --> 02:18:10,990
I'll go and vote.

3223
02:18:15,030 --> 02:18:17,130
Sorry, Keun Woo.

3224
02:18:17,690 --> 02:18:20,060
(Choi Hye Seon votes for Jeong Keun Woo.)

3225
02:18:23,700 --> 02:18:25,040
What are you going to do?

3226
02:18:26,470 --> 02:18:29,610
Me? I'm doing the math in my head.

3227
02:18:29,710 --> 02:18:31,880
Based on what I worked out,

3228
02:18:31,880 --> 02:18:34,080
Ji Min has a higher chance.

3229
02:18:34,080 --> 02:18:35,610
- Of letting her go?
- Yes.

3230
02:18:39,250 --> 02:18:40,250
Actually...

3231
02:18:40,950 --> 02:18:43,350
We should vote on our own.

3232
02:18:45,860 --> 02:18:50,030
Based on how they played today,

3233
02:18:50,030 --> 02:18:52,060
- then we should save Ji Min.
- Yes.

3234
02:18:52,630 --> 02:18:55,130
But today wasn't the only day.
There was yesterday and the day before.

3235
02:18:55,130 --> 02:18:56,770
- The first day too.
- There's tomorrow too.

3236
02:18:57,130 --> 02:18:58,400
Given that situation...

3237
02:18:58,640 --> 02:19:00,340
Actually, yesterday...

3238
02:19:01,370 --> 02:19:02,370
Keun Woo...

3239
02:19:03,140 --> 02:19:05,140
- went...
- Because he went instead of others?

3240
02:19:05,140 --> 02:19:06,340
He took one for the team.

3241
02:19:06,340 --> 02:19:08,650
Keun Woo is like this.
When that situation comes,

3242
02:19:08,650 --> 02:19:10,450
Keun Woo is the one who goes,
"Send me away."

3243
02:19:10,450 --> 02:19:11,920
He always took the bullet.

3244
02:19:11,920 --> 02:19:14,450
Right. It's the same situation
for two days straight.

3245
02:19:14,820 --> 02:19:16,820
I'm not sure if it's right
to send him away for two days straight...

3246
02:19:16,820 --> 02:19:18,350
just to save ourselves.

3247
02:19:18,690 --> 02:19:20,920
I understand Keun Woo's position.

3248
02:19:20,920 --> 02:19:22,990
I understand his heart...

3249
02:19:22,990 --> 02:19:25,130
and I make that decision
from time to time.

3250
02:19:25,430 --> 02:19:26,600
This is what it is.

3251
02:19:27,260 --> 02:19:28,500
I'm sure he wants to survive as well,

3252
02:19:28,500 --> 02:19:31,740
but there are younger ones
doing their best.

3253
02:19:31,740 --> 02:19:35,240
When a Deathmatch situation occurs,

3254
02:19:35,240 --> 02:19:37,840
he goes, "Just pick me."

3255
02:19:37,970 --> 02:19:40,310
Whenever these situations came,

3256
02:19:40,310 --> 02:19:43,810
it felt like there was a tendency
of sending him away like a scapegoat.

3257
02:19:44,210 --> 02:19:46,220
That made me feel very uncomfortable.

3258
02:19:46,220 --> 02:19:47,720
It's a form of sacrifice.

3259
02:19:47,720 --> 02:19:51,390
One sacrifice can be made
by the older guy,

3260
02:19:51,390 --> 02:19:53,460
but I believe this can't be repeated.

3261
02:20:07,340 --> 02:20:10,540
(Park Ji Min, Jeong Keun Woo)

3262
02:20:11,070 --> 02:20:13,580
(Hong Jin Ho votes for Park Ji Min.)

3263
02:20:13,580 --> 02:20:14,940
This is my vote.

3264
02:20:15,610 --> 02:20:17,110
As his friend...

3265
02:20:17,110 --> 02:20:19,550
and someone who occasionally
makes those decisions,

3266
02:20:19,550 --> 02:20:22,790
I didn't think it was right for the
same thing to happen two days straight.

3267
02:20:22,790 --> 02:20:24,920
That was the reason behind
voting for Ji Min.

3268
02:20:29,490 --> 02:20:30,990
I'm sorry.

3269
02:20:30,990 --> 02:20:32,060
(I'm sorry.)

3270
02:20:32,960 --> 02:20:35,370
(YunB votes for Park Ji Min.)

3271
02:20:38,800 --> 02:20:40,470
I'm voting for the one
who will be in the Deathmatch, right?

3272
02:20:40,840 --> 02:20:41,970
That's right.

3273
02:20:45,780 --> 02:20:48,440
(Heo Seong Beom completes his vote.)

3274
02:20:48,440 --> 02:20:51,920
(Hyun Sung Joo completes his vote.)

3275
02:20:52,220 --> 02:20:53,680
(Choi Hye Seon voted for Jeong Keun Woo.)

3276
02:20:53,680 --> 02:20:55,120
(Kang Ji Hoo, Hong Jin Ho, and Yun B
voted for Park Ji Min.)

3277
02:20:55,120 --> 02:20:56,590
(Heo Seong Beom and Hyun Sung Joo's
votes are unrevealed.)

3278
02:21:06,000 --> 02:21:07,430
I got so attached to them.

3279
02:21:07,730 --> 02:21:10,630
They were the ones I've always liked.

3280
02:21:10,870 --> 02:21:13,970
I really enjoyed being their teammates.

3281
02:21:15,040 --> 02:21:18,110
Even so, I had to survive.

3282
02:21:22,110 --> 02:21:25,720
I came this far. Winning in this survival
is about to be achieved.

3283
02:21:25,820 --> 02:21:29,150
It's upsetting, but it can't be helped.

3284
02:21:31,220 --> 02:21:36,760
(The last one to vote, Jeong Keun Woo)

3285
02:21:38,160 --> 02:21:41,430
(Park Ji Min, Jeong Keun Woo)

3286
02:21:44,800 --> 02:21:48,240
Whenever these situations come,

3287
02:21:48,840 --> 02:21:50,810
I always say I'll be the one to go.

3288
02:21:52,840 --> 02:21:54,710
I believe that's what a team leader...

3289
02:21:57,780 --> 02:22:00,320
and adults must do.

3290
02:22:00,750 --> 02:22:02,590
Ji Min has gone through
many different trials...

3291
02:22:02,590 --> 02:22:04,950
and experienced many survival shows,

3292
02:22:05,720 --> 02:22:08,460
but I want to be the one
to deal with those situations.

3293
02:22:08,460 --> 02:22:12,030
I told this to Jin Ho several times
and he scolded me.

3294
02:22:12,200 --> 02:22:13,560
Earlier, I mentioned...

3295
02:22:13,560 --> 02:22:15,900
- that I wanted to be in the Deathmatch.
- You offered to go.

3296
02:22:15,900 --> 02:22:18,940
Whenever things like Deathmatches pop up,

3297
02:22:18,940 --> 02:22:20,400
you don't have to offer yourself up.

3298
02:22:20,400 --> 02:22:21,640
- Okay.
- Right.

3299
02:22:21,640 --> 02:22:24,470
It's okay to make that move once.

3300
02:22:24,470 --> 02:22:26,380
- It's bad to do that constantly.
- Okay. I'll stop now.

3301
02:22:26,380 --> 02:22:27,480
- Right. You should stop.
- Right.

3302
02:22:27,480 --> 02:22:28,650
You're right.

3303
02:22:28,650 --> 02:22:30,480
I totally understand him.

3304
02:22:30,480 --> 02:22:31,650
He's a guy who does his best.

3305
02:22:31,650 --> 02:22:34,250
He's a guy who has great leadership
for the team.

3306
02:22:34,250 --> 02:22:36,520
I understand it when a guy like that
says that to me.

3307
02:22:37,090 --> 02:22:38,090
But...

3308
02:22:38,960 --> 02:22:41,790
I have a heart that wants
to protect my team at all costs.

3309
02:22:50,230 --> 02:22:53,770
(Park Ji Min, Jeong Keun Woo)

3310
02:22:55,410 --> 02:22:59,010
(Jeong Keun Woo votes for Jeong Keun Woo.)

3311
02:22:59,640 --> 02:23:01,580
You don't know anything, right?

3312
02:23:02,250 --> 02:23:03,410
Nobody revealed anything.

3313
02:23:03,410 --> 02:23:04,880
I don't even know what Ji Hoo is thinking.

3314
02:23:05,050 --> 02:23:07,950
It makes sense for Ji Hoo
to do this or that.

3315
02:23:07,950 --> 02:23:09,790
But whoever goes,

3316
02:23:09,790 --> 02:23:11,790
- I think they'll make it back.
- Or in Ji Hoo's situation,

3317
02:23:11,790 --> 02:23:13,460
he managed to survive.

3318
02:23:13,460 --> 02:23:16,560
The worst thing for him is
to be the only one left in his team.

3319
02:23:16,560 --> 02:23:17,560
He's incredible.

3320
02:23:17,560 --> 02:23:19,060
He kept surviving thanks to the sacrifice
of his teammates,

3321
02:23:19,060 --> 02:23:20,060
but he's tearless.

3322
02:23:21,000 --> 02:23:25,370
(Ji Hoo was lying alone in the room.)

3323
02:23:50,860 --> 02:23:52,200
I went to my room...

3324
02:23:52,530 --> 02:23:54,800
and lay down on Kyoung Hoon's bed.

3325
02:23:56,900 --> 02:23:58,740
I tried my best not to cry,

3326
02:23:58,740 --> 02:24:00,100
but...

3327
02:24:00,840 --> 02:24:02,540
I shed so many tears.

3328
02:24:03,370 --> 02:24:05,340
I cried my eyes out.

3329
02:24:19,920 --> 02:24:22,590
I caught a cold while doing the missions
of Bloody Game.

3330
02:24:22,830 --> 02:24:24,760
I thought I had to take some pills.

3331
02:24:24,760 --> 02:24:27,960
I thought that I had to eat something
in 50 minutes.

3332
02:24:28,300 --> 02:24:30,930
I found the rice cup
the older guys brought.

3333
02:24:31,270 --> 02:24:33,700
I was going to eat the rice cup, but...

3334
02:24:34,000 --> 02:24:35,410
How is this made?

3335
02:24:35,610 --> 02:24:37,510
The older guys used to make this for me.

3336
02:24:53,660 --> 02:24:55,090
After getting reminded of that,

3337
02:24:55,090 --> 02:24:59,630
I cried my eyes out
while reading the directions.

3338
02:25:12,080 --> 02:25:13,810
I had to eat before the voting time ended.

3339
02:25:13,810 --> 02:25:16,080
I ate while crying.

3340
02:25:21,550 --> 02:25:24,890
It was a Top Three moment...

3341
02:25:25,420 --> 02:25:26,860
of me crying in my life.

3342
02:25:27,960 --> 02:25:29,260
I cried even harder...

3343
02:25:29,560 --> 02:25:31,930
than when I broke up with my girlfriend.

3344
02:25:41,140 --> 02:25:42,910
The vote has ended.

3345
02:25:43,240 --> 02:25:45,710
Please gather in the main hall.

3346
02:25:48,510 --> 02:25:50,710
Gosh, it felt like yesterday
when it was loud in here.

3347
02:25:51,210 --> 02:25:53,580
- The group has become this small already?
- There are not many of us left.

3348
02:25:56,020 --> 02:25:58,390
The vote result will now be announced.

3349
02:25:59,020 --> 02:26:01,120
The player to enter the Deathmatch...

3350
02:26:11,970 --> 02:26:13,370
(Park Ji Min)

3351
02:26:13,370 --> 02:26:16,310
is Park Ji Min.

3352
02:26:16,770 --> 02:26:18,540
This is a better result. I'll be back.

3353
02:26:23,010 --> 02:26:24,710
I'm voting for the one
who will be in the Deathmatch, right?

3354
02:26:25,050 --> 02:26:26,220
That's right.

3355
02:26:28,650 --> 02:26:31,250
(Heo Seong Beom votes for Park Ji Min.)

3356
02:26:31,250 --> 02:26:32,760
Please return with a win.

3357
02:26:32,760 --> 02:26:35,020
This was the reason I went with.

3358
02:26:35,390 --> 02:26:37,330
We played the Killer Game yesterday.

3359
02:26:37,430 --> 02:26:41,200
The reason I was able to narrow down
Ji Min and Tae Gyun the fastest...

3360
02:26:41,200 --> 02:26:43,030
was because of Ji Min's mistake.

3361
02:26:43,270 --> 02:26:47,000
But later on,
Ji Min didn't even enter the Deathmatch.

3362
02:26:47,270 --> 02:26:49,440
Xitsuh ended up going home as a result.

3363
02:26:49,770 --> 02:26:52,140
Instead of sending Keun Woo for no reason,

3364
02:26:52,140 --> 02:26:55,810
I thought that it would be better
for Ji Min to go and return after a win...

3365
02:26:56,080 --> 02:26:59,820
to strengthen our team's next play.

3366
02:27:04,250 --> 02:27:05,490
(Park Ji Min, Jeong Keun Woo)

3367
02:27:05,490 --> 02:27:07,190
I will return with a win.

3368
02:27:08,290 --> 02:27:10,190
(Park Ji Min votes for Park Ji Min.)

3369
02:27:10,530 --> 02:27:13,200
I picked up the sword.

3370
02:27:13,400 --> 02:27:17,170
I picked up the sword with my own hand.

3371
02:27:17,670 --> 02:27:19,870
(Jeong Keun Woo: Choi Hye Seon,
Hyun Sung Joo, Jeong Keun Woo)

3372
02:27:19,870 --> 02:27:22,210
(Park Ji Min: Kang Ji Hoo, Hong Jin Ho,
YunB, Heo Seong Beom, Park Ji Min)

3373
02:27:22,310 --> 02:27:24,740
Park Ji Min,
please leave this area right now...

3374
02:27:24,740 --> 02:27:26,980
- and prepare for the Deathmatch.
- I'll place first.

3375
02:27:26,980 --> 02:27:28,640
- Beat all of them!
- You must place first!

3376
02:27:28,640 --> 02:27:30,210
- Thank you!
- You must beat all of them!

3377
02:27:30,210 --> 02:27:31,210
Come back with a win.

3378
02:27:31,210 --> 02:27:32,980
You're saying
I'm better than Jeong Keun Woo.

3379
02:27:32,980 --> 02:27:34,120
- Right.
- Come back with a win!

3380
02:27:34,850 --> 02:27:35,850
Come back with a win.

3381
02:27:40,020 --> 02:27:44,060
Deathmatch players,
please gather in the main hall.

3382
02:27:46,000 --> 02:27:47,900
I hope it's something like guessing
the names of soccer team emblems.

3383
02:27:48,530 --> 02:27:50,000
Guessing the engine displacement of cars.

3384
02:27:50,530 --> 02:27:51,670
Hello.

3385
02:27:51,670 --> 02:27:52,740
Hello.

3386
02:27:52,740 --> 02:27:54,340
(Park Ji Min, the one these two wished
to see, has come.)

3387
02:27:55,240 --> 02:27:57,410
We'll be going against each other again.

3388
02:27:57,410 --> 02:27:58,410
Good game.

3389
02:27:58,410 --> 02:28:00,140
Good game, have fun.

3390
02:28:01,140 --> 02:28:02,280
We were waiting for her.

3391
02:28:02,810 --> 02:28:06,980
I thought that Ji Min was the one
who came up with this structure.

3392
02:28:07,220 --> 02:28:09,920
I really wanted to crush her.

3393
02:28:10,120 --> 02:28:12,360
Ji Min joins the Deathmatch.

3394
02:28:12,720 --> 02:28:15,490
No matter what game,
I was determined to beat her.

3395
02:28:15,990 --> 02:28:18,360
Even if it was about mathematics
which I'm terrible at,

3396
02:28:18,360 --> 02:28:19,530
I was determined to do my best
to beat her.

3397
02:28:19,800 --> 02:28:21,730
I was picked for being a key figure?

3398
02:28:22,330 --> 02:28:24,870
They just came up with that reason...

3399
02:28:25,370 --> 02:28:27,540
to be able to send me away.

3400
02:28:27,540 --> 02:28:29,740
It was such an unimpressive reason.

3401
02:28:30,010 --> 02:28:32,140
I'm no key figure.

3402
02:28:32,140 --> 02:28:36,450
It's because you are already
a public enemy.

3403
02:28:36,450 --> 02:28:38,610
You will become a public enemy
even the next day.

3404
02:28:38,610 --> 02:28:42,050
Before others get blood on their hands,

3405
02:28:42,050 --> 02:28:44,050
I'll slit your throat first.

3406
02:28:45,150 --> 02:28:46,160
Kwak Beom.

3407
02:28:47,120 --> 02:28:48,120
Shin Seung Yong.

3408
02:28:48,790 --> 02:28:49,790
Park Ji Min.

3409
02:28:50,960 --> 02:28:53,760
These three players
have entered the Deathmatch.

3410
02:28:54,460 --> 02:28:57,200
Only one winner will survive...

3411
02:28:57,200 --> 02:29:00,440
and the other players will get eliminated.

3412
02:29:01,140 --> 02:29:05,210
Today's Deathmatch will be revealed.

3413
02:29:06,480 --> 02:29:07,980
Today's Deathmatch...

3414
02:29:09,750 --> 02:29:12,210
is Mix and Match.

3415
02:29:13,580 --> 02:29:14,920
Mix and Match...

3416
02:29:14,920 --> 02:29:17,050
is a game in which you must find
the right word...

3417
02:29:17,050 --> 02:29:18,890
after putting together the locations
of the black spaces...

3418
02:29:18,890 --> 02:29:20,760
of the grids
that get revealed successively.

3419
02:29:21,490 --> 02:29:23,830
A total of 12 rounds will be played.

3420
02:29:23,860 --> 02:29:25,190
In each round,

3421
02:29:25,190 --> 02:29:28,000
grids with the empty spaces
and black spaces...

3422
02:29:28,060 --> 02:29:31,730
will be revealed in order
after three seconds.

3423
02:29:32,640 --> 02:29:36,110
Players must align the grids
to form the word...

3424
02:29:36,110 --> 02:29:38,310
and find the answer.

3425
02:29:39,240 --> 02:29:43,250
The words are all from
the Standard Korean Language Dictionary.

3426
02:29:43,780 --> 02:29:45,610
When a player calls out to say the answer,

3427
02:29:45,610 --> 02:29:47,680
the answer must be called out
within five seconds.

3428
02:29:48,050 --> 02:29:49,420
When it's the right answer,

3429
02:29:49,420 --> 02:29:51,450
two-character words are worth two points.

3430
02:29:51,450 --> 02:29:53,120
Three-character words are
worth three points.

3431
02:29:53,120 --> 02:29:55,860
Four-character words are
worth four points.

3432
02:29:56,590 --> 02:29:59,200
When it's an incorrect answer,
one point will get deducted...

3433
02:29:59,260 --> 02:30:02,900
and the player must wait 30 seconds
to call out the answer again.

3434
02:30:03,530 --> 02:30:04,800
After 12 rounds,

3435
02:30:04,800 --> 02:30:08,500
the player with the highest score
will survive.

3436
02:30:09,110 --> 02:30:10,670
When the scores are the same,

3437
02:30:10,670 --> 02:30:13,680
the player who has answered
more questions will survive.

3438
02:30:14,040 --> 02:30:17,610
Mix and Match will begin shortly.

3439
02:30:22,450 --> 02:30:24,220
I'm not that quick. This is bad.

3440
02:30:24,220 --> 02:30:27,760
It's the same name as the game played
in Season Three's final.

3441
02:30:27,760 --> 02:30:31,030
When I thought about the games played
in Season Three,

3442
02:30:31,030 --> 02:30:32,860
I didn't feel confident.

3443
02:30:32,860 --> 02:30:35,030
But I might find a way out...

3444
02:30:35,030 --> 02:30:36,670
if I stay focused.

3445
02:30:36,670 --> 02:30:39,070
This can be a game...

3446
02:30:39,070 --> 02:30:40,770
that I can be good at.

3447
02:30:40,770 --> 02:30:41,940
- Right.
- Right.

3448
02:30:41,940 --> 02:30:43,110
That's what scares me.

3449
02:30:43,210 --> 02:30:44,240
This game?

3450
02:30:44,340 --> 02:30:46,280
It's a game of addition.
Adding up the pictures.

3451
02:30:46,480 --> 02:30:48,680
I started drawing at a young age...

3452
02:30:49,280 --> 02:30:50,910
and I entered an art school.

3453
02:30:50,910 --> 02:30:53,980
The first thing I mentioned about myself
was my spatial ability.

3454
02:30:53,980 --> 02:30:55,580
I have a talent in that area...

3455
02:30:55,580 --> 02:30:58,020
and I believe I have an advantage.

3456
02:30:58,090 --> 02:31:00,860
I hope they're simple words instead.

3457
02:31:02,560 --> 02:31:04,190
I felt really confident.

3458
02:31:04,460 --> 02:31:08,330
"The words are all from
the Standard Korean Language Dictionary."

3459
02:31:08,330 --> 02:31:10,400
That line struck me.

3460
02:31:10,700 --> 02:31:13,100
"I'm an announcer."

3461
02:31:14,040 --> 02:31:17,610
"A game like this had to come out
for the Deathmatch."

3462
02:31:17,610 --> 02:31:20,140
"Finding the word?"

3463
02:31:20,140 --> 02:31:21,610
It seemed like I had a good chance
for this game.

3464
02:31:21,740 --> 02:31:24,410
We will begin Round One.

3465
02:31:24,750 --> 02:31:26,950
The two-character word will be revealed.

3466
02:31:46,040 --> 02:31:51,070
(Round 1, 2-character word)

3467
02:31:51,070 --> 02:31:53,780
It seemed like Braille.

3468
02:32:00,350 --> 02:32:02,490
"Should I squint..."

3469
02:32:02,490 --> 02:32:04,220
"and leave afterimages?"

3470
02:32:04,290 --> 02:32:07,190
As the interval was a lot longer
than I thought,

3471
02:32:07,260 --> 02:32:09,530
I couldn't see any afterimages.

3472
02:32:09,630 --> 02:32:10,960
I had to start over each time.

3473
02:32:19,540 --> 02:32:20,670
Here's my answer!

3474
02:32:21,740 --> 02:32:23,010
Shin Seung Yong.

3475
02:32:25,370 --> 02:32:26,610
It's "dalgyal."

3476
02:32:31,750 --> 02:32:33,350
- That is correct.
- You are correct.

3477
02:32:33,520 --> 02:32:35,350
You get two points.

3478
02:32:36,420 --> 02:32:38,250
Here's the answer.

3479
02:32:39,590 --> 02:32:42,120
(Dalgyal)

3480
02:32:42,390 --> 02:32:45,130
"Gyal" was like that?

3481
02:32:46,060 --> 02:32:47,360
I figured out "dal."

3482
02:32:47,460 --> 02:32:49,570
"Gyal" threw me off.

3483
02:32:50,730 --> 02:32:53,670
The letters are written on a grid.

3484
02:32:53,770 --> 02:32:57,140
The way it's written is really important.

3485
02:32:57,210 --> 02:32:59,580
The first thing I did was to...

3486
02:32:59,580 --> 02:33:01,780
figure out the final consonants.

3487
02:33:01,840 --> 02:33:05,150
I figured out if the word
had final consonants or not.

3488
02:33:05,210 --> 02:33:07,050
If the word had final consonants,

3489
02:33:07,050 --> 02:33:09,250
I looked for the vowels.

3490
02:33:09,350 --> 02:33:11,390
Then, I looked for the first consonants.

3491
02:33:11,390 --> 02:33:14,090
This was the order of my deduction.

3492
02:33:14,790 --> 02:33:17,190
I'm quick with linguistics.

3493
02:33:17,360 --> 02:33:19,460
We will begin Round Two.

3494
02:33:19,460 --> 02:33:20,460
(Round 2 begins.)

3495
02:33:21,400 --> 02:33:23,670
The two-character word will be revealed.

3496
02:33:33,640 --> 02:33:39,520
(Round 2, 2-character word)

3497
02:33:47,290 --> 02:33:49,190
The length of the first consonants,

3498
02:33:49,190 --> 02:33:50,360
the length of the vowels,

3499
02:33:50,360 --> 02:33:52,560
and the length of the final consonants.
I couldn't...

3500
02:33:53,030 --> 02:33:54,500
figure them out at all.

3501
02:33:54,500 --> 02:33:57,330
I felt totally lost.

3502
02:34:03,540 --> 02:34:05,110
Whether it was mieum, ieung,

3503
02:34:05,110 --> 02:34:07,480
kiyuk, or nieun,

3504
02:34:07,480 --> 02:34:09,140
I could slowly tell what they were.

3505
02:34:14,580 --> 02:34:15,720
Here's my answer!

3506
02:34:16,090 --> 02:34:17,220
Kwak Beom.

3507
02:34:17,220 --> 02:34:18,450
(Kwak Beom makes his attempt
to answer the question.)

3508
02:34:19,120 --> 02:34:20,160
"Ilgeup."

3509
02:34:21,060 --> 02:34:22,660
- That is incorrect.
- Gosh.

3510
02:34:22,660 --> 02:34:24,390
You get one point deducted.

3511
02:34:25,130 --> 02:34:27,600
You can call out for the answer
